WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.834 --> 00:00:02.802
Nikhil: From exclusive
items to portion sizes,

00:00:02.802 --> 00:00:04.304
we wanted to find out all the differences

00:00:04.304 --> 00:00:06.973
between KFC in India and the US.

00:00:06.973 --> 00:00:09.776
This is "Food Wars."

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:16.182
Here in India, we have two
types of chicken sandwiches,

00:00:16.182 --> 00:00:18.385
a Krisper and a Zinger.

00:00:18.385 --> 00:00:20.854
In the US, we have two
chicken-sandwich options,

00:00:20.854 --> 00:00:22.622
the Chicken Little, 'cause it's little,

00:00:22.622 --> 00:00:25.492
and, of course, the Kentucky Fried Chicken

00:00:25.492 --> 00:00:28.094
chicken sandwich. The classic.

00:00:28.094 --> 00:00:29.195
Now let's weigh them to see

00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:32.866
how much they weigh, obviously.

00:00:32.866 --> 00:00:36.169
Ugh! This thing has not been cleaned

00:00:36.169 --> 00:00:37.470
in a very long time.

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:40.106
Nikhil: All right, first
up, the chicken Krisper.

00:00:40.106 --> 00:00:42.409
Joe: Our Chicken Little
in the US weighs ...

00:00:44.411 --> 00:00:45.912
Next up, the chicken Zinger.

00:00:47.914 --> 00:00:52.252
Joe: 240 grams for the
classic chicken sandwich.

00:00:52.252 --> 00:00:53.853
This thing is a work of art.

00:00:53.853 --> 00:00:55.922
All right, on to chicken popcorn.

00:00:55.922 --> 00:00:58.091
Here in India, we have it in three sizes,

00:00:58.091 --> 00:01:01.461
regular, medium, and large.

00:01:01.461 --> 00:01:03.063
We're going to weigh our large popcorn

00:01:03.063 --> 00:01:05.298
to see how much we get.

00:01:05.298 --> 00:01:08.835
I actually really love chicken popcorn.

00:01:11.037 --> 00:01:13.440
I have an idea. We should
weigh one popcorn chicken

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:15.508
and add that back to the total.

00:01:15.508 --> 00:01:17.077
My bad, my bad.

00:01:17.077 --> 00:01:19.779
They should serve this in movie theaters.

00:01:19.779 --> 00:01:22.082
I don't want regular popcorn anymore.

00:01:22.082 --> 00:01:23.016
Mm!

00:01:23.016 --> 00:01:25.985
I love that they sprinkle
in a bunch of sesame seeds,

00:01:25.985 --> 00:01:28.121
and it adds a nice crunch to it.

00:01:28.121 --> 00:01:30.390
What? Sesame seeds? We don't have that.

00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:32.325
All right. You guys are lucky.
That sounds really nice.

00:01:32.325 --> 00:01:34.127
We only have one size
according to the website

00:01:34.127 --> 00:01:36.262
and the KFC I went to, and that is this.

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:46.639
How accurate do these
measurements need to be, really?

00:01:46.639 --> 00:01:48.575
Oh, it's so good!

00:01:49.676 --> 00:01:50.877
Unfortunately, here in India,

00:01:50.877 --> 00:01:52.378
we do not have mashed potatoes,

00:01:52.378 --> 00:01:54.214
but that would be pretty awesome.

00:01:54.214 --> 00:01:57.016
We do have fries. We're big fans of them.

00:01:57.016 --> 00:02:01.287
And they come in two
sizes, medium and large.

00:02:01.287 --> 00:02:04.591
And in the US, we also have
two sizes of fries at KFC,

00:02:04.591 --> 00:02:06.993
the individual, for an individual,

00:02:06.993 --> 00:02:09.262
and the large, also for an individual.

00:02:09.262 --> 00:02:10.396
Nikhil: Let us now measure the large

00:02:10.396 --> 00:02:12.232
to see how much you get.

00:02:13.299 --> 00:02:15.768
140 grams.

00:02:18.104 --> 00:02:21.207
[laughing]

00:02:21.207 --> 00:02:22.509
That's never not funny.

00:02:22.509 --> 00:02:24.110
That's the third time that's happened,

00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:25.245
and it's always funny.

00:02:25.245 --> 00:02:26.946
Look at that block of fries.

00:02:26.946 --> 00:02:31.918
Our largest fry is more than
double their largest fry.

00:02:31.918 --> 00:02:33.186
Here's our individual.

00:02:36.923 --> 00:02:38.358
150!

00:02:39.225 --> 00:02:42.262
Our smallest is bigger than their largest.

00:02:42.262 --> 00:02:45.932
In KFC India, we can get our
chicken in six portion sizes.

00:02:45.932 --> 00:02:49.802
No. 1, the single piece.

00:02:49.802 --> 00:02:51.504
Two-piece.

00:02:51.504 --> 00:02:52.472
They like to give you

00:02:52.472 --> 00:02:56.276
one breast piece and one leg piece. Kind.

00:02:56.276 --> 00:02:59.245
Four-piece. Leg piece to top it all off.

00:02:59.245 --> 00:03:01.447
The leg piece on top, as they say.

00:03:01.447 --> 00:03:03.950
Like cherry on top. No? OK.

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:05.185
Now we move on to buckets.

00:03:05.185 --> 00:03:06.486
We have four sizes.

00:03:06.486 --> 00:03:08.821
The first one is a five-piece bucket

00:03:08.821 --> 00:03:10.924
that comes with only leg pieces

00:03:10.924 --> 00:03:13.793
and also does not come in
a bucket for some reason.

00:03:13.793 --> 00:03:16.262
Why, KFC? I want a bucket.

00:03:16.262 --> 00:03:18.131
Next up, we have a six-piece bucket,

00:03:18.131 --> 00:03:19.265
an eight-piece bucket,

00:03:19.265 --> 00:03:20.900
and the largest one of them all,

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:23.403
a 10-piece leg bucket.

00:03:23.403 --> 00:03:25.538
Whew, that's a lot of chicken.

00:03:25.538 --> 00:03:29.409
In the US, our KFC chicken
comes in seven portion sizes.

00:03:29.409 --> 00:03:31.311
One, which you can get à la carte;

00:03:31.311 --> 00:03:33.279
two-piece, with a combo;

00:03:33.279 --> 00:03:35.081
three-piece, with a combo;

00:03:35.081 --> 00:03:37.217
four-piece, with a combo.

00:03:37.217 --> 00:03:38.851
Then [snaps] buckets.

00:03:38.851 --> 00:03:40.019
Did that work? OK.

00:03:40.019 --> 00:03:42.589
We have an eight-piece.

00:03:42.589 --> 00:03:45.225
Yeah, eight pieces.

00:03:46.993 --> 00:03:48.695
The 12-piece.

00:03:51.331 --> 00:03:54.901
And our largest bucket, the 16-piece.

00:03:54.901 --> 00:03:56.002
Ready, Yuelei?

00:03:57.203 --> 00:03:58.638
What?

00:04:00.907 --> 00:04:02.508
You get the idea.

00:04:02.508 --> 00:04:03.943
Next up, you're going to need a drink

00:04:03.943 --> 00:04:05.378
to wash all that chicken down.

00:04:05.378 --> 00:04:08.281
Here in India, we don't serve
cups, we just serve cans.

00:04:08.281 --> 00:04:12.952
We have Pepsi; 7Up; Mirinda,
which is an orange soda;

00:04:12.952 --> 00:04:15.455
Red Bull; and a Pepsi PET bottle.

00:04:15.455 --> 00:04:17.824
However, these will vary
from store to store.

00:04:17.824 --> 00:04:20.226
In some places, they
might not serve plastic,

00:04:20.226 --> 00:04:22.195
and in some places, you
might not get these drinks,

00:04:22.195 --> 00:04:23.429
you might get something else.

00:04:23.429 --> 00:04:27.567
They also serve something
called a virgin mojito Krusher,

00:04:27.567 --> 00:04:29.702
which they don't deliver, unfortunately,

00:04:29.702 --> 00:04:31.237
but here's an image of it.

00:04:32.572 --> 00:04:33.740
Refreshing.

00:04:33.740 --> 00:04:36.242
American drinks come in
these following sizes:

00:04:36.242 --> 00:04:38.244
the regular, which is 20 ounces,

00:04:38.244 --> 00:04:40.513
and the large, which is 30 ounces.

00:04:40.513 --> 00:04:41.948
And we don't stop there.

00:04:41.948 --> 00:04:43.916
If you want, you can also get

00:04:43.916 --> 00:04:46.519
half-a-gallon bag

00:04:46.519 --> 00:04:48.955
of your favorite drink of choice.

00:04:48.955 --> 00:04:49.889
Look at this thing!

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:55.628
Mm.

00:04:57.830 --> 00:04:59.165
It's convenient.

00:05:00.833 --> 00:05:01.668
[burps]

00:05:04.904 --> 00:05:07.473
Here is everything you'll
find on the menu at KFC India

00:05:07.473 --> 00:05:09.142
that you won't get in the US.

00:05:09.142 --> 00:05:13.012
And here's everything you
can find at a KFC in the US

00:05:13.012 --> 00:05:14.580
you won't find in India.

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:17.850
Take a look, India. Take a good look.

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:19.085
OK, let's start with chicken.

00:05:19.085 --> 00:05:21.287
In India, apart from the crispy chicken,

00:05:21.287 --> 00:05:24.891
we also get smoky red chicken.

00:05:24.891 --> 00:05:26.492
Ooh.

00:05:26.492 --> 00:05:27.660
Wow.

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:30.930
I believe this is KFC's
answer to tandoori chicken.

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:32.298
If you guys don't know what a tandoor is,

00:05:32.298 --> 00:05:34.233
it's basically a cylindrical oven

00:05:34.233 --> 00:05:37.537
that they light up using
wood fire or charcoal,

00:05:37.537 --> 00:05:40.740
and it adds a really
smoky flavor to the meats

00:05:40.740 --> 00:05:42.542
or breads that you cook inside of it.

00:05:42.542 --> 00:05:46.012
I doubt KFCs across the
country have an actual tandoor,

00:05:46.012 --> 00:05:48.781
but the flavoring
definitely smells like that.

00:05:48.781 --> 00:05:50.850
The marinade looks like that.

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:57.423
Oh, my God, that's actually pretty good.

00:05:57.423 --> 00:05:59.459
You know what, KFC?

00:05:59.459 --> 00:06:00.760
Pretty good job.

00:06:00.760 --> 00:06:02.395
You have to remember, KFC is competing

00:06:02.395 --> 00:06:06.232
with a lot of Mughlai restaurants
across every Indian city,

00:06:06.232 --> 00:06:08.101
and while this doesn't
have as much of that

00:06:08.101 --> 00:06:11.604
smoky char that a lot
of tandoori kebabs have,

00:06:11.604 --> 00:06:12.772
it has a lot of flavor,

00:06:12.772 --> 00:06:15.208
and the chicken is quite juicy.

00:06:15.208 --> 00:06:16.376
Good job.

00:06:16.376 --> 00:06:17.577
It's super spicy though,

00:06:17.577 --> 00:06:21.147
so if you're somebody
who can't handle spice,

00:06:21.147 --> 00:06:22.582
go a little easy on this one.

00:06:22.582 --> 00:06:25.351
When an Indian says
something's spicy, it's spicy.

00:06:25.351 --> 00:06:27.186
I believe you, man. I believe you.

00:06:27.186 --> 00:06:28.588
That looks incredible.

00:06:28.588 --> 00:06:29.989
We, unfortunately,

00:06:29.989 --> 00:06:32.592
don't really have anything
too spicy on the menu

00:06:32.592 --> 00:06:35.027
for the chicken-on-the-bone options.

00:06:35.027 --> 00:06:36.462
Really the only thing that we have here

00:06:36.462 --> 00:06:37.630
that apparently you guys don't have

00:06:37.630 --> 00:06:39.665
is something that is what I associate

00:06:39.665 --> 00:06:42.468
Kentucky Fried Chicken
with, is extra-crispy.

00:06:42.468 --> 00:06:44.637
I don't know exactly what
makes it extra-crispy,

00:06:44.637 --> 00:06:46.839
but it is, as you can imagine,

00:06:46.839 --> 00:06:49.242
crispier than the regular chicken.

00:06:50.243 --> 00:06:52.512
[crunching]

00:06:52.512 --> 00:06:54.614
Extra-crispy to me is far superior

00:06:54.614 --> 00:06:56.315
to the regular way they cook chicken.

00:06:56.315 --> 00:06:57.750
I think it should be the other way around.

00:06:57.750 --> 00:06:58.618
This should be the regular,

00:06:58.618 --> 00:07:01.053
and the other one should
be, like, half-crispy.

00:07:01.053 --> 00:07:03.756
You know what I mean? This is way better.

00:07:03.756 --> 00:07:05.625
All right, let's move on
to chicken sandwiches.

00:07:05.625 --> 00:07:07.994
Here in India, we don't have
an American chicken sandwich,

00:07:07.994 --> 00:07:09.829
but we have a Zinger

00:07:09.829 --> 00:07:13.332
and a smaller sandwich
called a Krisper. Cute.

00:07:13.332 --> 00:07:15.034
The Krisper looks like it wants to grow up

00:07:15.034 --> 00:07:16.536
and be a Zinger someday.

00:07:16.536 --> 00:07:17.703
They also come in two variants,

00:07:17.703 --> 00:07:21.340
a spicy Krisper and a tandoori Zinger.

00:07:21.340 --> 00:07:22.542
Let's taste all of them.

00:07:24.877 --> 00:07:26.412
Oh, that's pretty yum.

00:07:26.412 --> 00:07:28.247
They've used a different
kind of mayonnaise here.

00:07:28.247 --> 00:07:30.283
It has a bit of sweetness to it

00:07:30.283 --> 00:07:32.518
and a spicy kick at the end.

00:07:32.518 --> 00:07:35.621
And now for the legendary Zinger.

00:07:35.621 --> 00:07:37.023
Back in the day, there were only two

00:07:37.023 --> 00:07:38.825
fast-food chains here in India,

00:07:38.825 --> 00:07:40.426
it was McDonald's and KFC.

00:07:40.426 --> 00:07:43.563
And while McDonald's had more
affordable burger options,

00:07:43.563 --> 00:07:46.966
the KFC Zinger was so delicious,

00:07:46.966 --> 00:07:49.569
it was always a treat to eat.

00:07:51.504 --> 00:07:54.006
Mm. And it still is.

00:07:54.006 --> 00:07:56.209
I love that they use a whole

00:07:56.209 --> 00:07:58.945
boneless piece of proper chicken in there.

00:07:58.945 --> 00:08:00.146
Delicious mayo.

00:08:00.146 --> 00:08:01.514
It's so delicious.

00:08:01.514 --> 00:08:03.516
OK, now let's try the spicy variants.

00:08:03.516 --> 00:08:05.985
This is the spicy Krisper.

00:08:05.985 --> 00:08:07.620
Look at this sauce!

00:08:07.620 --> 00:08:10.523
It's almost blood-red. I'm excited.

00:08:12.859 --> 00:08:14.694
Oh, my God.

00:08:14.694 --> 00:08:17.763
This sauce almost has
a Szechuan taste to it.

00:08:17.763 --> 00:08:20.933
Next up, the Zinger, but tandoori.

00:08:23.903 --> 00:08:26.539
Mm. I love the fullness of the chicken

00:08:26.539 --> 00:08:28.374
that comes in these burgers

00:08:28.374 --> 00:08:31.978
versus, like, a minced chicken
patty in other restaurants.

00:08:31.978 --> 00:08:33.312
There's so much bite to it.

00:08:33.312 --> 00:08:34.881
It's so juicy, tender.

00:08:34.881 --> 00:08:36.115
That all sounds amazing.

00:08:36.115 --> 00:08:37.750
Stop, you're going too fast!

00:08:37.750 --> 00:08:40.152
I have to say, those
sandwiches look delicious,

00:08:40.152 --> 00:08:42.288
and I am jealous.

00:08:42.288 --> 00:08:44.257
One sandwich you can get here in the US,

00:08:44.257 --> 00:08:45.291
can't get in India,

00:08:45.291 --> 00:08:47.827
is this little guy, the Chicken Little.

00:08:47.827 --> 00:08:50.897
Looks to be a chicken tender

00:08:50.897 --> 00:08:53.399
in between these tiny little buns.

00:08:53.399 --> 00:08:55.535
Pickles, goodbye.

00:08:57.803 --> 00:08:59.171
Could probably eat, like, five of those.

00:08:59.171 --> 00:09:01.774
Slightly different from
what you have in India,

00:09:01.774 --> 00:09:03.509
so I'm going to use it as an excuse

00:09:03.509 --> 00:09:05.244
to show it off yet again.

00:09:05.244 --> 00:09:07.113
Our crispy chicken sandwich.

00:09:07.113 --> 00:09:10.449
This thing, the original, the bad boy.

00:09:10.449 --> 00:09:11.784
Also with pickles.

00:09:11.784 --> 00:09:13.052
Hang on.

00:09:13.052 --> 00:09:14.887
Get off of my sandwich.

00:09:14.887 --> 00:09:18.558
But it has this really creamy
mayo sauce on it, the bun.

00:09:18.558 --> 00:09:19.725
I love this.

00:09:21.427 --> 00:09:22.261
Yeah.

00:09:23.596 --> 00:09:28.234
Other chicken stuff we
got here you ain't got.

00:09:28.234 --> 00:09:29.168
I'm already getting loopy.

00:09:29.168 --> 00:09:31.771
Start over here, Nashville
hot tender chicken.

00:09:31.771 --> 00:09:33.272
Here, this, I think, is the spiciest thing

00:09:33.272 --> 00:09:34.440
you're getting at the KFC menu.

00:09:34.440 --> 00:09:35.808
And I'm gonna be straight
up, I've had these before,

00:09:35.808 --> 00:09:36.642
these are pretty good.

00:09:36.642 --> 00:09:38.377
And they're really crispy, Yuelei.

00:09:38.377 --> 00:09:40.479
Want to hear that crisp again?

00:09:40.479 --> 00:09:42.815
[crunching]

00:09:44.016 --> 00:09:45.818
Not sure if it's made
it over to India yet.

00:09:45.818 --> 00:09:48.588
It is called a chicken pot pie.

00:09:48.588 --> 00:09:51.223
It's a pie, but instead
of there being, you know,

00:09:51.223 --> 00:09:53.626
fruit or any of the sweet stuff you like,

00:09:53.626 --> 00:09:56.095
they fill a pie with chicken,

00:09:56.095 --> 00:09:57.463
and what do you think else is in here?

00:09:57.463 --> 00:09:59.265
Corn, gravy, peas maybe.

00:09:59.265 --> 00:10:00.600
I have no idea. I'm not
going to rip this thing open.

00:10:00.600 --> 00:10:02.702
This thing, it's got some weight to it.

00:10:02.702 --> 00:10:04.704
This is a meal right
here. This is not a side.

00:10:04.704 --> 00:10:07.540
I don't know where it is
in the menu, but whew.

00:10:07.540 --> 00:10:10.610
This right here, the KFC Famous Bowl.

00:10:10.610 --> 00:10:13.346
And it is famous, let me tell you.

00:10:13.346 --> 00:10:15.147
Nikhil, if you're wondering what this is,

00:10:15.147 --> 00:10:17.650
someone at KFC was like,

00:10:17.650 --> 00:10:19.952
"How can we put everything into one bowl?"

00:10:19.952 --> 00:10:21.354
And this thing was born.

00:10:21.354 --> 00:10:24.490
It is mashed potatoes, corn,

00:10:24.490 --> 00:10:26.559
the popcorn chicken,

00:10:26.559 --> 00:10:29.729
cheese, and gravy, all
in a convenient bowl

00:10:29.729 --> 00:10:31.864
for you to eat while you are driving.

00:10:34.800 --> 00:10:36.802
It generally does nothing for the flavor.

00:10:36.802 --> 00:10:39.472
It's exactly what I would
think this would taste like.

00:10:39.472 --> 00:10:41.907
It's just a bunch of
this stuff in one bowl.

00:10:41.907 --> 00:10:44.677
Yes, in India, you can
get wings at the KFC,

00:10:44.677 --> 00:10:47.446
but at our KFC in the US, you
can get your wings sauced.

00:10:47.446 --> 00:10:49.615
And we have three different sauces,

00:10:49.615 --> 00:10:52.985
honey barbecue, Buffalo, Nashville hot.

00:10:55.454 --> 00:10:57.189
Honey barbecue, thumbs down.

00:10:57.189 --> 00:10:58.391
This Buffalo's a lot more orange

00:10:58.391 --> 00:10:59.992
than I recall Buffalo being.

00:10:59.992 --> 00:11:01.260
I cannot quite place my finger

00:11:01.260 --> 00:11:03.262
on why suddenly my stomach is killing me.

00:11:06.432 --> 00:11:08.467
Do you see inside there?

00:11:08.467 --> 00:11:09.735
OK.

00:11:09.735 --> 00:11:11.604
[Yuelei laughs]

00:11:11.604 --> 00:11:12.805
On to the next wing.

00:11:14.707 --> 00:11:17.109
Bring on that food poisoning, baby.

00:11:17.109 --> 00:11:19.945
Um, yeah, all these are bad.

00:11:19.945 --> 00:11:22.048
All right, moving away from chicken,

00:11:22.048 --> 00:11:25.117
India's KFC actually has
vegetarian alternatives

00:11:25.117 --> 00:11:26.619
for all our burgers.

00:11:26.619 --> 00:11:29.255
There is a vegetarian Krisper,

00:11:29.255 --> 00:11:33.325
a vegetarian spicy Krisper,
and a vegetarian Zinger.

00:11:33.325 --> 00:11:35.761
Now, while India has a majority population

00:11:35.761 --> 00:11:38.097
of nonvegetarians, around 70%,

00:11:38.097 --> 00:11:40.032
there is a huge vegetarian population,

00:11:40.032 --> 00:11:41.701
which is why a lot of
fast-food restaurants

00:11:41.701 --> 00:11:44.203
have to make sure they have
a lot of vegetarian options

00:11:44.203 --> 00:11:46.439
on their menu to make it more approachable

00:11:46.439 --> 00:11:48.908
and acceptable for all people over here.

00:11:48.908 --> 00:11:51.777
There's also levels to
vegetarianism over here.

00:11:51.777 --> 00:11:54.480
There are I-will-eat-egg-but-not-chicken
vegetarians.

00:11:54.480 --> 00:11:57.383
There are I-will-eat-fish-but-not-lamb
vegetarians.

00:11:57.383 --> 00:11:59.085
There are I-will-eat-the-curry-

00:11:59.085 --> 00:12:00.853
but-not-the-pieces vegetarians.

00:12:00.853 --> 00:12:03.956
There are I-am-vegetarian-only-on-Tuesdays
vegetarians.

00:12:03.956 --> 00:12:05.558
There are I-have-made-a-promise-to-God-

00:12:05.558 --> 00:12:07.460
for-this-one-month vegetarians.

00:12:07.460 --> 00:12:08.961
There are I-am-vegetarian-

00:12:08.961 --> 00:12:11.731
so-you-will-all-be-vegetarian vegetarians.

00:12:11.731 --> 00:12:14.900
They're the weird ones, and
we try not to talk about them.

00:12:14.900 --> 00:12:19.572
Which is why KFC in India
brands itself as just KFC.

00:12:19.572 --> 00:12:22.141
There's no Kentucky Fried
Chicken anywhere here

00:12:22.141 --> 00:12:23.642
because, obviously,

00:12:23.642 --> 00:12:25.611
I'm not going to go to a
place that's named that

00:12:25.611 --> 00:12:28.380
if I'm one of these many
types of vegetarians.

00:12:28.380 --> 00:12:31.484
One iconic dish that you'll
find on the KFC India menu

00:12:31.484 --> 00:12:33.352
is biryani.

00:12:33.352 --> 00:12:36.889
And so KFC India has
taken a very bold decision

00:12:36.889 --> 00:12:38.758
to launch their own biryanis.

00:12:38.758 --> 00:12:40.292
If you don't know what biryani is,

00:12:40.292 --> 00:12:43.996
you are living under a
gigantic boulder, my friend.

00:12:43.996 --> 00:12:45.631
Hey, guess I live under a boulder

00:12:45.631 --> 00:12:49.068
because I, unfortunately, am
not familiar with biryani,

00:12:49.068 --> 00:12:50.736
but I would love to know more about it.

00:12:58.577 --> 00:13:00.513
Hello! I am Crystelle Pereira,

00:13:00.513 --> 00:13:01.947
and I am a cook and a baker,

00:13:01.947 --> 00:13:03.482
and you may know me as a finalist

00:13:03.482 --> 00:13:04.950
from "The Great British Bake Off."

00:13:04.950 --> 00:13:07.186
This [bell dings] is biryani.

00:13:07.186 --> 00:13:10.289
Now, biryani is a typical rice
dish you find in South Asia,

00:13:10.289 --> 00:13:12.057
and the way you make it is in layers.

00:13:12.057 --> 00:13:14.226
My dad is a biryani master at home,

00:13:14.226 --> 00:13:16.462
and the way he makes
it is with cooked rice,

00:13:16.462 --> 00:13:18.864
cooked potatoes, some
fried onions, and a curry.

00:13:18.864 --> 00:13:20.466
We like to go for a mutton biryani,

00:13:20.466 --> 00:13:21.700
but you can get chicken or fish,

00:13:21.700 --> 00:13:24.069
and in this case, vegetarian biryani.

00:13:24.069 --> 00:13:25.171
We absolutely love it,

00:13:25.171 --> 00:13:26.939
and we always eat it as a family unit

00:13:26.939 --> 00:13:29.441
with a lovely pot of
cooling raita on the side,

00:13:29.441 --> 00:13:31.010
which is a lovely cooling yogurt dish

00:13:31.010 --> 00:13:33.546
which goes really well
with the spicy biryani.

00:13:33.546 --> 00:13:35.881
And it's basically our
equivalent of a Sunday roast,

00:13:35.881 --> 00:13:38.117
because you have it in a big
pot and you all take scoops.

00:13:38.117 --> 00:13:39.552
And I actually don't think

00:13:39.552 --> 00:13:42.822
I've ever eaten biryani
by myself for one person.

00:13:42.822 --> 00:13:45.624
Now, we have to talk
about this KFC biryani,

00:13:45.624 --> 00:13:48.027
because for me, biryani is a home dish.

00:13:48.027 --> 00:13:49.595
You make it in a home kitchen,

00:13:49.595 --> 00:13:52.398
it's cooked by a family member,
and it's cooked with love.

00:13:52.398 --> 00:13:54.333
My first impression, a KFC biryani,

00:13:54.333 --> 00:13:57.036
those two words just
don't go together for me.

00:13:57.036 --> 00:13:58.170
Just to give you guys context

00:13:58.170 --> 00:14:01.507
of what it's like to be Indian
and eat a biryani at KFC,

00:14:01.507 --> 00:14:05.678
it's like being Italian and
eating a pasta at Domino's.

00:14:05.678 --> 00:14:07.746
Got it, thank you.

00:14:07.746 --> 00:14:08.747
Continue.

00:14:08.747 --> 00:14:10.382
They come in four flavors.

00:14:10.382 --> 00:14:13.352
No. 1, classic chicken, nice and crispy.

00:14:13.352 --> 00:14:15.888
No. 2, popcorn chicken.

00:14:15.888 --> 00:14:20.092
No. 3, the spicy red
chicken that I really enjoy.

00:14:20.092 --> 00:14:21.961
And No. 4, the veg patty,

00:14:21.961 --> 00:14:25.998
which, it's so tempting to
just push that to the side,

00:14:25.998 --> 00:14:29.268
because veg biryani is already just

00:14:29.268 --> 00:14:32.872
a concept that we're
not a fan of over here.

00:14:32.872 --> 00:14:37.209
But just for now, you can stay here.

00:14:37.209 --> 00:14:40.779
OK, I'm going to begin with
the popcorn chicken biryani,

00:14:40.779 --> 00:14:44.516
which is just so
blasphemous to begin with.

00:14:48.053 --> 00:14:49.922
Mm.

00:14:50.789 --> 00:14:52.157
Hm.

00:14:52.992 --> 00:14:54.627
It's not a biryani.

00:14:54.627 --> 00:14:55.561
It's ...

00:14:56.762 --> 00:14:58.664
I'm so upset right now.

00:14:58.664 --> 00:15:01.533
This one, the spicy red chicken,

00:15:01.533 --> 00:15:03.836
has a bit of that tandoori vibe to it.

00:15:03.836 --> 00:15:06.538
They've really tried to
overcompensate with the spices.

00:15:06.538 --> 00:15:08.641
There's a lot of clove flavor

00:15:08.641 --> 00:15:11.210
just to convince you you're
eating a biryani, so,

00:15:11.210 --> 00:15:12.745
go easy on that curry.

00:15:14.980 --> 00:15:17.316
I could eat this, like, if I was hungry.

00:15:17.316 --> 00:15:18.450
Not a biryani, though.

00:15:18.450 --> 00:15:21.887
That biryani looks real
depressing. I am sorry.

00:15:21.887 --> 00:15:24.623
But we do have these
exclusive side dishes,

00:15:24.623 --> 00:15:26.325
which are mashed potatoes,

00:15:26.325 --> 00:15:27.927
I can't believe you guys
don't have mashed potatoes.

00:15:27.927 --> 00:15:30.829
It feels like this is flagship stuff here.

00:15:30.829 --> 00:15:32.097
Macaroni and cheese.

00:15:32.097 --> 00:15:34.667
Biscuits. Again, no biscuits?

00:15:34.667 --> 00:15:36.035
Coleslaw.

00:15:36.035 --> 00:15:40.172
This giant dish of just gravy,

00:15:40.172 --> 00:15:41.941
and, of course, sweet corn.

00:15:41.941 --> 00:15:46.645
New country, new sauces,
y'all know what that means.

00:15:46.645 --> 00:15:48.013
Sauce talk.

00:15:48.013 --> 00:15:50.783
First one, I mean, the KFC sauce.

00:15:50.783 --> 00:15:53.919
Why this isn't at every KFC
internationally, I have no idea.

00:15:53.919 --> 00:15:55.387
Get a load of that sauce right there.

00:15:57.756 --> 00:16:00.693
I think it's, like, ketchup
and mayo, but it's really good.

00:16:00.693 --> 00:16:01.961
Honey barbecue.

00:16:02.828 --> 00:16:04.830
I know what that tastes like.

00:16:04.830 --> 00:16:06.231
Honey mustard.

00:16:07.066 --> 00:16:08.167
That's not your thing?

00:16:09.468 --> 00:16:10.769
Honey.

00:16:10.769 --> 00:16:13.138
And, of course, you got classic ranch.

00:16:16.175 --> 00:16:20.145
Not much of a ranch aficionado,
but theirs is just OK.

00:16:20.145 --> 00:16:22.214
And, oh, I forgot about
their hot sauce, Yuelei.

00:16:25.918 --> 00:16:28.220
India does not have too
many exclusive dips.

00:16:28.220 --> 00:16:30.622
In fact, we just have a
veg eggless mayonnaise

00:16:30.622 --> 00:16:33.058
and a tandoori masala mayonnaise.

00:16:33.058 --> 00:16:34.360
It's time to taste.

00:16:35.761 --> 00:16:37.763
I'm using the same hand,
because here in India,

00:16:37.763 --> 00:16:39.665
we don't eat with our left hand.

00:16:40.699 --> 00:16:41.934
If you're wondering why,

00:16:41.934 --> 00:16:44.737
commenters, you let them know.

00:16:46.005 --> 00:16:48.040
"Why don't Indians

00:16:48.040 --> 00:16:50.109
eat with their left hand?"

00:16:58.884 --> 00:17:02.988
Well, it's just mayonnaise,
so good job on that.

00:17:04.990 --> 00:17:06.091
Mayonnaise again,

00:17:06.091 --> 00:17:10.396
with a little bit of a sweet
but also spicy kick to it.

00:17:10.396 --> 00:17:11.730
I wish we had more options,

00:17:11.730 --> 00:17:14.400
especially considering there are so many

00:17:14.400 --> 00:17:17.102
different delicious chicken options.

00:17:17.102 --> 00:17:20.739
I'd love to be able to dip
my tenders in more sauces.

00:17:20.739 --> 00:17:22.808
That is a weird sentence.

00:17:22.808 --> 00:17:24.209
For those of you with a sweet tooth,

00:17:24.209 --> 00:17:27.312
we have two exclusive dessert options.

00:17:27.312 --> 00:17:29.581
Chocolate chip cookie

00:17:29.581 --> 00:17:33.519
and this chocolate chip cake.

00:17:33.519 --> 00:17:35.154
How good does this look?

00:17:35.154 --> 00:17:37.623
Here in India, we have
two exclusive desserts.

00:17:37.623 --> 00:17:42.428
A choco mud pie and a coffee mousse cake.

00:17:42.428 --> 00:17:44.430
Ooh, boy!

00:17:44.430 --> 00:17:47.132
Just look at this cross
section, my friend.

00:17:47.132 --> 00:17:50.502
Next up, coffee mousse cake.

00:17:52.337 --> 00:17:54.039
Yeah,

00:17:54.039 --> 00:17:57.543
these are pretty average as desserts.

00:17:57.543 --> 00:17:59.545
Drinks, drinks,

00:17:59.545 --> 00:18:01.814
drinks!

00:18:01.814 --> 00:18:04.083
Maybe my favorite part of
the exclusives section.

00:18:04.083 --> 00:18:05.284
Exclusive drinks you can get in the US

00:18:05.284 --> 00:18:07.219
you cannot get in India.

00:18:07.219 --> 00:18:08.253
Mountain Dew.

00:18:08.253 --> 00:18:10.889
I'm back, baby. Mm.

00:18:10.889 --> 00:18:13.358
And if you're a Mountain
Dew fan, such as me,

00:18:13.358 --> 00:18:16.962
you know KFC has got the exclusive

00:18:18.630 --> 00:18:20.532
Mountain Dew Sweet Lightning.

00:18:20.532 --> 00:18:22.935
So, Mountain Dew Sweet lightning
is like peach Mountain Dew,

00:18:22.935 --> 00:18:24.036
and it's really good.

00:18:24.036 --> 00:18:26.171
It's really good. Mm!

00:18:26.171 --> 00:18:28.841
Think this is a lemonade,
the US-style lemonade,

00:18:28.841 --> 00:18:30.809
not that weird UK Sprite lemonade.

00:18:32.010 --> 00:18:32.845
Oh, so good.

00:18:32.845 --> 00:18:35.881
From there, you can also get Sierra Mist.

00:18:35.881 --> 00:18:37.316
[sighs]

00:18:37.316 --> 00:18:39.785
Ugh, ugh!

00:18:39.785 --> 00:18:43.188
And, of course, sweet tea.

00:18:45.090 --> 00:18:46.892
Whoa, that's, like, really sweet.

00:18:46.892 --> 00:18:48.360
Oh, that's really good.

00:18:48.360 --> 00:18:51.663
Exclusive drinks in KFC India.

00:18:51.663 --> 00:18:54.867
We have Mirinda, which is an orange soda,

00:18:54.867 --> 00:18:56.268
and Red Bull.

00:18:56.268 --> 00:18:58.370
Let's talk about Mirinda.

00:18:58.370 --> 00:19:01.373
This is a drink that
really evokes nostalgia.

00:19:01.373 --> 00:19:05.277
'90s kids will know what I'm
talking about when I say,

00:19:07.346 --> 00:19:09.748
"Mirindaaaaa."

00:19:12.551 --> 00:19:15.187
Which country is getting
the better deal on its KFC?

00:19:15.187 --> 00:19:17.789
Let's compare a few
menu items to find out.

00:19:17.789 --> 00:19:20.626
Both countries offer
eight-piece chicken bucket.

00:19:20.626 --> 00:19:25.197
Here in LA, one of these goes for $19.99.

00:19:25.197 --> 00:19:27.633
If you order an eight-piece chicken bucket

00:19:27.633 --> 00:19:29.368
here at KFC India,

00:19:29.368 --> 00:19:33.272
it will cost you 699.05 rupees,

00:19:33.272 --> 00:19:34.406
very specific,

00:19:34.406 --> 00:19:38.310
which is currently 9.15 US dollars.

00:19:38.310 --> 00:19:40.379
That makes the American eight-piece bucket

00:19:40.379 --> 00:19:43.815
118% more expensive than the one in India.

00:19:43.815 --> 00:19:47.853
Does making your meal a combo
help the US price out at all?

00:19:47.853 --> 00:19:50.989
Take this chicken-sandwich
combo, with fries and a drink.

00:19:50.989 --> 00:19:54.960
It will set you back, in America, $9.99.

00:19:54.960 --> 00:19:57.529
The Indian equivalent is a Zinger meal,

00:19:57.529 --> 00:20:00.098
where you can get a chicken
sandwich, some medium fries,

00:20:00.098 --> 00:20:03.602
and a drink for 319.05 rupees,

00:20:03.602 --> 00:20:07.072
or 4.18 US dollars.

00:20:07.072 --> 00:20:08.640
In fact, the price difference is so great,

00:20:08.640 --> 00:20:11.176
you can get something called
the Ultimate Savings Bucket

00:20:11.176 --> 00:20:14.580
for just 599 rupees, or $7.88.

00:20:14.580 --> 00:20:18.016
And this contains four pieces
of hot and crispy chicken,

00:20:18.016 --> 00:20:20.619
six hot wings, four boneless strips,

00:20:20.619 --> 00:20:24.523
three drinks, and three dips. Yeesh.

00:20:24.523 --> 00:20:26.525
In fact, you can throw in a
choco mud pie as a dessert

00:20:26.525 --> 00:20:28.393
and still get all of this for much cheaper

00:20:28.393 --> 00:20:30.062
than the American combo meal.

00:20:30.062 --> 00:20:33.532
But is it really that cheap here in India?

00:20:33.532 --> 00:20:35.300
No, because two-thirds of India

00:20:35.300 --> 00:20:36.535
is still under the poverty line,

00:20:36.535 --> 00:20:39.738
and for them, this meal is
still very aspirational.

00:20:39.738 --> 00:20:41.607
They earn less than $2 a day.

00:20:41.607 --> 00:20:42.608
Sorry to be a downer,

00:20:42.608 --> 00:20:45.210
but this is still a meal
that is only available

00:20:45.210 --> 00:20:47.246
to the really privileged here in India.

00:20:49.982 --> 00:20:52.584
Unfortunately, KFC does
not share a full list

00:20:52.584 --> 00:20:54.419
of ingredients with the public.

00:20:54.419 --> 00:20:55.821
It's actually the same in the US.

00:20:55.821 --> 00:20:59.324
All KFC shares with the
public is a list of allergens.

00:20:59.324 --> 00:21:01.293
So, what do we know about KFC?

00:21:01.293 --> 00:21:04.930
Well, the KFC India website
has a couple of clues.

00:21:04.930 --> 00:21:07.366
We know that all of our
chicken is farmed here

00:21:07.366 --> 00:21:08.367
and not imported,

00:21:08.367 --> 00:21:11.870
and all of it is 100%
whole muscle chicken.

00:21:13.572 --> 00:21:15.841
That means it's made from
whole pieces of chicken

00:21:15.841 --> 00:21:17.843
and not cut-together minced chicken,

00:21:17.843 --> 00:21:19.344
like you find in chicken nuggets.

00:21:19.344 --> 00:21:22.381
In fact, the website says they
have an open-kitchen policy,

00:21:22.381 --> 00:21:25.250
and what that means is
anybody can walk into a KFC

00:21:25.250 --> 00:21:27.452
and apparently ask for a kitchen tour.

00:21:27.452 --> 00:21:30.055
And you can go into the
kitchen, look at everything,

00:21:30.055 --> 00:21:31.957
and ask as many questions as you want.

00:21:31.957 --> 00:21:35.193
I have never heard of
that in my entire life,

00:21:35.193 --> 00:21:36.194
an open-kitchen policy.

00:21:36.194 --> 00:21:37.929
I've worked in several kitchens,

00:21:37.929 --> 00:21:39.364
and I'll tell you straight up,

00:21:39.364 --> 00:21:41.533
if I was in a kitchen working
and some dude walks in

00:21:41.533 --> 00:21:42.868
and is like, "Hey, can I
get a tour of the kitchen?"

00:21:42.868 --> 00:21:45.504
I'd be like, "Yeah, here's
your tour. There's the exit."

00:21:45.504 --> 00:21:47.506
Definitely can't do that
in the United States.

00:21:47.506 --> 00:21:50.342
Don't go into a KFC
chicken and demand a tour.

00:21:50.342 --> 00:21:53.578
The KFC US website also
gives us some hints

00:21:53.578 --> 00:21:55.947
about the ingredients it uses over here.

00:21:55.947 --> 00:21:59.284
For instance, all of our
chicken is raised on US farms

00:21:59.284 --> 00:22:02.187
to the USDA and FDA's standards.

00:22:02.187 --> 00:22:05.090
So that means there are no added hormones

00:22:05.090 --> 00:22:07.693
or steroids in American KFC chicken.

00:22:07.693 --> 00:22:09.995
In addition to this, as of 2019,

00:22:09.995 --> 00:22:12.898
Yum Brands, the parent company of KFC,

00:22:12.898 --> 00:22:16.802
stopped purchasing chicken
raised using antibiotics.

00:22:16.802 --> 00:22:18.837
Indian chicken farmers
were previously criticized

00:22:18.837 --> 00:22:20.972
for overusing antibiotics.

00:22:20.972 --> 00:22:24.042
As recently as 2018, The Bureau
of Investigative Journalism

00:22:24.042 --> 00:22:27.079
found out that a lot of Indian
farmers were feeding colistin

00:22:27.079 --> 00:22:29.014
to their chickens as a growth promoter

00:22:29.014 --> 00:22:30.882
without any medical supervision.

00:22:30.882 --> 00:22:34.152
Colistin is known as the
antibiotic of the last resort.

00:22:34.152 --> 00:22:35.454
Holy f---.

00:22:35.454 --> 00:22:38.490
Oh, my God, that's so frightening!

00:22:38.490 --> 00:22:40.292
And it's only given to humans

00:22:40.292 --> 00:22:42.527
when other antibiotics have failed.

00:22:42.527 --> 00:22:44.696
So if we give our chickens colistin,

00:22:44.696 --> 00:22:47.666
then the humans who consume it
might become resistant to it.

00:22:47.666 --> 00:22:51.303
In fact, they can develop a
antibiotic-resistant superbug,

00:22:51.303 --> 00:22:52.537
and that's not good.

00:22:52.537 --> 00:22:55.874
Yuelei, this sounds like
the plot to a horror movie.

00:22:55.874 --> 00:22:58.276
What is he talking about?

00:22:58.276 --> 00:22:59.945
That is terrifying.

00:22:59.945 --> 00:23:02.381
I'm gonna assume we don't do that here?

00:23:02.381 --> 00:23:05.083
And if we do, oh, God.

00:23:05.083 --> 00:23:06.518
But when a report came out

00:23:06.518 --> 00:23:07.953
talking about the ill effects of colistin,

00:23:07.953 --> 00:23:09.855
India ended up banning it completely,

00:23:09.855 --> 00:23:12.858
so we're safe from colistin, at last.

00:23:12.858 --> 00:23:14.926
We should also point out
that the KFC India website

00:23:14.926 --> 00:23:16.862
is in major need of an update.

00:23:16.862 --> 00:23:19.765
There is an FAQ page where
people have asked things like,

00:23:19.765 --> 00:23:21.800
"How many calories does
this chicken have?"

00:23:21.800 --> 00:23:25.504
Or, "Sometimes I see red
deposits in my chicken.

00:23:25.504 --> 00:23:27.406
What is it?"

00:23:27.406 --> 00:23:29.074
And for almost all of these questions,

00:23:29.074 --> 00:23:31.109
the answers are just filler text.

00:23:31.109 --> 00:23:33.712
So if you ask me what
those red deposits are,

00:23:33.712 --> 00:23:35.380
I genuinely don't know.

00:23:35.380 --> 00:23:36.415
That's interesting. Let's take a look

00:23:36.415 --> 00:23:38.216
at this website right now.

00:23:38.216 --> 00:23:41.253
Ahem. "Is KFC providing
healthcare to their employees?"

00:23:41.253 --> 00:23:42.354
KFC responds,

00:23:42.354 --> 00:23:45.323
"standard dummy text ever since the 1500s,

