00:35:15.646 --> 00:35:17.081
Hot apple juice. When are you gonna,

00:35:17.081 --> 00:35:19.484
"Ooh, I want some apple
juice right about now"?

00:35:19.484 --> 00:35:20.718
"I haven't seen you in forever!

00:35:20.718 --> 00:35:22.353
Let's meet up for apple juice."

00:35:22.353 --> 00:35:24.355
Cinnamon dolce crème.

00:35:24.355 --> 00:35:25.356
Ugh!

00:35:25.356 --> 00:35:26.991
Steamed milk.

00:35:26.991 --> 00:35:27.825
Eh, barf!

00:35:27.825 --> 00:35:29.026
Vanilla crème.

00:35:29.026 --> 00:35:31.229
When you walk past that ice
cream place in the mall,

00:35:31.229 --> 00:35:34.065
it tastes the way it
smells, like strong vanilla.

00:35:34.065 --> 00:35:35.533
I couldn't imagine having
more than two sips of that.

00:35:35.533 --> 00:35:36.834
Already my stomach's starting to hurt.

00:35:36.834 --> 00:35:38.069
I'm gonna be so sick.

00:35:38.069 --> 00:35:40.538
And now it's time for the cold exclusives.

00:35:40.538 --> 00:35:43.374
I'm not having a caffeine crash at all.

00:35:43.374 --> 00:35:44.342
[error ding]

00:35:44.342 --> 00:35:45.943
The citrus cold brew.

00:35:46.911 --> 00:35:47.912
Citrusy.

00:35:47.912 --> 00:35:51.916
Out of everything, this one has
kind of a nice, mild flavor.

00:35:51.916 --> 00:35:54.118
The cocoa chai almond.

00:35:56.888 --> 00:35:58.689
Ooh, I just had such a mild one.

00:35:58.689 --> 00:36:02.426
I took a big sip, and
this one is sweet again.

00:36:02.426 --> 00:36:05.563
Vietnamese caramel cold brew.

00:36:05.563 --> 00:36:07.398
It should typically have condensed milk,

00:36:07.398 --> 00:36:09.967
but this has normal milk,
and it's quite good.

00:36:09.967 --> 00:36:11.402
Nitro cold brew.

00:36:11.402 --> 00:36:12.603
It's basically cold brew,

00:36:12.603 --> 00:36:14.906
but if you press a button,
you drink it faster.

00:36:14.906 --> 00:36:15.873
[ba-dum tish]

00:36:15.873 --> 00:36:17.308
Dumb joke.

00:36:17.308 --> 00:36:19.310
It tastes like any other cold brew.

00:36:19.310 --> 00:36:23.214
I'd be interested to know
what the nitrogen process is.

00:36:23.214 --> 00:36:24.882
What is nitro cold brew?

00:36:24.882 --> 00:36:26.918
Well, they add nitrogen to it.

00:36:26.918 --> 00:36:28.519
And you know what that does?

00:36:28.519 --> 00:36:29.554
I have no idea.

00:36:30.488 --> 00:36:33.057
Next up, chocolate truffle cold brew.

00:36:33.057 --> 00:36:36.127
You know, that sounds like
something your child self

00:36:36.127 --> 00:36:38.162
and your adult self would want to combine

00:36:38.162 --> 00:36:39.830
if they had to collaborate on a drink.

00:36:39.830 --> 00:36:41.199
Let's see if it's actually good.

00:36:42.466 --> 00:36:44.402
Absolutely not.

00:36:44.402 --> 00:36:48.272
Oh, my God, stardust mocha again.

00:36:48.272 --> 00:36:49.373
Mm.

00:36:49.373 --> 00:36:51.909
I still don't know what
the hell stardust is.

00:36:51.909 --> 00:36:53.844
There are chunks of something.

00:36:53.844 --> 00:36:55.846
Something otherworldly.

00:36:55.846 --> 00:36:58.282
It's like cookies and cream. It's an Oreo.

00:36:58.282 --> 00:36:59.584
It's an Oreo!

00:36:59.584 --> 00:37:03.254
Thandai spice, same flavor, but now cold.

00:37:03.254 --> 00:37:04.088
Mm,

00:37:04.088 --> 00:37:05.990
hm!

00:37:05.990 --> 00:37:09.627
Too much sugar for one
young man to consume.

00:37:09.627 --> 00:37:11.028
I'm losing it!

00:37:11.028 --> 00:37:12.930
I'm seeing the light.

00:37:12.930 --> 00:37:14.165
Oh, no, I'm literally seeing the light.

00:37:14.165 --> 00:37:15.299
There's a light above me.

00:37:15.299 --> 00:37:16.400
You know, the funny thing is

00:37:16.400 --> 00:37:18.035
thandai is meant to be consumed cold,

00:37:18.035 --> 00:37:21.305
so this is the appropriate
temperature and way to drink it.

00:37:21.305 --> 00:37:23.975
But it's layered with
so much whipped cream,

00:37:23.975 --> 00:37:25.876
and it's so sweet.

00:37:25.876 --> 00:37:29.647
Thandai requires a balance
of spices and sweetness,

00:37:29.647 --> 00:37:31.716
and that's what this is lacking.

00:37:31.716 --> 00:37:33.784
And the final two drinks
are salted caramel

00:37:33.784 --> 00:37:36.854
and strawberry with cream,
but I already tasted those.

00:37:36.854 --> 00:37:39.390
Maybe it got better with
time, you never know.

00:37:39.390 --> 00:37:41.225
You ought to give everything a chance.

00:37:42.660 --> 00:37:44.795
I'm never giving anything
a chance ever again.

00:37:44.795 --> 00:37:46.864
And now for the pre-bottled drinks.

00:37:46.864 --> 00:37:48.933
They've got three of
them in 1-liter bottles.

00:37:48.933 --> 00:37:52.203
This is the iced shaken hibiscus lemonade.

00:37:52.203 --> 00:37:53.904
Looks quite refreshing.

00:37:54.972 --> 00:37:55.973
Mm.

00:37:55.973 --> 00:37:57.875
That is very nice.

00:37:57.875 --> 00:38:00.177
It says it serves four to five cups,

00:38:00.177 --> 00:38:01.979
which, if you're in an Indian family,

00:38:01.979 --> 00:38:04.482
they're going to make this
last for at least 20 people.

00:38:04.482 --> 00:38:06.484
And it's very reminiscent of Rooh Afza,

00:38:06.484 --> 00:38:08.653
which is a rose flavoring
that we add to water,

00:38:08.653 --> 00:38:09.820
and it's super delicious.

00:38:09.820 --> 00:38:11.622
I think this is a good substitute.

00:38:11.622 --> 00:38:14.025
White mocha caramel cold brew.

00:38:15.126 --> 00:38:16.560
Oh, my God.

00:38:16.560 --> 00:38:19.730
I've gotten to the stage
where I can smell sugar.

00:38:19.730 --> 00:38:21.165
I can see sugar.

00:38:21.165 --> 00:38:22.667
I can hear sugar.

00:38:22.667 --> 00:38:25.303
I think I am sugar at this point.

00:38:25.303 --> 00:38:27.305
Starbucks signature chocolate.

00:38:27.305 --> 00:38:29.507
Normally I would be
very excited about this,

00:38:29.507 --> 00:38:33.077
but I am so soaked to the
brim with sweet stuff.

00:38:34.078 --> 00:38:34.979
It's actually good.

00:38:34.979 --> 00:38:36.347
It's, like, the amount of chocolate

00:38:36.347 --> 00:38:38.049
you want to put in your cocoa,

00:38:38.049 --> 00:38:40.885
but you know it's
probably not good for you.

00:38:40.885 --> 00:38:43.554
I'm losing my goddamn mind. [laughs]

00:38:43.554 --> 00:38:45.056
All right, starting down here.

00:38:45.056 --> 00:38:46.691
Something you can only get in the US

00:38:46.691 --> 00:38:50.161
is the mocha cookie crumble Frappuccino.

00:38:50.161 --> 00:38:52.963
It's looking a little sad.

00:38:52.963 --> 00:38:56.634
So, "Food Wars" tip, bring your own whip.

00:38:57.935 --> 00:38:59.537
That's another one of Joe's tips!

00:38:59.537 --> 00:39:02.206
Mm, I'm not getting the cookie part of it.

00:39:02.206 --> 00:39:04.342
It just tastes like a chocolate milkshake.

00:39:04.342 --> 00:39:05.976
I don't know if that's really
doing much for the flavor.

00:39:05.976 --> 00:39:08.713
The caramel ribbon crunch Frappuccino.

00:39:09.647 --> 00:39:11.515
I don't know how anyone could
drink a whole one of these.

00:39:11.515 --> 00:39:13.084
The recommended serving for this, Joe,

00:39:13.084 --> 00:39:14.585
should be, like, two sips.

00:39:14.585 --> 00:39:17.088
It's like, sip No. 2,
and I'm good for a week.

00:39:17.088 --> 00:39:17.922
Ugh.

00:39:17.922 --> 00:39:19.256
The high-fructose corn syrup

00:39:19.256 --> 00:39:21.125
is working overtime in that one.

00:39:21.125 --> 00:39:23.728
The caffè vanilla Frappuccino.

00:39:25.029 --> 00:39:26.797
You know I always keep this thang on me.

00:39:27.665 --> 00:39:29.800
The least objectionable one, I guess.

00:39:29.800 --> 00:39:31.202
Actually a little weak, to be honest.

00:39:31.202 --> 00:39:33.471
Then again, after these two,
maybe it's perfectly fine.

00:39:33.471 --> 00:39:35.806
Nitro, the official cold brew

00:39:35.806 --> 00:39:38.542
of the "Fast and Furious"
franchise, Joseph.

00:39:38.542 --> 00:39:40.444
Just pour this on your
engine, and off you go,

00:39:40.444 --> 00:39:42.113
off you and Vin Diesel go.

00:39:42.113 --> 00:39:43.814
It doesn't require ice.

00:39:43.814 --> 00:39:45.383
Has a smoother flavor, right?

00:39:45.383 --> 00:39:46.851
Now, if you want something
a little bit sweeter

00:39:46.851 --> 00:39:47.818
in your cold brew,

00:39:47.818 --> 00:39:51.055
you can get yourself a vanilla
sweet cream nitro cold brew.

00:39:52.456 --> 00:39:53.424
Joe fucks with it.

00:39:53.424 --> 00:39:54.959
We got a vanilla oat milk,

00:39:54.959 --> 00:39:56.560
we got a brown sugar oat milk,

00:39:56.560 --> 00:39:58.729
and we got a chocolate almond milk.

00:39:58.729 --> 00:40:00.131
Here they are.

00:40:00.131 --> 00:40:01.866
Not as strong of a flavor
as I thought it would be.

00:40:01.866 --> 00:40:02.800
Brown sugar.

00:40:03.634 --> 00:40:04.902
I'm definitely tasting it.

00:40:04.902 --> 00:40:06.003
Yeah, not bad.

00:40:06.003 --> 00:40:08.239
I have reason to believe
this was unshooken.

00:40:08.239 --> 00:40:09.240
Think I could shake it without?

00:40:11.142 --> 00:40:13.544
I would recommend this
one out of all three,

00:40:13.544 --> 00:40:16.280
but insist they shake it in front of you.

00:40:16.280 --> 00:40:18.048
You can get yourself an iced flat white

00:40:18.048 --> 00:40:19.917
and an iced honey flat white.

00:40:22.953 --> 00:40:23.788
Skip 'em.

00:40:23.788 --> 00:40:25.656
Iced cinnamon dolce latte

00:40:25.656 --> 00:40:28.659
and an iced Starbucks blond latte.

00:40:28.659 --> 00:40:29.493
Not bad.

00:40:30.728 --> 00:40:32.897
Can confirm a sip is good.

00:40:32.897 --> 00:40:34.165
I don't know about a whole one of these.

00:40:34.165 --> 00:40:36.233
Already I'm kind of like, eh.

00:40:36.233 --> 00:40:37.868
Starbuck teas,

00:40:37.868 --> 00:40:39.603
or, as my mum calls them,

00:40:39.603 --> 00:40:41.071
"I can make this at home."

00:40:41.071 --> 00:40:44.108
Starting off with Indian spice majestic.

00:40:44.108 --> 00:40:45.576
Wow, OK.

00:40:46.444 --> 00:40:48.045
Oh! Can I just say,

00:40:48.045 --> 00:40:49.647
drinking this after everything else

00:40:49.647 --> 00:40:51.749
is such a breath of fresh air.

00:40:51.749 --> 00:40:53.584
You know, it's a simple tea,

00:40:53.584 --> 00:40:56.754
but it's very flavorful, very spicy.

00:40:56.754 --> 00:40:57.788
Would recommend.

00:40:57.788 --> 00:41:01.058
Next up, matcha espresso fusion.

00:41:01.058 --> 00:41:04.361
It's part of the trifecta
of three ingredients

00:41:04.361 --> 00:41:06.197
that have become very popular in India.

00:41:06.197 --> 00:41:10.367
Matcha, peri-peri, and red velvet.

00:41:12.870 --> 00:41:16.674
I feel like the espresso counters
the sweetness that it has,

00:41:16.674 --> 00:41:18.075
and the matcha flavor's there.

00:41:18.075 --> 00:41:19.810
Again, just cut down on the sweetness,

00:41:19.810 --> 00:41:21.612
and this would actually be good.

00:41:21.612 --> 00:41:25.349
Now, the exclusive hot teas
you get here in the US.

00:41:25.349 --> 00:41:28.919
The royal English breakfast tea latte,

00:41:28.919 --> 00:41:31.689
London fog tea latte,

00:41:31.689 --> 00:41:34.158
honey citrus mint tea,

00:41:34.158 --> 00:41:36.961
a jade citrus mint brewed tea,

00:41:36.961 --> 00:41:39.396
the mint majesty.

00:41:39.396 --> 00:41:41.799
Mint, matcha, green, all bad.

00:41:41.799 --> 00:41:44.068
The trinity of gross. I don't want it.

00:41:44.068 --> 00:41:46.437
The peach tranquility.

00:41:46.437 --> 00:41:47.872
And they spell it "tranquility,"

00:41:47.872 --> 00:41:49.840
but it should be tranquili-T-E-A.

00:41:49.840 --> 00:41:51.242
I feel like they missed a trick there.

00:41:51.242 --> 00:41:52.910
OK, so those are the two hot teas.

00:41:52.910 --> 00:41:54.445
It's now time for the cold teas,

00:41:54.445 --> 00:41:57.448
starting with an iced green tea.

00:41:57.448 --> 00:41:59.850
I feel like when you
start drinking green tea,

00:41:59.850 --> 00:42:03.687
it's a sign of adulthood,
and there's no going back.

00:42:03.687 --> 00:42:04.788
That's actually pretty good.

00:42:04.788 --> 00:42:06.357
And now I feel old.

00:42:07.358 --> 00:42:10.127
Hibiscus passion lemonade.

00:42:10.127 --> 00:42:11.829
So many ingredients,

00:42:11.829 --> 00:42:13.631
but I know I'm going to taste only sugar.

00:42:13.631 --> 00:42:16.800
Hey, that's pretty good.

00:42:16.800 --> 00:42:19.069
It's kind of flowery, fruity.

00:42:19.069 --> 00:42:20.371
I really like this.

00:42:20.371 --> 00:42:23.641
A maveha espresso fusion.

00:42:23.641 --> 00:42:25.075
Oh, this is an iced matcha?

00:42:25.075 --> 00:42:26.911
Oh, OK, sorry.

00:42:26.911 --> 00:42:28.345
My bad, my bad. It's,

00:42:28.345 --> 00:42:30.581
guys, it's the Starbucks handwriting.

00:42:30.581 --> 00:42:32.116
Honestly, sometimes I think it's just

00:42:32.116 --> 00:42:34.885
doctors writing prescriptions
on these coffee mugs.

00:42:34.885 --> 00:42:36.353
By the way, let me know in the comments,

00:42:36.353 --> 00:42:38.422
what's the weirdest way
somebody has spelled your name

00:42:38.422 --> 00:42:39.590
in Starbucks?

00:42:40.558 --> 00:42:44.428
Mm. I prefer this to
the weird hot sweet one.

00:42:44.428 --> 00:42:46.730
Yeah, I like the teas way
more than the coffees.

00:42:46.730 --> 00:42:49.667
So, I don't know what
that says about Starbucks,

00:42:49.667 --> 00:42:51.702
but I'm a fan.

00:42:51.702 --> 00:42:53.103
I feel the exact opposite.

00:42:53.103 --> 00:42:54.505
I do not like tea at all.

00:42:54.505 --> 00:42:56.974
And this is all the
stuff on a Starbucks menu

00:42:56.974 --> 00:42:59.243
I have never gotten and
would like to never get.

00:42:59.243 --> 00:43:01.178
But, gotta do it. It's the job.

00:43:01.178 --> 00:43:03.047
So we will start down here.

00:43:03.047 --> 00:43:06.150
At the Starbucks in the
US, you can get yourself

00:43:06.150 --> 00:43:09.320
iced black tea and an
iced black tea lemonade.

00:43:09.320 --> 00:43:10.654
Moving on, you can get peach teas.

00:43:10.654 --> 00:43:11.989
We got an iced peach green tea

00:43:11.989 --> 00:43:14.692
and an iced peach tea lemonade.

00:43:14.692 --> 00:43:17.127
So, this tastes good because
it's peach and lemonade.

00:43:17.127 --> 00:43:18.095
I don't taste any tea.

00:43:18.095 --> 00:43:21.498
Green iced green tea lemonade.

00:43:21.498 --> 00:43:23.701
Oh, grande, not -- the first GR is grande.

00:43:23.701 --> 00:43:25.336
Grande iced green tea latte.

00:43:25.336 --> 00:43:26.804
"Latte." Lemonade.

00:43:26.804 --> 00:43:28.372
Ugh, I'm losing it. See? I don't,

00:43:28.372 --> 00:43:31.809
I stop drinking caffeine for
a second, and I fall apart.

00:43:31.809 --> 00:43:33.811
Oh, matcha? No!

00:43:33.811 --> 00:43:35.713
No, not matcha!

00:43:35.713 --> 00:43:37.848
Grande matcha lemonade.
All right, lemonade.

00:43:37.848 --> 00:43:40.985
Lemonade is doing all the
heavy lifting on all of these.

00:43:41.919 --> 00:43:42.987
I absolutely hate this.

00:43:42.987 --> 00:43:45.456
Royal English breakfast.

00:43:45.456 --> 00:43:47.024
Mm!

00:43:47.024 --> 00:43:48.158
You know what'll help?

00:43:48.158 --> 00:43:49.493
A little caffeine.

00:43:49.493 --> 00:43:50.928
Mm!

00:43:50.928 --> 00:43:52.262
Whoo! All right.

00:43:52.262 --> 00:43:54.131
Also at Starbucks, you can get
something called Refreshers.

00:43:54.131 --> 00:43:56.333
From what I can tell,
they are fruit juices

00:43:56.333 --> 00:43:58.235
with fruit in it. Imagine that.

00:43:58.235 --> 00:43:59.937
I would never normally get a Refresher,

00:43:59.937 --> 00:44:02.106
I just wouldn't think to, but
now I get to try all of them!

00:44:02.106 --> 00:44:04.174
Pink drink!

00:44:04.174 --> 00:44:05.809
Ooh, yeah. Fruity.

00:44:05.809 --> 00:44:09.513
Moving on, we have the
strawberry acai lemonade.

00:44:10.581 --> 00:44:11.415
I like this.

00:44:11.415 --> 00:44:13.484
Similar problem to a
lot of the Frappuccinos.

00:44:13.484 --> 00:44:15.586
One taste, and I'm like,
I could get into it.

00:44:15.586 --> 00:44:16.687
But a whole one of these,

00:44:16.687 --> 00:44:19.256
I feel my gut kind of starting to, blech.

00:44:19.256 --> 00:44:21.825
Just the mango dragon fruit, right?

00:44:21.825 --> 00:44:23.093
Dragon drink.

00:44:23.093 --> 00:44:26.897
Mango dragon fruit lemonade.

00:44:26.897 --> 00:44:28.465
I think this is the best one so far.

00:44:28.465 --> 00:44:29.299
[beep]

00:44:29.299 --> 00:44:31.435
One second. All right. Don't put that in.

00:44:31.435 --> 00:44:32.269
[beep]

00:44:32.269 --> 00:44:35.139
Moving on, we have the green drink zone.

00:44:35.139 --> 00:44:37.274
Star drink. Assuming star fruit.

00:44:37.274 --> 00:44:38.275
Kiwi star fruit.

00:44:38.275 --> 00:44:40.978
Does lemonade kick it
up even another notch?

00:44:40.978 --> 00:44:42.846
Hm, this one, I like the flavor the best,

00:44:42.846 --> 00:44:43.947
but it's a little strong.

00:44:43.947 --> 00:44:44.982
Yeah, all these are pretty good.

00:44:44.982 --> 00:44:48.085
The last Refresher is the

00:44:48.085 --> 00:44:50.254
strawberry acai.

00:44:50.254 --> 00:44:51.689
They have a regular lemonade

00:44:51.689 --> 00:44:53.157
and a blended strawberry lemonade.

00:44:53.157 --> 00:44:54.458
I mean, come on. Lemonade?

00:44:54.458 --> 00:44:56.460
Everything else that's had
lemonade in it, I've enjoyed.

00:44:56.460 --> 00:44:59.229
So let's just go straight to the source.

00:44:59.229 --> 00:45:00.064
Whoa, dude.

00:45:00.064 --> 00:45:02.066
Starbucks lemonade is, like, really good.

00:45:02.066 --> 00:45:03.600
Is this even in the top
10 things you would get

00:45:03.600 --> 00:45:05.335
at Starbucks, a lemonade? What?

00:45:05.335 --> 00:45:08.939
Now, if you like your lemonade,
a little bit of strawberry.

00:45:09.940 --> 00:45:11.141
This is fantastic.

00:45:11.141 --> 00:45:11.975
Wow.

00:45:11.975 --> 00:45:14.344
Even after all these, this is a standout.

00:45:14.344 --> 00:45:15.546
This is really good.

00:45:15.546 --> 00:45:16.914
Why is this so good?

00:45:19.349 --> 00:45:20.417
Fantastic.

00:45:20.417 --> 00:45:21.685
Food!

00:45:21.685 --> 00:45:23.687
We have a lot of Indian exclusives.

00:45:23.687 --> 00:45:26.023
I'm going to start with the salads.

00:45:26.023 --> 00:45:28.058
This is a vegetarian grain salad.

00:45:28.058 --> 00:45:30.661
It's got quinoa, it's
got some paneer in it,

00:45:30.661 --> 00:45:34.965
it's got corn kernels that look unborn.

00:45:36.266 --> 00:45:39.570
I'm sure this is super healthy,
but it's also very dry.

00:45:39.570 --> 00:45:42.406
Now the meat version of
it. It's got chicken.

00:45:43.440 --> 00:45:45.442
I'm not really a fan of cold salads.

00:45:45.442 --> 00:45:47.945
If you are a health freak,
you might enjoy this.

00:45:47.945 --> 00:45:51.715
But if you're a fan of
food, you probably won't.

00:45:51.715 --> 00:45:53.884
OK, next up, I'm going to
try all of their rolls.

00:45:53.884 --> 00:45:55.986
Rolls are a huge staple here in India.

00:45:55.986 --> 00:45:58.155
They're one of the most
famous street foods,

00:45:58.155 --> 00:46:00.958
and it's great for the
working-class citizen.

00:46:00.958 --> 00:46:03.393
This is the murgh kathi roll.

00:46:03.393 --> 00:46:06.163
Murgh means chicken in Hindi.

00:46:07.765 --> 00:46:09.466
Oh, that's pretty good.

00:46:09.466 --> 00:46:11.835
Finally! Some spice!

00:46:11.835 --> 00:46:14.338
Oh, my God. This is a life-saver.

00:46:14.338 --> 00:46:16.473
I feel like I'm being brought back to life

00:46:16.473 --> 00:46:18.842
after all those drinks.
This is really good.

00:46:18.842 --> 00:46:21.111
You'll find this only in
India, but honestly, Starbucks,

00:46:21.111 --> 00:46:22.813
you should consider selling this all over,

00:46:22.813 --> 00:46:25.249
because it is tasty.

00:46:25.249 --> 00:46:27.084
Next up is a kakori kebab roll.

00:46:27.084 --> 00:46:31.188
Kakori kebab is basically
minced meat, typically lamb,

00:46:31.188 --> 00:46:34.625
and it's served with a paratha or a roti.

00:46:34.625 --> 00:46:35.793
I've never seen it in a roll,

00:46:35.793 --> 00:46:38.195
and I've never seen it in a pink roll.

00:46:40.531 --> 00:46:42.099
Mm, you can see.

00:46:42.099 --> 00:46:43.700
The main thing about a kakori kebab is

00:46:43.700 --> 00:46:45.636
it should melt in your mouth.

00:46:45.636 --> 00:46:47.538
This has too much of a bite to it.

00:46:47.538 --> 00:46:48.505
Not a fan.

00:46:48.505 --> 00:46:50.874
Next up, chatpata paneer roll.

00:46:50.874 --> 00:46:54.745
Chatpata means full of masala
and flavor, and it's zingy.

00:46:54.745 --> 00:46:56.747
And paneer is cottage cheese.

00:46:56.747 --> 00:46:58.982
We love our cottage cheese here in India,

00:46:58.982 --> 00:47:01.685
and we call it paneer. And you should too.

00:47:01.685 --> 00:47:03.821
Next up, cheese chili toast.

00:47:03.821 --> 00:47:05.756
So, obviously, if you
order this at Starbucks,

00:47:05.756 --> 00:47:08.258
I assume they actually toast
this and the cheese melts

00:47:08.258 --> 00:47:09.526
and it's super delicious.

00:47:10.961 --> 00:47:11.895
I can tell you right now,

00:47:11.895 --> 00:47:14.464
this flavor profile will go
really well with Indians.

00:47:14.464 --> 00:47:16.166
We love our cheese chili toast.

00:47:16.166 --> 00:47:19.203
Monsoon season, mum goes to the kitchen,

00:47:19.203 --> 00:47:22.639
toasts the bread, lot of
butter, some cheese, some chili.

00:47:22.639 --> 00:47:24.441
Bite into it, your mouth's on fire,

00:47:24.441 --> 00:47:26.710
but it's rainy and cold, so you're all OK.

00:47:26.710 --> 00:47:29.346
This is not quite there,
but I feel like it could be.

00:47:29.346 --> 00:47:31.715
Next up, tandoori paneer sandwich.

00:47:31.715 --> 00:47:36.286
I'm gonna have to say that
this bread is a little hard,

00:47:36.286 --> 00:47:37.855
to say the least.

00:47:37.855 --> 00:47:39.823
Might be a bit of an old sandwich.

00:47:41.458 --> 00:47:42.793
Flavor is good, though.

00:47:42.793 --> 00:47:45.796
If I had any of this food
fresh at a Starbucks,

00:47:45.796 --> 00:47:47.764
I might have a very different opinion.

00:47:47.764 --> 00:47:50.801
So far, the paneer items
have been way better

00:47:50.801 --> 00:47:52.302
than the meat items.

00:47:52.302 --> 00:47:53.370
I'm starting to guess there's somebody

00:47:53.370 --> 00:47:56.406
in the Starbucks R&amp;D team
who really likes paneer.

00:47:56.406 --> 00:47:58.675
Sandwiches and protein boxes, here we go.

00:47:58.675 --> 00:48:01.078
You can get a bunch of
exclusive sandwiches,

00:48:01.078 --> 00:48:03.146
US Starbucks, starting right here,

00:48:03.146 --> 00:48:07.417
with the crispy grilled
cheese on sourdough, again.

00:48:07.417 --> 00:48:09.519
Ham and cheese on a baguette.

00:48:09.519 --> 00:48:14.024
Then we get the turkey pesto
with provolone on ciabatta.

00:48:14.024 --> 00:48:16.093
Chicken and bacon on brioche.

00:48:16.093 --> 00:48:17.160
Why is it -- could we get that chicken

00:48:17.160 --> 00:48:18.428
on the whole thing here, guys?

00:48:18.428 --> 00:48:21.064
A focaccia tomato mozzarella.

00:48:21.064 --> 00:48:21.932
At a Starbucks, you can get

00:48:21.932 --> 00:48:24.935
a chicken caprese on ciabatta sandwich.

00:48:24.935 --> 00:48:28.272
On to the protein boxes.

00:48:28.272 --> 00:48:30.173
The chickpea bites and avocado.

00:48:30.173 --> 00:48:31.708
You can tell what's in there.

00:48:31.708 --> 00:48:34.511
Obviously avocado, chickpea bites.

00:48:34.511 --> 00:48:36.880
Egg and cheddar.

00:48:36.880 --> 00:48:38.215
Cheese and fruit.

00:48:38.215 --> 00:48:40.183
Peanut butter and jam.

00:48:40.183 --> 00:48:43.086
Grilled chicken and hummus.
There's your hummus,

00:48:43.086 --> 00:48:44.755
there's your pita, there's
your grilled chicken.

00:48:44.755 --> 00:48:45.789
You can also get,

00:48:45.789 --> 00:48:47.991
which was not available
at the store today,

00:48:47.991 --> 00:48:49.960
egg and Gouda protein box,

00:48:49.960 --> 00:48:51.695
a cheese trio protein box,

00:48:51.695 --> 00:48:54.164
and a cheddar and salami protein box.

00:48:54.164 --> 00:48:58.769
Next up, egg white and
chicken multigrain croissant.

00:48:58.769 --> 00:49:02.172
Should I just call it a
croy-sant to upset people,

00:49:02.172 --> 00:49:03.640
the denizens of the internet?

00:49:04.975 --> 00:49:07.077
If you are somebody trying
to be protein-conscious,

00:49:07.077 --> 00:49:09.646
put on the pounds, this
might be good for you.

00:49:09.646 --> 00:49:12.950
Next up, a masala chicken croissant.

00:49:14.151 --> 00:49:17.321
I guess you can't go
wrong with masala chicken.

00:49:17.321 --> 00:49:19.489
You can go wrong with a croissant.

00:49:19.489 --> 00:49:20.624
This tastes really good.

00:49:20.624 --> 00:49:24.494
Next up, a basil, tomato,
mozzarella sandwich.

00:49:25.929 --> 00:49:28.532
I can imagine just eating
this on a summer day.

00:49:28.532 --> 00:49:29.366
Really yum.

00:49:29.366 --> 00:49:33.103
Next up, creamy spinach and corn pocket.

00:49:33.103 --> 00:49:34.905
Pocket! That's pretty cute.

00:49:34.905 --> 00:49:37.441
As a kid, this was the only
way I enjoyed eating spinach,

00:49:37.441 --> 00:49:39.576
unless it was in palak paneer.

00:49:39.576 --> 00:49:41.011
But right now, I appreciate,

00:49:41.011 --> 00:49:43.680
and I really like it in this pocket.

00:49:43.680 --> 00:49:46.350
Next up, chicken seekh pocket.

00:49:46.350 --> 00:49:48.618
Seekh kebab is basically minced meat,

00:49:48.618 --> 00:49:51.989
and it's sort of pressed onto
a skewer and then grilled.

00:49:51.989 --> 00:49:53.357
Over here, they've done
that, and then they've

00:49:53.357 --> 00:49:56.193
chopped them into little sausage pieces.

00:49:57.828 --> 00:50:01.298
Mm. Minty, it has that pudina flavor,

00:50:01.298 --> 00:50:03.233
a lot of onions that have
just been caramelized,

00:50:03.233 --> 00:50:06.670
so it's sweet but also
spicy. I really like this.

00:50:06.670 --> 00:50:09.773
Starting with the breakfast
sandwiches and wraps,

00:50:09.773 --> 00:50:12.576
the bacon, Gouda, egg. There's
Gouda somewhere on here.

00:50:12.576 --> 00:50:14.544
A sausage, egg, and cheddar.

00:50:14.544 --> 00:50:17.180
The double-smoked bacon,
cheddar, and egg. Dude.

00:50:17.180 --> 00:50:18.315
It's good.

00:50:18.315 --> 00:50:19.983
Ham and Swiss croissant.

00:50:19.983 --> 00:50:22.019
A bacon, sausage, and egg wrap.

00:50:22.019 --> 00:50:23.387
What's up?

00:50:23.387 --> 00:50:24.388
I didn't ...

00:50:26.223 --> 00:50:27.924
Other sandwiches you can get are

00:50:27.924 --> 00:50:29.860
spinach, feta, egg wrap,

00:50:29.860 --> 00:50:30.961
the roasted ham,

00:50:30.961 --> 00:50:33.130
the turkey bacon, cheddar,
and egg white sandwich,

00:50:33.130 --> 00:50:35.365
and the Impossible breakfast sandwich.

00:50:35.365 --> 00:50:36.299
But you know what they do have?

00:50:36.299 --> 00:50:37.701
Bacon and Gruyère.

00:50:37.701 --> 00:50:39.603
Egg white and roasted red pepper.

00:50:39.603 --> 00:50:40.871
Kale and mushroom.

00:50:40.871 --> 00:50:43.907
Get yourself an avocado
spread. For dipping.

00:50:43.907 --> 00:50:45.342
Bagels!

00:50:45.342 --> 00:50:46.476
We got 'em.

00:50:46.476 --> 00:50:47.878
Can I assume this is an everything?

00:50:47.878 --> 00:50:49.046
'Cause it's got everything.

00:50:49.046 --> 00:50:50.213
Cinnamon raisin.

00:50:50.213 --> 00:50:52.082
I can tell because of the raisins.

00:50:52.082 --> 00:50:55.052
Hey, plain. For the New Yorker, right?

00:50:55.052 --> 00:50:57.187
Oatmeal! Oatmeal.

00:50:57.187 --> 00:51:00.557
We got regular, and they
come with a nut medley,

00:51:00.557 --> 00:51:02.559
brown sugar, dried fruit.

00:51:02.559 --> 00:51:05.662
I bet it's like a puck now.
It's been sitting for a while.

00:51:05.662 --> 00:51:07.397
All right. [crew laughing]

00:51:07.397 --> 00:51:08.698
You can also get a blueberry one.

00:51:08.698 --> 00:51:10.901
It's obviously just same
stuff with blueberries.

00:51:10.901 --> 00:51:13.770
Strawberry and overnight grains.

00:51:13.770 --> 00:51:17.074
Next up, a double chocolate chip cookie.

00:51:18.508 --> 00:51:21.211
I think if I put this in a
microwave for five seconds,

00:51:21.211 --> 00:51:23.280
this is a banging, banging cookie.

00:51:23.280 --> 00:51:24.448
A tea cake.

00:51:24.448 --> 00:51:26.783
This is lemon-flavored.

00:51:26.783 --> 00:51:30.020
And finally, they have a banana loaf cake,

00:51:30.020 --> 00:51:33.690
but, guys, I am dangerously
allergic to banana.

00:51:33.690 --> 00:51:35.792
And so I wish this cake the best of luck.

00:51:35.792 --> 00:51:37.727
Maybe you guys can try it and
let me know in the comments

00:51:37.727 --> 00:51:40.297
whether it's worth ordering.

00:51:40.297 --> 00:51:42.165
On to the baked goods. In the US,

00:51:42.165 --> 00:51:43.366
you can get an assortment of baked goods,

00:51:43.366 --> 00:51:44.534
as you can see in front of me.

00:51:44.534 --> 00:51:47.671
I'll just start down here. We got scones.

00:51:47.671 --> 00:51:49.406
Oh, this is a blueberry scone.

00:51:49.406 --> 00:51:51.575
Petite vanilla bean scone.

00:51:51.575 --> 00:51:53.243
These can't be the same price.

00:51:53.243 --> 00:51:54.311
Cake pops.

00:51:54.311 --> 00:51:55.645
You got chocolate.

00:51:55.645 --> 00:51:56.513
Which one do you think is Earth

00:51:56.513 --> 00:51:58.115
and which one do you think is birthday?

00:51:58.115 --> 00:51:59.483
I feel like this has got to be birthday.

00:51:59.483 --> 00:52:01.485
Glazed doughnut, ay.

00:52:01.485 --> 00:52:02.619
Red velvet cake.

00:52:02.619 --> 00:52:03.453
Pumpkin loaf.

00:52:03.453 --> 00:52:05.255
You can also get a cinnamon coffee cake.

00:52:05.255 --> 00:52:06.523
Yeah, brownie.

00:52:06.523 --> 00:52:07.891
Chocolate chip cookie.

00:52:07.891 --> 00:52:09.493
Available, yet not today,

00:52:09.493 --> 00:52:11.761
pumpkin cream cheese muffin.

00:52:11.761 --> 00:52:13.630
It is now time for ice creams.

00:52:13.630 --> 00:52:15.732
Did you know Starbucks makes ice creams?

00:52:15.732 --> 00:52:17.267
I had no idea.

00:52:17.267 --> 00:52:20.871
Java chip ice cream.
This looks really good.

00:52:20.871 --> 00:52:22.873
Check it out, son.

00:52:25.142 --> 00:52:26.109
Yum!

00:52:26.109 --> 00:52:28.211
Coffee, chocolate chips, and mocha.

00:52:28.211 --> 00:52:30.147
That is something else.
I really like this.

00:52:30.147 --> 00:52:32.415
Next up, vanilla ice
cream and chocolate sauce.

00:52:32.415 --> 00:52:34.518
Now, everybody in India,

00:52:34.518 --> 00:52:38.288
their childhood has involved
Amul vanilla ice cream

00:52:38.288 --> 00:52:40.023
and Hershey's chocolate syrup.

00:52:40.023 --> 00:52:43.593
Let's see if this sort
of evokes that nostalgia.

00:52:44.461 --> 00:52:47.197
Ooh, the vanilla ice cream is so good.

00:52:47.197 --> 00:52:49.699
Next up, vanilla ice cream
with strawberry sauce.

00:52:49.699 --> 00:52:51.601
You either got the
Hershey's chocolate sauce

00:52:51.601 --> 00:52:53.937
or the Hershey's strawberry sauce.

00:52:55.071 --> 00:52:57.974
Younger Kini would not
have appreciated this,

00:52:57.974 --> 00:53:00.343
but older Kini, really enjoying it.

00:53:00.343 --> 00:53:03.680
It's fruity, tangy, sour,
and it really complements

00:53:03.680 --> 00:53:05.582
the yummy vanilla creamy ice cream.

00:53:05.582 --> 00:53:07.684
Next up, we have the same java chip,

00:53:07.684 --> 00:53:11.688
but now with more chocolate
chips and chocolate sauce.

00:53:11.688 --> 00:53:14.124
So, this is a bit of an overload.

00:53:15.192 --> 00:53:16.026
Too much.

00:53:16.026 --> 00:53:18.461
Are you, can you zoom in on my hand?

00:53:19.896 --> 00:53:21.665
It's shaking right now.

00:53:21.665 --> 00:53:23.233
Caramel macchiato.

00:53:23.233 --> 00:53:24.668
Mm. It's really nice.

00:53:24.668 --> 00:53:27.204
It's not too sweet. It's kind of salty.

00:53:27.204 --> 00:53:31.575
Next, the affogato, which
is ice cream in coffee.

00:53:32.676 --> 00:53:35.045
I love how we're taking
hot, bitter coffee,

00:53:35.045 --> 00:53:37.681
and sweet, creamy ice
cream, mixing them together,

00:53:37.681 --> 00:53:39.816
and somehow they're not choosing violence.

00:53:39.816 --> 00:53:44.087
They're choosing to be friends,
harmonious in my mouth.

00:53:44.087 --> 00:53:46.990
Affogato again, but
this is house affogato.

00:53:46.990 --> 00:53:49.025
So I'm going to assume, Starbucks,

00:53:49.025 --> 00:53:50.493
that this should be better.

00:53:50.493 --> 00:53:52.195
You're putting your name on it.

00:53:53.897 --> 00:53:54.965
Tastes the same.

00:53:54.965 --> 00:53:58.235
And, finally, we have the
caramel macchiato ice cream.

00:53:58.235 --> 00:54:00.670
It's similar to the small cup
of caramel macchiato I had,

00:54:00.670 --> 00:54:04.608
except this does not have
a drizzle of caramel sauce.

00:54:04.608 --> 00:54:06.343
If you were ordering ice
cream from Starbucks,

00:54:06.343 --> 00:54:08.345
I would recommend the simple java chip

00:54:08.345 --> 00:54:10.614
and the simple caramel macchiato.

00:54:10.614 --> 00:54:11.982
No drizzle of sauces.

00:54:11.982 --> 00:54:14.084
It's not as sweet. It's kind of nice.

00:54:14.417 --> 00:54:16.286
Joe: From calorie count to portion sizes,

00:54:16.286 --> 00:54:21.024
we wanted to find out all the differences between McDonald's in India and the US.

00:54:21.024 --> 00:54:22.926
Joe: This is "Food Wars."

00:54:26.696 --> 00:54:29.366
Drinks in McDonald's
India come in three sizes:

00:54:29.366 --> 00:54:31.901
regular, medium, and large.

00:54:31.901 --> 00:54:34.838
Drinks in the McDonald's
in the US, four sizes:

00:54:34.838 --> 00:54:38.275
extra small, small, medium, and large.

00:54:41.177 --> 00:54:42.746
Time to keep 'em honest.

00:54:44.214 --> 00:54:47.884
Lost a couple drops. 26, 27 fluid ounces.

00:54:47.884 --> 00:54:49.586
Whoo!

00:54:49.586 --> 00:54:52.088
Hm.

00:54:52.088 --> 00:54:54.057
Fries in India come in three sizes:

00:54:54.057 --> 00:54:56.293
regular, medium, and large.

00:54:56.293 --> 00:55:00.430
In America, our fries come
in four sizes, I think.

00:55:00.430 --> 00:55:03.400
We have a small, kids,

00:55:03.400 --> 00:55:06.169
or kids, small —

00:55:06.169 --> 00:55:08.271
I can't tell the difference either —

00:55:08.271 --> 00:55:10.507
medium, and large.

00:55:10.507 --> 00:55:12.742
The medium and large
come in these really cool

00:55:12.742 --> 00:55:15.645
new packaging where you can
just open it up like that

00:55:15.645 --> 00:55:17.013
and it's nice and easy to share.

00:55:17.013 --> 00:55:18.148
It's a little plate.

00:55:18.148 --> 00:55:19.983
Good job, McDonald's. Very innovative.

00:55:19.983 --> 00:55:21.584
But now it's time to measure

00:55:21.584 --> 00:55:23.453
and see how much we're really getting.

00:55:23.453 --> 00:55:25.355
Joe: First things first, the large.

00:55:27.924 --> 00:55:29.259
175 grams.

00:55:29.259 --> 00:55:31.461
Obviously it's different
per scoops or whatever.

00:55:31.461 --> 00:55:32.495
Yeah, let's go here.

00:55:32.495 --> 00:55:36.132
This one, almost exactly 100 grams.

00:55:36.132 --> 00:55:38.068
This one,

00:55:38.068 --> 00:55:39.169
80 grams.

00:55:39.169 --> 00:55:40.370
Fry math, hang on.

00:55:42.472 --> 00:55:44.074
This is, like...

00:55:44.074 --> 00:55:45.075
yep, there you go.

00:55:45.075 --> 00:55:46.509
That's a 20-gram difference right there.

00:55:46.509 --> 00:55:48.011
So, you tell me, internet.

00:55:48.011 --> 00:55:49.913
Is the kids and the small different sizes?

00:55:49.913 --> 00:55:50.980
I don't think they are.

00:55:50.980 --> 00:55:54.050
"Food Wars" is on it! We're on it, baby!

00:55:54.050 --> 00:55:55.018
What about McNuggets?

00:55:55.018 --> 00:55:58.154
Here in India, you can
order them in three sizes:

00:55:58.154 --> 00:56:01.891
six pieces, nine pieces, and 20 pieces.

00:56:01.891 --> 00:56:04.761
They gave it to us in
two boxes of 10 each.

00:56:04.761 --> 00:56:06.730
Oh, is that it, India? Cute.

00:56:06.730 --> 00:56:09.332
Our McNuggets start at four,

00:56:09.332 --> 00:56:10.767
then you got six,

00:56:10.767 --> 00:56:12.102
10,

00:56:12.102 --> 00:56:13.336
20,

00:56:13.336 --> 00:56:14.704
and not to be outdone,

00:56:14.704 --> 00:56:17.140
booyah, 40 McNuggets.

00:56:17.140 --> 00:56:19.676
All the mathheads watching
will be quick to point out

00:56:19.676 --> 00:56:23.680
that that is double India's
largest nugget option.

00:56:23.680 --> 00:56:25.982
The only burger that
India shares with the US

00:56:25.982 --> 00:56:28.618
is the McChicken,
the humble McChicken.

00:56:28.618 --> 00:56:31.654
Not even gonna bother
with the analog scale now.

00:56:31.654 --> 00:56:32.822
Boop!

00:56:32.822 --> 00:56:34.924
149 grams.

00:56:34.924 --> 00:56:37.193
Ah, just so frustrating.

00:56:37.193 --> 00:56:39.763
Just one more gram and
it would be perfect.

00:56:39.763 --> 00:56:42.499
With the paper? I mean, we'll do this and

00:56:43.733 --> 00:56:46.836
shave off an eighth of an ounce.

00:56:46.836 --> 00:56:51.007
Our McChicken weighs 140 grams.

00:56:53.376 --> 00:56:54.744
Here is everything you'll find on the menu

00:56:54.744 --> 00:56:57.914
at McDonald's India that you
will not find in the USA.

00:56:57.914 --> 00:56:59.516
And here's all the McDonald's menu items

00:56:59.516 --> 00:57:02.685
from the US you won't find in India.

00:57:02.685 --> 00:57:04.387
Here in India, we can't really recreate

00:57:04.387 --> 00:57:06.156
the iconic McDonald's Big Mac

00:57:06.156 --> 00:57:08.057
because it's made from a beef patty,

00:57:08.057 --> 00:57:10.160
and to keep to the religious sentiments

00:57:10.160 --> 00:57:11.828
of Hindus and even Muslims,

00:57:11.828 --> 00:57:13.096
we don't serve beef or pork

00:57:13.096 --> 00:57:14.664
in a lot of fast-food restaurants.

00:57:14.664 --> 00:57:18.568
We have something called
the chicken Maharaja Mac.

00:57:18.568 --> 00:57:22.672
As you can see, it's got
three buns, two patties,

00:57:22.672 --> 00:57:25.241
a lot of cheese and mayonnaise,

00:57:25.241 --> 00:57:27.977
some tomatoes, onions, lettuce.

00:57:27.977 --> 00:57:30.914
Lettuce try it now.
[ba-dum tish]

00:57:32.449 --> 00:57:34.117
Oh, my God.

00:57:34.117 --> 00:57:36.486
That is truly a Maharaja Mac.

00:57:36.486 --> 00:57:38.822
If you're wondering, a raja is a king,

00:57:38.822 --> 00:57:41.090
and a maharaja is like an emperor.

00:57:41.090 --> 00:57:43.660
So this is clearly our
answer to the Big Mac.

00:57:43.660 --> 00:57:45.695
Now let's taste the veg Maharaja Mac.

00:57:45.695 --> 00:57:47.464
I think it's actually
a very cool challenge

00:57:47.464 --> 00:57:48.865
that a lot of fast-food restaurants here

00:57:48.865 --> 00:57:50.567
have had to adapt to the Indian palate,

00:57:50.567 --> 00:57:53.369
as well as sensibilities of food.

00:57:53.369 --> 00:57:56.039
We have come up with such
cool, iconic fast food

00:57:56.039 --> 00:57:58.041
that you won't get
anywhere else in the world.

00:57:58.041 --> 00:58:00.276
Like, look at this! This is outrageous!

00:58:00.276 --> 00:58:02.745
There's no way to eat
this without being messy.

00:58:02.745 --> 00:58:04.080
There's literally no way.

00:58:07.083 --> 00:58:08.084
Mm!

00:58:08.084 --> 00:58:10.220
Oh, my God. That's really good.

00:58:10.220 --> 00:58:12.555
Yes to all that, looks really good.

00:58:12.555 --> 00:58:15.091
Because of India's lack of beef,

00:58:15.091 --> 00:58:18.061
all the American beef options
are technically exclusives.

00:58:22.165 --> 00:58:23.399
All right.

00:58:23.399 --> 00:58:24.467
Big Mac.

00:58:24.467 --> 00:58:28.438
There it is, just brimming with stuff.

00:58:28.438 --> 00:58:30.340
My go-to for, like, 20 years.

00:58:30.340 --> 00:58:31.908
I still get it occasionally.

00:58:31.908 --> 00:58:34.844
The classic McDonald's hamburger.

00:58:34.844 --> 00:58:36.946
Beef patty, ketchup, and mustard.

00:58:36.946 --> 00:58:40.750
Of course, you can get it with cheese. Hi.

00:58:40.750 --> 00:58:44.153
You can upgrade to a double
cheeseburger or a McDouble.

00:58:44.153 --> 00:58:45.922
What's the difference, you ask?

00:58:45.922 --> 00:58:47.123
I'm not sure either.

00:58:47.123 --> 00:58:49.826
So let's start with the
double cheeseburger.

00:58:49.826 --> 00:58:51.561
Look at that. Look how yellow that is.

00:58:51.561 --> 00:58:54.430
Beef, cheese, beef, cheese, toppos.

00:58:54.430 --> 00:58:59.235
The McDouble is beef, cheese, beef.

00:58:59.235 --> 00:59:00.870
So it's just one slice of cheese

00:59:00.870 --> 00:59:02.171
in the middle, but not on top.

00:59:02.171 --> 00:59:05.008
What's the price difference?
Can we get that on-screen?

00:59:05.008 --> 00:59:06.809
And how much is a slice of cheese?

00:59:07.677 --> 00:59:09.245
Joe's hack, get yourself a McDouble

00:59:09.245 --> 00:59:11.114
and bring your own slice
of American cheese.

00:59:11.114 --> 00:59:13.983
Booyah. Save yourself
this amount of money.

00:59:13.983 --> 00:59:16.085
The problem with millennials today,

00:59:16.085 --> 00:59:18.154
the reason you guys can't buy houses is

00:59:18.154 --> 00:59:20.490
you're spending all
your money at Starbucks,

00:59:20.490 --> 00:59:22.959
you're getting your double cheeseburgers

00:59:22.959 --> 00:59:26.296
instead of a McDouble and
bringing your own cheese slice.

00:59:26.296 --> 00:59:28.364
I mean, you guys are terrible with money!

00:59:28.364 --> 00:59:29.799
You're eating, what, seven,

00:59:29.799 --> 00:59:31.401
eight McDoubles a day like me, right?

00:59:31.401 --> 00:59:35.104
And that adds up to, like,
at the end of the year, $18?

00:59:35.104 --> 00:59:38.308
10,000 years later, that's
a down payment on a house.

00:59:39.642 --> 00:59:40.843
What are you guys doing?

00:59:40.843 --> 00:59:44.981
All right, next up is the
iconic McAloo tikki burger.

00:59:44.981 --> 00:59:47.850
You take mashed potato, and
you fry it in breadcrumbs,

00:59:47.850 --> 00:59:49.919
and you get this really delicious cutlet.

00:59:49.919 --> 00:59:53.089
Here in India, they
adapted it into this burger

00:59:53.089 --> 00:59:54.958
with a very special sauce,

00:59:54.958 --> 00:59:57.293
some tomato, and chopped onions.

00:59:59.629 --> 01:00:01.898
Mm. It's just so classic.

01:00:01.898 --> 01:00:03.433
They nailed this burger.

01:00:03.433 --> 01:00:06.135
Next up, there is a Mexican McAloo tikki,

01:00:06.135 --> 01:00:09.939
which I assume has some
stereotypical Mexican ingredients

01:00:09.939 --> 01:00:12.642
and flavors like jalapeño.

01:00:12.642 --> 01:00:14.677
Yes! Jalapeño.

01:00:14.677 --> 01:00:15.878
Mm, nice.

01:00:15.878 --> 01:00:18.448
It's way more spicy. Good twist.

01:00:18.448 --> 01:00:21.417
Next up, they have a McEgg burger.

01:00:21.417 --> 01:00:23.653
McEgg. McEgg, McEgg.

01:00:23.653 --> 01:00:25.054
I don't know why I did that.

01:00:25.054 --> 01:00:26.589
Let's see what that looks like.

01:00:26.589 --> 01:00:27.991
Ugh!

01:00:27.991 --> 01:00:29.092
Sorry.

01:00:29.092 --> 01:00:31.194
I did not expect... pesto?

01:00:31.194 --> 01:00:33.563
Next up is a chicken kebab burger.

01:00:33.563 --> 01:00:36.165
Every time an Indian
fast-food chain tries to adapt

01:00:36.165 --> 01:00:39.736
an Indian special food into a burger,

01:00:39.736 --> 01:00:41.204
I take it with a pinch of salt

01:00:41.204 --> 01:00:43.272
because this is not what
we're used to seeing

01:00:43.272 --> 01:00:44.273
when we think of kebabs,

01:00:44.273 --> 01:00:47.410
but I'm going to try it,
and let's see what happens.

01:00:47.410 --> 01:00:48.711
Mm.

01:00:48.711 --> 01:00:50.346
It's very, very dry.

01:00:50.346 --> 01:00:53.316
Patty has almost a
cardboard-y taste to it.

01:00:53.316 --> 01:00:55.318
I wouldn't put those flavors together

01:00:55.318 --> 01:00:57.553
if I was thinking kebab.

01:00:57.553 --> 01:01:00.456
McCardboard tikki, maybe? No? OK.

01:01:00.456 --> 01:01:01.791
That's a bit harsh. I'm sorry.

01:01:01.791 --> 01:01:03.693
Next up is the McVeggie,

01:01:03.693 --> 01:01:07.664
which is the vegetarian
counterpart to our McChicken.

01:01:07.664 --> 01:01:10.533
If I had to eat this
versus the chicken one,

01:01:10.533 --> 01:01:12.602
I would not be upset at all.

01:01:12.602 --> 01:01:13.536
Really good.

01:01:13.536 --> 01:01:15.738
Next up, we have two "American" burgers:

01:01:15.738 --> 01:01:18.808
the American Cheese Supreme veg

01:01:18.808 --> 01:01:22.278
and the American Cheese Supreme chicken.

01:01:22.278 --> 01:01:24.080
My hunch for what makes them American

01:01:24.080 --> 01:01:27.583
is that they will have a
nice big square of cheese

01:01:27.583 --> 01:01:30.653
and they will not be spicy at all.

01:01:30.653 --> 01:01:33.823
Except they have a lot
of jalapeños on them.

01:01:33.823 --> 01:01:38.361
Joe, let me know if this
constitutes "American."

01:01:38.361 --> 01:01:39.962
That's American cheese, my man.

01:01:39.962 --> 01:01:41.364
That's what makes it American.

01:01:41.364 --> 01:01:42.899
I don't know about those
other toppings, but,

01:01:42.899 --> 01:01:43.766
yeah, it sounds about right.

01:01:43.766 --> 01:01:45.468
All right, so this is what
the McDonald's website

01:01:45.468 --> 01:01:47.503
says is in this burger.

01:01:47.503 --> 01:01:50.273
"Whole-wheat buns
sourced from Maharashtra,

01:01:50.273 --> 01:01:52.809
tangy jalapeños from Karnataka,

01:01:52.809 --> 01:01:56.212
shredded onions grown
in local Indian farms,

01:01:56.212 --> 01:02:00.583
and cheese from Amaravati, also in India."

01:02:00.583 --> 01:02:03.453
Quite close to home, this burger.

01:02:03.453 --> 01:02:06.055
Currently, this would
probably be my favorite order,

01:02:06.055 --> 01:02:08.991
a McSpicy chicken, and
there's the vegetarian option,

01:02:08.991 --> 01:02:12.762
which is a McSpicy paneer,
which is just leaking lettuce.

01:02:12.762 --> 01:02:14.363
For those of you who
don't know what paneer is,

01:02:14.363 --> 01:02:16.365
it's basically cottage cheese.

01:02:16.365 --> 01:02:17.600
We love our paneer.

01:02:17.600 --> 01:02:20.603
We put it in curries, we eat
it plain, we put it in kebabs.

01:02:20.603 --> 01:02:23.139
It is so delicious. Let's try this.

01:02:25.341 --> 01:02:27.810
Mm. It has just the right kick,

01:02:27.810 --> 01:02:29.445
and it goes really well with the paneer.

01:02:29.445 --> 01:02:31.647
Fair warning, while this
may have a light kick

01:02:31.647 --> 01:02:34.584
of spice for us, it might
be a hard kick for you.

01:02:34.584 --> 01:02:38.387
So, take everything with
a pinch of chili powder.

01:02:38.387 --> 01:02:40.957
Gonna move up to something
called the Quarter Pounder,

01:02:40.957 --> 01:02:42.592
and that's, like, their big burger.

01:02:42.592 --> 01:02:44.227
So you can get a Quarter
Pounder with cheese.

01:02:44.227 --> 01:02:45.061
Here it is.

01:02:45.061 --> 01:02:47.063
I mean, it looks fake, right?

01:02:47.063 --> 01:02:48.865
Like, "Just kidding, it's cake!"

01:02:48.865 --> 01:02:52.235
Or the new one is, "It's
actually a candle!"

01:02:52.235 --> 01:02:55.571
And then you can get a Quarter
Pounder with cheese deluxe.

01:02:55.571 --> 01:02:58.207
More veggies on it, all
the junk that I brush off.

01:02:58.207 --> 01:03:02.178
You can upgrade to a double
Quarter Pounder with cheese.

01:03:02.178 --> 01:03:05.748
Let's take a look. Oh, man.
Look how thick this is!

01:03:05.748 --> 01:03:09.485
And then you can get that
same double with bacon.

01:03:09.485 --> 01:03:10.653
Yeah!

01:03:10.653 --> 01:03:13.523
Oh, man. Skimping on the bacon. Guys!

01:03:13.523 --> 01:03:15.925
What we lack in beef
burgers we make up for

01:03:15.925 --> 01:03:18.027
in gourmet burgers.

01:03:18.027 --> 01:03:20.029
That's right. Here at McDonald's India,

01:03:20.029 --> 01:03:21.330
we have our own collection of

01:03:21.330 --> 01:03:24.534
chef's special gourmet burgers.

01:03:24.534 --> 01:03:25.501
Delicious.

01:03:25.501 --> 01:03:27.036
And I think this is a rolling menu.

01:03:27.036 --> 01:03:28.905
I think they introduce new
things from time to time.

01:03:28.905 --> 01:03:32.608
The buns themselves
look a lot more gourmet.

01:03:32.608 --> 01:03:34.644
You know, there's a nice
rift down the middle.

01:03:34.644 --> 01:03:36.612
Kind of looks like a butt, but that's OK.

01:03:36.612 --> 01:03:38.147
We're not gonna concentrate on that.

01:03:39.182 --> 01:03:41.818
First up, we have triple
cheese American veg burger

01:03:41.818 --> 01:03:44.854
and triple cheese American
chicken burger.

01:03:44.854 --> 01:03:48.691
Same thing. Cheese, jalapeño,
some sauce, lettuce,

01:03:48.691 --> 01:03:51.594
simple chicken patty, gourmet bun.

01:03:51.594 --> 01:03:53.129
Does this scream "American" to you?

01:03:53.129 --> 01:03:55.965
Next up, Cheese Lava American veg burger

01:03:55.965 --> 01:03:58.868
and Cheese Lava American chicken burger,

01:03:58.868 --> 01:04:00.136
again with American

01:04:00.136 --> 01:04:03.139
and again with the strange relation

01:04:03.139 --> 01:04:06.576
of food to volcanoes and lava.

01:04:08.077 --> 01:04:09.245
OK.

01:04:09.245 --> 01:04:11.347
This burger is very spicy.

01:04:11.347 --> 01:04:14.584
This qualifies as a
volcano product, for sure.

01:04:14.584 --> 01:04:16.452
Congratulations, McDonald's.

01:04:16.452 --> 01:04:20.022
The lava in the title
of this burger works.

01:04:20.022 --> 01:04:22.291
The McSpicy chicken premium, though,

01:04:22.291 --> 01:04:25.361
has an egg patty inside of it.

01:04:25.361 --> 01:04:27.697
Mm-mm.

01:04:27.697 --> 01:04:30.366
Mm, that's pretty good.

01:04:30.366 --> 01:04:32.501
I just feel so existential right now.

01:04:33.436 --> 01:04:35.037
Imagine sitting here at this table

01:04:35.037 --> 01:04:38.741
and just tasting every single
burger on a McDonald's menu.

01:04:39.909 --> 01:04:41.544
Amazing.

01:04:41.544 --> 01:04:43.479
But also, s---.

01:04:43.479 --> 01:04:45.681
We also have some exclusive wrap options.

01:04:45.681 --> 01:04:49.051
We have Big Spicy paneer
and Big Spicy chicken.

01:04:49.051 --> 01:04:52.655
I think this is the same
McSpicy chicken patty,

01:04:52.655 --> 01:04:55.224
and it's wrapped around a tortilla,

01:04:55.224 --> 01:04:57.493
which is actually way
closer to an Indian chapati

01:04:57.493 --> 01:04:59.061
than most other fast-food restaurants.

01:04:59.061 --> 01:05:01.430
It doesn't feel as synthetic.

01:05:01.430 --> 01:05:03.566
Our McDonald's in the US

01:05:03.566 --> 01:05:06.202
had wraps for a brief period of time.

01:05:06.202 --> 01:05:09.171
One day they were gone. Nobody noticed.

01:05:09.171 --> 01:05:11.207
Yeah, you guys got some chicken
stuff that we don't have,

01:05:11.207 --> 01:05:12.541
but we got a few of our own.

01:05:12.541 --> 01:05:14.277
More recently than you think,

01:05:14.277 --> 01:05:16.946
they finally introduced
their chicken sandwich

01:05:16.946 --> 01:05:20.816
to an already-crowded
chicken-sandwich market,

01:05:20.816 --> 01:05:23.152
and that is of course their
crispy chicken sandwich,

01:05:23.152 --> 01:05:26.088
and this thing is fantastic.

01:05:26.088 --> 01:05:27.490
It's one of the best ones.

01:05:27.490 --> 01:05:28.724
They were late to the game,

01:05:28.724 --> 01:05:30.359
and they kind of took
it over, in my opinion.

01:05:30.359 --> 01:05:32.795
And what I like about it,
it's simple. Look at this.

01:05:32.795 --> 01:05:35.965
You just got crispy
chicken, pickles that suck.

01:05:35.965 --> 01:05:37.400
It's baller. It tastes great.

01:05:37.400 --> 01:05:39.235
Like it a little spicy, India?

01:05:39.235 --> 01:05:40.369
It probably doesn't
compare to what you guys

01:05:40.369 --> 01:05:42.104
are rocking in India but, you know,

01:05:42.104 --> 01:05:44.340
this one has a little nice heat to it.

01:05:44.340 --> 01:05:45.641
Pickles, sauce.

01:05:45.641 --> 01:05:47.310
Want to take it up a notch?

01:05:47.310 --> 01:05:48.678
Gotta go deluxe.

01:05:48.678 --> 01:05:51.180
The cool crispness of the vegetables

01:05:51.180 --> 01:05:54.483
just clash so well with the spicy sauce.

01:05:54.483 --> 01:05:56.152
It's good. It's good.

01:05:56.152 --> 01:05:57.753
Nikhil, say the word,

01:05:57.753 --> 01:05:59.855
and I'm putting one in
the post for you tomorrow.

01:05:59.855 --> 01:06:01.290
So when it arrives in three weeks,

01:06:01.290 --> 01:06:03.092
you can throw it out.

01:06:03.092 --> 01:06:05.594
Now we're getting into
exclusive side dishes.

01:06:05.594 --> 01:06:08.364
Here in India, we have these add-ons.

01:06:08.364 --> 01:06:11.767
No. 1, the veg pizza McPuff.

01:06:11.767 --> 01:06:14.603
This is one of the most
delicious things we have here.

01:06:14.603 --> 01:06:16.772
It's basically a pizza Hot Pocket.

01:06:16.772 --> 01:06:19.108
Masala wedges. These are potato wedges

01:06:19.108 --> 01:06:22.912
with classic Indian masala flavor to them.

01:06:22.912 --> 01:06:24.080
Ooh, boy.

01:06:24.080 --> 01:06:25.948
Masalas are basically what we use

01:06:25.948 --> 01:06:28.017
to spice and flavor dishes,

01:06:28.017 --> 01:06:30.386
and they consist primarily
of ground-up spices

01:06:30.386 --> 01:06:32.521
like cardamom, cloves,

01:06:32.521 --> 01:06:34.390
red chilies, Kashmiri chilies.

01:06:34.390 --> 01:06:36.792
You go to every Indian home, the mums,

01:06:36.792 --> 01:06:39.462
the grandmums will have
their own random, you know,

01:06:39.462 --> 01:06:43.265
masala mix that they
use and that's guarded

01:06:43.265 --> 01:06:46.068
and treasured in their family, forever.

01:06:46.068 --> 01:06:48.337
Next up, we have cheesy masala wedges.

01:06:48.337 --> 01:06:52.475
They're also serving a
classic cup of boiled corn,

01:06:52.475 --> 01:06:56.912
which is so unique, and they
give you a side of Amul butter.

01:06:56.912 --> 01:06:59.849
Guys, Amul butter is part of our culture.

01:06:59.849 --> 01:07:02.785
Makhan. Makhan!

01:07:02.785 --> 01:07:03.686
This is probably going to be

01:07:03.686 --> 01:07:05.454
the most delicious bite of the day.

01:07:08.924 --> 01:07:10.126
I love corn.

01:07:10.126 --> 01:07:11.494
Next up, chicken strips.

01:07:11.494 --> 01:07:15.498
They come in packs of two, three, or five.

01:07:15.498 --> 01:07:18.467
Cheesy nugget veg bites.

01:07:18.467 --> 01:07:20.002
Yeah, this is just a vegetarian version

01:07:20.002 --> 01:07:20.903
of the chicken nuggets,

01:07:20.903 --> 01:07:23.272
and it's got some corn, some tomato.

01:07:24.473 --> 01:07:25.941
Mm, it's OK.

01:07:25.941 --> 01:07:29.779
Next, we have the double cheese McMuffin.

01:07:29.779 --> 01:07:33.682
And lastly, we have Mexican cheesy fries.

01:07:33.682 --> 01:07:35.351
On the McDonald's India website,

01:07:35.351 --> 01:07:37.486
one British customer said

01:07:37.486 --> 01:07:40.923
that these Mexican cheesy
fries are "the real deal."

01:07:40.923 --> 01:07:43.859
I have no idea how a
British person can say

01:07:43.859 --> 01:07:45.694
that Mexican cheesy
fries are the real deal,

01:07:45.694 --> 01:07:47.830
but anytime a British person says

01:07:47.830 --> 01:07:50.633
that another culture's
food is "the real deal,"

01:07:50.633 --> 01:07:54.603
it puts a little fear in
our small Indian hearts.

01:07:54.603 --> 01:07:56.072
Yeah those fries look like ass.

01:07:56.072 --> 01:08:00.509
And the next exclusive side
that we have is apple slices.

01:08:02.144 --> 01:08:04.747
Cut 'em up, put 'em in a plastic bag.

01:08:04.747 --> 01:08:07.716
'Bout to get saucy. That's
right, ladies and gentlemen.

01:08:10.920 --> 01:08:13.189
Sauce talk.

01:08:13.189 --> 01:08:14.256
Thank you.

01:08:15.357 --> 01:08:16.325
Spicy Buffalo.

01:08:17.860 --> 01:08:18.894
Not that good.

01:08:18.894 --> 01:08:20.863
We got a tangy barbecue.

01:08:21.797 --> 01:08:22.631
Ooh.

01:08:24.100 --> 01:08:25.000
Much better.

01:08:25.000 --> 01:08:26.936
Mm. Honey mustard.

01:08:29.438 --> 01:08:30.639
Tastes like salad dressing.

01:08:30.639 --> 01:08:31.740
Sweet and sour.

01:08:33.542 --> 01:08:34.844
I would tie it with the tangy barbecue

01:08:34.844 --> 01:08:37.213
because it's so different,
so we'll keep these guys

01:08:37.213 --> 01:08:38.314
same tier.

01:08:38.314 --> 01:08:41.383
Ranch, I don't know.
America, we love our ranch.

01:08:41.383 --> 01:08:42.351
Ranch is just OK.

01:08:42.351 --> 01:08:44.720
That's right, I said it. Ranch is just OK.

01:08:44.720 --> 01:08:48.324
Oh, and all ranch tastes the same. Yeah.

01:08:48.324 --> 01:08:49.925
And finally, honey.

01:08:52.094 --> 01:08:53.395
How do you like that?

01:08:53.395 --> 01:08:54.830
Honey's the best one.

01:08:54.830 --> 01:08:57.133
And all that money, all that energy,

01:08:57.133 --> 01:08:59.635
all that time creating all these recipes,

01:08:59.635 --> 01:09:02.905
trying to sway the American mind,

01:09:02.905 --> 01:09:06.742
and you got beat by a bunch of bees.

01:09:06.742 --> 01:09:08.878
Power to the bees!

01:09:08.878 --> 01:09:11.080
We have one exclusive spice mix

01:09:11.080 --> 01:09:13.249
as well as one exclusive
sauce here in India.

01:09:13.249 --> 01:09:15.351
We have chili sauce, which
is pretty straightforward.

01:09:15.351 --> 01:09:16.452
It's chili sauce.

01:09:16.452 --> 01:09:18.487
But let me tell you about

01:09:18.487 --> 01:09:21.657
peri-peri spice mix.

01:09:21.657 --> 01:09:25.828
So, McDonald's launched
this in 2013 here in India,

01:09:25.828 --> 01:09:28.531
and it was so popular, there were riots

01:09:28.531 --> 01:09:29.932
when they said they were
going to discontinue it.

01:09:29.932 --> 01:09:33.636
And so now, it's a permanent
addition to the menu.

01:09:33.636 --> 01:09:35.871
First, you get this shake bag,

01:09:35.871 --> 01:09:37.907
then you grab your fries,

01:09:37.907 --> 01:09:40.109
and then you just pour that in there.

01:09:40.109 --> 01:09:40.976
Ah.

01:09:47.816 --> 01:09:49.985
Boom! Oh, boy.

01:09:49.985 --> 01:09:52.087
Can we cut to a before of the fries?

01:09:52.087 --> 01:09:55.691
You saw how they were. Now look at these.

01:09:55.691 --> 01:09:58.194
You can see the little flecks of spice

01:09:58.194 --> 01:10:00.229
just adorning each fry.

01:10:07.570 --> 01:10:08.938
Hello, it's Crystelle.

01:10:08.938 --> 01:10:11.941
And I know Nikhil has
peri-peri McDonald's chips,

01:10:11.941 --> 01:10:14.577
but in the UK, it is all about Nando's.

01:10:14.577 --> 01:10:15.878
Cheeky Nando's.

01:10:15.878 --> 01:10:17.580
Let's talk about peri-peri.

01:10:17.580 --> 01:10:20.249
Peri means pepper. And
it's a blend of spices,

01:10:20.249 --> 01:10:23.552
so it's got things like paprika,
ground bird's eye chili,

01:10:23.552 --> 01:10:25.988
a bit of oregano, a pinch
of ginger and cardamom,

01:10:25.988 --> 01:10:27.656
but it's a Portuguese spice blend.

01:10:27.656 --> 01:10:29.725
It's funny because
obviously Nikhil mentioned

01:10:29.725 --> 01:10:32.161
that the peri-peri fries
just blew off in India,

01:10:32.161 --> 01:10:34.430
and it makes sense, because I'm from Goa,

01:10:34.430 --> 01:10:35.931
which is in the south of India.

01:10:35.931 --> 01:10:38.200
Goa was colonized by the Portuguese.

01:10:38.200 --> 01:10:40.069
And so I really think that Indians

01:10:40.069 --> 01:10:42.004
are accustomed to that
Portuguese taste palate,

01:10:42.004 --> 01:10:45.841
which is why peri-peri fries
are doing so well in India.

01:10:45.841 --> 01:10:47.109
But enough of the talking.

01:10:47.109 --> 01:10:49.645
I want to dig into these
fries, because they look great.

01:10:49.645 --> 01:10:51.680
Mm. Oh, this is so good.

01:10:51.680 --> 01:10:53.182
Harry, get involved.

01:10:53.182 --> 01:10:54.216
You're not eating chips
without me, are you?

01:10:54.216 --> 01:10:56.185
Oh, sorry, I've already had a head start.

01:10:56.185 --> 01:10:57.486
Harry: Cheers.
Crystelle: Cheers.

01:10:58.487 --> 01:11:02.391
God damn, if that isn't like crack.

01:11:02.391 --> 01:11:03.359
For the early risers,

01:11:03.359 --> 01:11:05.661
there's plenty of
exclusive breakfast items

01:11:05.661 --> 01:11:06.996
at the US McDonald's.

01:11:06.996 --> 01:11:09.064
Sausage biscuit with egg.

01:11:09.064 --> 01:11:10.566
Next one,

01:11:10.566 --> 01:11:11.767
sausage biscuit.

01:11:11.767 --> 01:11:14.403
I mean, they take the
egg out, so it's just ...

01:11:14.403 --> 01:11:17.806
This, of course, is
bacon, egg, and cheese.

01:11:17.806 --> 01:11:18.807
Ladies and gentlemen,

01:11:18.807 --> 01:11:20.376
we've reached the point of the breakfast

01:11:20.376 --> 01:11:21.977
where we get into the McGriddles.

01:11:21.977 --> 01:11:23.045
I love McGriddles.

01:11:23.045 --> 01:11:25.648
What's a McGriddle, you ask,
India? Fantastic question.

01:11:25.648 --> 01:11:28.417
McDonald's had this genius idea

01:11:28.417 --> 01:11:31.186
to replace the breakfast
sandwiches they already had

01:11:31.186 --> 01:11:32.821
with pancakes.

01:11:32.821 --> 01:11:36.892
And they also, like, inject
syrup into it somehow?

01:11:36.892 --> 01:11:40.863
But it is a breakfast sandwich
with pancakes for buns,

01:11:40.863 --> 01:11:45.234
and it's the best idea anyone's
ever had, anywhere, ever.

01:11:45.234 --> 01:11:48.771
[Joe laughing]

01:11:48.771 --> 01:11:50.372
Look at this! Look at this, look at this.

01:11:50.372 --> 01:11:52.308
They've even got a little M on there.

01:11:52.308 --> 01:11:53.475
This mini pancake.

01:11:53.475 --> 01:11:55.477
I know I'm wearing the
gloves, but this one's mine.

01:11:56.945 --> 01:11:57.813
Mm.

01:11:57.813 --> 01:12:01.784
We have a veg McMuffin
and a sausage McMuffin.

01:12:03.285 --> 01:12:04.119
Mm.

01:12:04.119 --> 01:12:06.755
The sausage here in India
is not made out of pork,

01:12:06.755 --> 01:12:08.090
like it is in the US.

01:12:08.090 --> 01:12:10.592
Instead, it's made out of simple chicken.

01:12:10.592 --> 01:12:14.096
Speaking of sausage, you
can get a breakfast burrito.

01:12:15.597 --> 01:12:18.367
Bro, I could put five of
these away, easy. Easy.

01:12:18.367 --> 01:12:20.436
If you're, like, a total drag

01:12:20.436 --> 01:12:23.138
and you want oatmeal in
the morning, we have it.

01:12:23.138 --> 01:12:25.507
It's about as inspiring
as you would think.

01:12:25.507 --> 01:12:27.076
Hotcakes and sausage.

01:12:27.076 --> 01:12:29.311
Of course, it comes with hot syrup.

01:12:29.311 --> 01:12:30.346
This here,

01:12:31.580 --> 01:12:33.682
the big breakfast with hotcakes.

01:12:33.682 --> 01:12:34.717
And it's big.

01:12:34.717 --> 01:12:37.553
A lot of eggs, kind of
wimpy-looking bacon,

01:12:37.553 --> 01:12:40.356
got yourself two English muffins here.

01:12:40.356 --> 01:12:43.359
And, of course, comes with a hash brown.

01:12:43.359 --> 01:12:45.327
Potatoes. Who doesn't love 'em?

01:12:45.327 --> 01:12:47.463
McDonald's hash brown, undefeated.

01:12:47.463 --> 01:12:48.430
These things are so good.

01:12:48.430 --> 01:12:50.232
India exclusive desserts.

01:12:50.232 --> 01:12:53.235
We have a Black Forest McFlurry,

01:12:53.235 --> 01:12:55.104
a vanilla chocolate muffin,

01:12:55.104 --> 01:12:57.539
and a chocolate chip muffin.

01:12:57.539 --> 01:13:00.542
It's kind of like a
McFlurry soup right now.

01:13:02.344 --> 01:13:05.881
This would be really good when
it was actually a McFlurry.

01:13:05.881 --> 01:13:08.283
Desserts! USA, we got 'em.

01:13:08.283 --> 01:13:09.918
So, starting down here, very simple,

01:13:09.918 --> 01:13:11.754
chocolate chip cookies.

01:13:11.754 --> 01:13:13.622
This next thing, apple fritter, right?

01:13:14.823 --> 01:13:15.924
Mm.

01:13:15.924 --> 01:13:19.128
This right here is called a
glazed pull-apart doughnut.

01:13:19.128 --> 01:13:20.262
Blueberry muffin.

01:13:20.262 --> 01:13:21.497
If you've had one, you've had them all.

01:13:21.497 --> 01:13:22.765
This is a what type of pie?

01:13:22.831 --> 01:13:24.400
Anders: A guava and cream pie.

01:13:24.400 --> 01:13:25.801
Let's see what's inside.

01:13:25.801 --> 01:13:29.037
OK. I'm suddenly more interested. Yeah!

01:13:29.037 --> 01:13:31.039
Guava and cream.

01:13:31.039 --> 01:13:33.642
How about we'll call it
the cream and guava pie?

01:13:33.642 --> 01:13:34.777
Nah, this sucks.

01:13:34.777 --> 01:13:36.245
[Anders laughing]

01:13:37.079 --> 01:13:38.080
I don't f--- with it.

01:13:38.080 --> 01:13:40.783
Standard menu item, the
McDonald's apple pie.

01:13:40.783 --> 01:13:41.617
Everyone knows about this.

01:13:41.617 --> 01:13:43.952
I don't want a pizza version of this.

01:13:43.952 --> 01:13:46.989
Eh! And last but not least, cinnamon roll.

01:13:46.989 --> 01:13:48.257
Too sticky. I don't feel like eating it.

01:13:52.327 --> 01:13:53.962
Update: It's not sticky.

01:13:53.962 --> 01:13:56.365
It's actually [knocks on cinnamon roll].

01:13:56.365 --> 01:13:58.667
Exclusive drinks, starting with,

01:13:58.667 --> 01:14:00.302
we have something called

01:14:00.302 --> 01:14:03.806
B Natural's mixed fruit juice.

01:14:03.806 --> 01:14:04.973
Next up, we have something

01:14:04.973 --> 01:14:09.011
that they call raw mango fruit splash.

01:14:09.011 --> 01:14:10.179
Oh!

01:14:10.179 --> 01:14:11.680
It's a bit too sweet.

01:14:11.680 --> 01:14:13.782
Berry lemonade splash.

01:14:13.782 --> 01:14:17.453
All of these come in these very unique

01:14:17.453 --> 01:14:19.822
reusable bottles, apparently.

01:14:19.822 --> 01:14:23.992
Next up, strawberry chiller,
green apple chiller,

01:14:23.992 --> 01:14:26.962
and lemon chiller.

01:14:28.130 --> 01:14:30.532
It's just flavored water.
That's exactly what it is.

01:14:30.532 --> 01:14:33.068
It's flavored water,
and I kind of like it.

01:14:33.068 --> 01:14:35.604
This is a mixed berry smoothie.

01:14:37.639 --> 01:14:39.541
It's still quite sweet, but quite good.

01:14:39.541 --> 01:14:42.144
Next up, American mud pie shake.

01:14:43.612 --> 01:14:46.315
Mm. That's pretty yum.

01:14:46.315 --> 01:14:47.783
Drink roulette.

01:14:47.783 --> 01:14:50.052
Ooh, and the ice melted. Fantastic.

01:14:50.052 --> 01:14:52.754
Dr. Pepper. Let's go!

01:14:52.754 --> 01:14:55.524
Coke, nonexclusive. Let's go.

01:14:55.524 --> 01:14:57.025
Sweet tea, too sweet.

01:14:58.494 --> 01:15:00.729
Ugh, yeah. Unsweetened
tea, not sweet enough.

01:15:00.729 --> 01:15:01.797
You guys combine.

01:15:01.797 --> 01:15:04.266
For the kids watching,
why are you watching?

01:15:04.266 --> 01:15:06.101
Where are your parents or supervisors?

01:15:06.101 --> 01:15:08.804
You can get yourself apple juice, milk.

01:15:08.804 --> 01:15:10.272
Come on, you're drinking milk?

01:15:10.272 --> 01:15:11.540
The thought of drinking straight milk,

01:15:11.540 --> 01:15:12.741
like, hurts my stomach.

01:15:12.741 --> 01:15:14.243
There's also chocolate milk on the menu.

01:15:14.243 --> 01:15:15.210
Once upon a time,

01:15:15.210 --> 01:15:18.180
this was an iced French vanilla latte.

01:15:18.180 --> 01:15:21.250
Now it's more of a room-temperature
French vanilla latte.

01:15:23.085 --> 01:15:25.220
That's just OK. It's, like, really sweet.

01:15:25.220 --> 01:15:26.822
Strawberry banana smoothie.

01:15:27.890 --> 01:15:29.358
Yeah, I always loved getting these.

01:15:29.358 --> 01:15:30.459
These are good.

01:15:30.459 --> 01:15:32.561
So I'm going to assume
they're not good for me.

01:15:32.561 --> 01:15:33.996
Exclusive hot drinks.

01:15:33.996 --> 01:15:36.565
First off, we have strawberry green tea.

01:15:36.565 --> 01:15:39.301
Next up, English breakfast tea

01:15:39.301 --> 01:15:41.603
and Moroccan tea.

01:15:41.603 --> 01:15:44.039
Next up, a flat white coffee.

01:15:44.039 --> 01:15:47.476
India, a land where we run on chai,

01:15:47.476 --> 01:15:50.379
and McDonald's does
not have a chai option.

01:15:50.379 --> 01:15:52.080
Caramel macchiato,

01:15:52.080 --> 01:15:54.016
cappuccino,

01:15:54.016 --> 01:15:55.217
caramel latte,

01:15:55.217 --> 01:15:56.285
a vanilla cappuccino.

01:15:56.285 --> 01:15:58.320
The V does look like a U.

01:15:58.320 --> 01:16:01.523
McDonald's premium roast coffee.

01:16:03.458 --> 01:16:04.660
I'm going to hang on to this one.

01:16:06.995 --> 01:16:10.566
In India, a chicken Maharaja
Mac will cost you 231 rupees

01:16:10.566 --> 01:16:11.733
for just the sandwich.

01:16:11.733 --> 01:16:14.403
That's around $3.03.

01:16:14.403 --> 01:16:16.471
We do not have the chicken Maharaja Mac,

01:16:16.471 --> 01:16:18.140
but we do have the Big Mac,

01:16:18.140 --> 01:16:21.443
and a Big Mac in the US costs $4.89.

01:16:21.443 --> 01:16:24.446
That is a 61% price increase.

01:16:24.446 --> 01:16:26.515
Now, what if you turn this into a meal?

01:16:26.515 --> 01:16:29.618
A McSaver Maharaja Mac combo
comes with regular fries

01:16:29.618 --> 01:16:33.655
and a regular drink and
will cost you 356 rupees.

01:16:33.655 --> 01:16:37.025
That is $4.67, still less than the price

01:16:37.025 --> 01:16:39.027
of the American sandwich on its own.

01:16:39.027 --> 01:16:41.430
But does the combo meal
make a difference in the US?

01:16:41.430 --> 01:16:42.698
A medium Big Mac combo,

01:16:42.698 --> 01:16:45.667
so Big Mac, medium fries, medium drink,

01:16:45.667 --> 01:16:47.903
is $8.99.

01:16:47.903 --> 01:16:51.206
That's a 92% cost increase,

01:16:51.206 --> 01:16:53.842
even worse than if you just
bought the sandwich on its own.

01:16:53.842 --> 01:16:55.477
On the Indian McDonald's menu,

01:16:55.477 --> 01:16:56.878
you'll find a two-person meal,

01:16:56.878 --> 01:17:00.115
which contains a chicken
Maharaja Mac, a veg Maharaja Mac,

01:17:00.115 --> 01:17:04.086
large fries, two pizza
McPuffs, and a drink.

01:17:04.086 --> 01:17:08.724
All of this will cost
you 681 rupees, or $8.93.

01:17:08.724 --> 01:17:10.792
So, basically, you're
getting food for two people

01:17:10.792 --> 01:17:13.629
for the price of one
person's meal in the US.

01:17:13.629 --> 01:17:15.430
However, while it seems a lot cheaper

01:17:15.430 --> 01:17:17.299
than the food in the US,

01:17:17.299 --> 01:17:18.867
it's still very expensive

01:17:18.867 --> 01:17:21.236
and aspirational to people over here.

01:17:21.236 --> 01:17:23.305
Your minimum wage per hour

01:17:23.305 --> 01:17:25.641
is equal to our daily minimum wage.

01:17:25.641 --> 01:17:26.742
And so, yeah,

01:17:26.742 --> 01:17:28.910
a lot of people can't really
afford this kind of food.

01:17:28.910 --> 01:17:30.545
The English-speaking Indians that you see

01:17:30.545 --> 01:17:33.281
in a lot of YouTube videos on the internet

01:17:33.281 --> 01:17:34.716
aren't really a proper reflection

01:17:34.716 --> 01:17:36.752
of the majority of people
that live in this country,

01:17:36.752 --> 01:17:38.854
who still can't afford food like this.

01:17:38.854 --> 01:17:41.123
So, I'm checking my privilege,

01:17:41.123 --> 01:17:42.991
and we should all make sure we check ours.

01:17:42.991 --> 01:17:44.593
But let's play devil's advocate.

01:17:44.593 --> 01:17:46.895
McDonald's India has definitely included

01:17:46.895 --> 01:17:49.398
a lot more affordable
options on their menu.

01:17:49.398 --> 01:17:51.700
And so they are more approachable

01:17:51.700 --> 01:17:54.903
to the average urban Indian
than other fast-food chains.

01:17:58.373 --> 01:17:59.408
Let's compare some items

01:17:59.408 --> 01:18:02.778
to see who has the least
healthy McDonald's food.

01:18:02.778 --> 01:18:06.381
In the US, a McChicken
contains 400 calories,

01:18:06.381 --> 01:18:09.718
21 grams of fat, 39 grams of carbs.

01:18:09.718 --> 01:18:11.253
5 of those are sugar,

01:18:11.253 --> 01:18:13.622
and 560 milligrams of sodium.

01:18:13.622 --> 01:18:15.157
How about the Indian McChicken?

01:18:15.157 --> 01:18:18.060
One of these contains 398 calories,

01:18:18.060 --> 01:18:20.595
15 grams of total fat, 48 grams of carbs,

01:18:20.595 --> 01:18:22.731
5 grams of which are sugars,

01:18:22.731 --> 01:18:25.734
787 milligrams of sodium.

01:18:25.734 --> 01:18:29.371
So the Indian version has
slightly fewer calories,

01:18:29.371 --> 01:18:33.442
way lesser fats, but much
more carbs and sodium.

01:18:33.442 --> 01:18:34.743
What if we made that a combo meal?

01:18:34.743 --> 01:18:37.612
Well, a medium fry in the
US contains the following:

01:18:37.612 --> 01:18:40.515
320 calories, 15 grams of total fat,

01:18:40.515 --> 01:18:42.918
43 grams of carbs, no sugar,

01:18:42.918 --> 01:18:45.087
and 260 milligrams of sodium.

01:18:45.087 --> 01:18:48.790
While a medium fries in
India contains 340 calories,

01:18:48.790 --> 01:18:51.993
17 grams of total fat, 41 grams of carbs,

01:18:51.993 --> 01:18:53.495
0 grams of sugars,

01:18:53.495 --> 01:18:56.798
and 256 milligrams of sodium.

01:18:56.798 --> 01:18:59.367
And if we add the medium Coke,

01:18:59.367 --> 01:19:02.838
that is adding 210 calories, no fat,

01:19:02.838 --> 01:19:05.741
56 grams of carbs, 56 of those are sugar,

01:19:05.741 --> 01:19:08.009
and 55 milligrams of sodium.

01:19:08.009 --> 01:19:09.811
Ooh, a nice salty Coke.

01:19:09.811 --> 01:19:11.279
We'll do the same. Here in India,

01:19:11.279 --> 01:19:14.783
one medium Coke will
cost you 151 calories,

01:19:14.783 --> 01:19:17.452
0 grams of fat, 38 grams of carbs,

01:19:17.452 --> 01:19:19.921
38 grams of which are sugars,

01:19:19.921 --> 01:19:22.791
and there are 0 grams
of sodium, but my God,

01:19:22.791 --> 01:19:25.827
that is a lot of sugar packed in this cup.

01:19:25.827 --> 01:19:27.929
That leaves the Indian
meal at a grand total

01:19:27.929 --> 01:19:31.366
of 889 calories, 32 grams of fat,

01:19:31.366 --> 01:19:33.201
127 grams of carbs,

01:19:33.201 --> 01:19:35.036
out of which 43 grams are sugars,

01:19:35.036 --> 01:19:39.674
and 1,043 milligrams of sodium.

01:19:39.674 --> 01:19:40.575
Sheesh.

01:19:40.575 --> 01:19:43.411
Which means this whole bad boy altogether

01:19:43.411 --> 01:19:45.447
is 930 calories,

01:19:45.447 --> 01:19:46.982
36 grams of total fat,

01:19:46.982 --> 01:19:48.450
138 grams of carbs,

01:19:48.450 --> 01:19:50.652
61 of those grams are sugar,

01:19:50.652 --> 01:19:53.455
875 milligrams of sodium.

01:19:53.455 --> 01:19:56.258
Little bit lower sodium than India,

01:19:56.258 --> 01:20:00.562
but we got you guys beat in
calorie, fats, carbs, and sugar.

01:20:00.562 --> 01:20:04.699
Mm, mm, mm, mm! We win. We win.

01:20:04.699 --> 01:20:05.801
Ah!

01:20:05.801 --> 01:20:06.768
Unfortunately for India,

01:20:06.768 --> 01:20:08.503
the combo stats are a little misleading,

01:20:08.503 --> 01:20:10.572
and the difference maker is the Coke,

01:20:10.572 --> 01:20:13.408
because the American meal
has a larger portion.

01:20:13.408 --> 01:20:16.211
If you order the Coke
Zero in both countries,

01:20:16.211 --> 01:20:19.181
the Indian meal will actually
have a higher calorie count.

01:20:21.650 --> 01:20:23.685
McDonald's India does
not share a full list

01:20:23.685 --> 01:20:24.886
of their ingredients,

01:20:24.886 --> 01:20:27.823
but there are some things
we do know about their food.

01:20:27.823 --> 01:20:29.057
Like, did you know that McDonald's India

01:20:29.057 --> 01:20:31.226
actually changed Indian farming practices

01:20:31.226 --> 01:20:33.929
just so they could grow the
kind of potato that they wanted?

01:20:33.929 --> 01:20:36.264
When they first launched in India in 1996,

01:20:36.264 --> 01:20:37.699
McDonald's promised the government

01:20:37.699 --> 01:20:39.367
that they would use products grown

01:20:39.367 --> 01:20:41.303
and sourced right here in India.

01:20:41.303 --> 01:20:43.338
But people who had eaten McDonald's abroad

01:20:43.338 --> 01:20:46.374
realized that the fries
didn't taste quite the same.

01:20:46.374 --> 01:20:48.043
The reason for this is
that Indian potatoes

01:20:48.043 --> 01:20:49.411
were too small, round,

01:20:49.411 --> 01:20:51.980
had way too much moisture
and sugar content.

01:20:51.980 --> 01:20:55.150
And so the fries made out of
them were not long enough,

01:20:55.150 --> 01:20:57.485
they didn't get crispy
enough, and they didn't have

01:20:57.485 --> 01:21:00.455
that distinctive McDonald's oomph to them.

01:21:00.455 --> 01:21:02.958
So, McDonald's partnered
with McCain Foods,

01:21:02.958 --> 01:21:06.661
and they spent nine years
trying to perfect their potato.

01:21:06.661 --> 01:21:09.464
They imported saplings
which had the perfect shape

01:21:09.464 --> 01:21:11.233
and starch content that they needed.

01:21:11.233 --> 01:21:13.435
They also chose Gujarat
as their farming location

01:21:13.435 --> 01:21:14.903
for its climate, and they switched

01:21:14.903 --> 01:21:17.806
from a flood irrigation
to a sprinkler system

01:21:17.806 --> 01:21:20.442
to reduce moisture content and save water.

01:21:20.442 --> 01:21:23.578
The result: bigger and
more starchy potatoes

01:21:23.578 --> 01:21:25.547
that can be used to make
the McDonald's fries

01:21:25.547 --> 01:21:27.315
that you know and love.

01:21:27.315 --> 01:21:30.552
McDonald's in the US
mostly uses russet Burbank

01:21:30.552 --> 01:21:34.089
or Shepody, "shep-a-tee," potatoes.

01:21:34.089 --> 01:21:35.724
Potato me.

01:21:35.724 --> 01:21:40.262
So, these are big enough that
the distinctive long fry,

01:21:40.262 --> 01:21:42.931
yeah, look how long this is. Wow!

01:21:42.931 --> 01:21:46.001
Known to be low moisture
and low sugar content.

01:21:46.001 --> 01:21:48.370
This means they can
remain crispy when fried

01:21:48.370 --> 01:21:49.938
and don't caramelize too fast,

01:21:49.938 --> 01:21:52.574
so you can get a nice, even browning.

01:21:52.574 --> 01:21:54.809
McDonald's in the US actually discloses

01:21:54.809 --> 01:21:55.844
all of its ingredients,

01:21:55.844 --> 01:21:58.113
so we can figure out a
few other differences.

01:21:58.113 --> 01:21:59.381
In the US, for instance,

01:21:59.381 --> 01:22:01.683
our mayonnaise contains egg yolk,

01:22:01.683 --> 01:22:03.618
as does most American mayo.

01:22:03.618 --> 01:22:06.421
Thanks to the FAQ page on
the McDonald's India website,

01:22:06.421 --> 01:22:08.790
we found out that the
mayonnaise is eggless,

01:22:08.790 --> 01:22:10.158
along with all of the other sauces

01:22:10.158 --> 01:22:11.826
except for the tartar sauce.

01:22:11.826 --> 01:22:14.529
When people describe things
as vegetarian here in India,

01:22:14.529 --> 01:22:17.098
they typically mean it
doesn't contain egg.

01:22:17.232 --> 01:22:19.200
Joe: From calorie count to portion sizes,

01:22:19.200 --> 01:22:21.102
we wanted to find out all the differences

01:22:21.102 --> 01:22:23.905
between Domino's in India and the US.

01:22:23.905 --> 01:22:25.740
This is "Food Wars."

01:22:28.944 --> 01:22:32.414
Here in India, our Domino's
pizzas come in three sizes.

01:22:32.414 --> 01:22:35.083
Our Domino's pizza comes in four sizes.

01:22:35.083 --> 01:22:38.086
Nikhil: The small, 8
inches with four slices.

01:22:38.086 --> 01:22:41.389
Joe: The small, 10-inch,
which is six slices.

01:22:41.389 --> 01:22:43.858
The medium, 10 inches with six slices.

01:22:43.858 --> 01:22:47.696
Joe: The medium, 12 inches,
which is eight slices.

01:22:47.696 --> 01:22:51.733
And the large, 12 inches
with eight slices.

01:22:51.733 --> 01:22:54.336
Joe: The large, 14-inch, which is,

01:22:54.336 --> 01:22:56.471
I don't know, four, eight, nine,

01:22:56.471 --> 01:22:59.207
16 slices, 'cause I don't
know why they cut it this way.

01:22:59.207 --> 01:23:00.775
I didn't ask them to, so.

01:23:00.775 --> 01:23:02.010
And the extra large,

01:23:02.010 --> 01:23:05.613
16 inches, or six slices.

01:23:08.650 --> 01:23:11.086
Unfortunately, our large margherita pizza

01:23:11.086 --> 01:23:14.089
only comes in one crust option,
which is the hand-tossed.

01:23:14.089 --> 01:23:15.323
You don't get it in pan

01:23:15.323 --> 01:23:17.158
or in cheese burst or any other kind.

01:23:17.158 --> 01:23:19.227
So I am going to weigh one slice

01:23:19.227 --> 01:23:21.162
of large margherita hand-tossed pizza

01:23:21.162 --> 01:23:23.298
to see how much it weighs.

01:23:23.298 --> 01:23:25.133
93 grams.

01:23:25.133 --> 01:23:27.836
And I will weigh a
slice of our hand-tossed

01:23:27.836 --> 01:23:30.438
and our pan to compare the weight.

01:23:30.438 --> 01:23:33.408
Please note that our mediums

01:23:33.408 --> 01:23:36.878
are the same size as their larges.

01:23:36.878 --> 01:23:38.947
That's pretty insane.

01:23:38.947 --> 01:23:41.483
Yeah, I'm not surprised
by that at all, buddy.

01:23:41.483 --> 01:23:42.917
Hand-tossed.

01:23:42.917 --> 01:23:45.620
One random slice is

01:23:45.620 --> 01:23:47.055
79 grams.

01:23:47.055 --> 01:23:50.191
A slice of pan,

01:23:50.191 --> 01:23:53.161
same surface size, we'll say,

01:23:53.161 --> 01:23:54.295
but obviously a lot thicker,

01:23:54.295 --> 01:23:55.830
like, way, I mean, come on.

01:23:57.132 --> 01:23:58.466
Ha!

01:23:58.466 --> 01:24:00.769
139 grams.

01:24:00.769 --> 01:24:02.303
So that's a little less than double.

01:24:04.339 --> 01:24:08.243
This is a large Domino's margherita pizza.

01:24:08.243 --> 01:24:11.146
It's also known as a
plain or cheese in the US.

01:24:11.146 --> 01:24:12.547
This is 12 inches long.

01:24:12.547 --> 01:24:16.985
It costs 419 rupees, or $5.55

01:24:16.985 --> 01:24:18.586
at current conversion rates.

01:24:18.586 --> 01:24:21.089
So the total surface area of this pizza

01:24:21.089 --> 01:24:23.792
is 729.7 centimeters squared,

01:24:23.792 --> 01:24:27.262
which means it costs 0.76 cents

01:24:27.262 --> 01:24:29.931
per square centimeter of this pizza.

01:24:29.931 --> 01:24:32.033
Take our large 14-inch pizza,

01:24:32.033 --> 01:24:36.538
which is $13.99, or 1,056 Indian rupee,

01:24:36.538 --> 01:24:41.342
with an area of 993.1 squared centimeters.

01:24:41.342 --> 01:24:42.877
Just like these slices are squared.

01:24:42.877 --> 01:24:44.345
I totally did that on purpose.

01:24:44.345 --> 01:24:48.550
That's 1.4 cents per square centimeter.

01:24:48.550 --> 01:24:52.987
That means the Indian pizza is 45% cheaper

01:24:52.987 --> 01:24:54.289
than the American version.

01:24:56.558 --> 01:24:59.327
This is everything you'll get
on a menu at Domino's India

01:24:59.327 --> 01:25:01.663
that you will not get in America.

01:25:01.663 --> 01:25:03.565
Little skyscrapers.

01:25:03.565 --> 01:25:05.567
You guys have actual skyscrapers.

01:25:05.567 --> 01:25:08.436
We have Domino's-pizza-box skyscrapers.

01:25:08.436 --> 01:25:10.472
Here's everything at the US Domino's

01:25:10.472 --> 01:25:12.173
you can't get in India.

01:25:12.173 --> 01:25:13.608
We have five --

01:25:13.608 --> 01:25:14.442
that's 10.

01:25:14.442 --> 01:25:17.078
We have five different crust options.

01:25:17.078 --> 01:25:18.480
We have pan.

01:25:18.480 --> 01:25:21.549
Then you have wheat thin crust,

01:25:21.549 --> 01:25:23.051
cheese burst.

01:25:23.051 --> 01:25:25.086
Is there supposed to be cheese in here?

01:25:25.086 --> 01:25:26.888
Oh!

01:25:26.888 --> 01:25:29.290
There is cheese in here, for sure.

01:25:29.290 --> 01:25:31.359
Then we have hand-tossed,

01:25:31.359 --> 01:25:35.130
and we have something
called new hand-tossed.

01:25:35.130 --> 01:25:38.166
Maybe somebody else's hands
were used to make this one.

01:25:38.166 --> 01:25:40.935
In the US, our Domino's
has five crust options.

01:25:40.935 --> 01:25:42.437
This one right here, gluten-free.

01:25:42.437 --> 01:25:44.439
But you can only get
that as a small pizza.

01:25:44.439 --> 01:25:46.508
Next, over here, hand-tossed.

01:25:46.508 --> 01:25:48.877
Over here, the much thicker pan.

01:25:48.877 --> 01:25:50.311
That's medium only.

01:25:50.311 --> 01:25:52.881
This guy in the middle
here is the crunchy thin,

01:25:52.881 --> 01:25:55.216
which I just found out five seconds ago

01:25:55.216 --> 01:25:56.718
they also cut in squares.

01:25:56.718 --> 01:25:57.652
Didn't know that.

01:25:57.652 --> 01:26:01.656
Last and certainly not least,
this is the Brooklyn style.

01:26:01.656 --> 01:26:03.291
They're thin slices, but
you can only get this

01:26:03.291 --> 01:26:05.293
as the large and the extra large.

01:26:05.293 --> 01:26:07.262
Hell yeah, that looks so good.

01:26:07.262 --> 01:26:08.897
Just by looking at them,

01:26:08.897 --> 01:26:12.800
I can tell that the hand-tossed
is slightly thinner.

01:26:14.569 --> 01:26:15.737
Mm.

01:26:15.737 --> 01:26:17.238
New hand-tossed.

01:26:19.440 --> 01:26:21.442
It's a little firmer as a crust.

01:26:21.442 --> 01:26:24.412
I would opt for the
regular hand-tossed pizza.

01:26:24.412 --> 01:26:26.080
Finally, just for fun,

01:26:26.080 --> 01:26:27.182
the cheese burst.

01:26:29.250 --> 01:26:30.885
That is such a guilty pleasure.

01:26:30.885 --> 01:26:32.854
So, I thought this was cheese burst

01:26:32.854 --> 01:26:35.757
in the sense that just the
outer ring of crust had cheese.

01:26:35.757 --> 01:26:39.961
The entire pizza base is cheese burst.

01:26:39.961 --> 01:26:43.598
All right, here is our
range of vegetarian pizzas.

01:26:43.598 --> 01:26:45.767
Here in India, to keep with
the religious sentiments

01:26:45.767 --> 01:26:47.268
of both Hindus and Muslims,

01:26:47.268 --> 01:26:49.637
who are a majority in our country,

01:26:49.637 --> 01:26:52.941
we avoid using beef and pork
in most fast-food restaurants.

01:26:52.941 --> 01:26:54.209
But what that means is that we get

01:26:54.209 --> 01:26:57.478
a lot of delicious vegetarian options.

01:26:57.478 --> 01:26:59.814
No. 1, Mexican Green Wave.

01:26:59.814 --> 01:27:01.783
I will say the colors on this pizza

01:27:01.783 --> 01:27:04.085
definitely look like the Mexican flag.

01:27:04.085 --> 01:27:07.255
Jalapeños, some tomatoes, onion, cheese.

01:27:07.255 --> 01:27:10.158
Next up, we have veggie paradise.

01:27:10.158 --> 01:27:11.125
Wow.

01:27:11.125 --> 01:27:14.596
Imagine calling an
entire pizza a paradise.

01:27:14.596 --> 01:27:18.499
Red peppers, capsicum,
olives, corn, and cheese.

01:27:18.499 --> 01:27:19.834
You guys in the comments, let me know,

01:27:19.834 --> 01:27:21.936
does this look like paradise to you?

01:27:21.936 --> 01:27:23.771
I'm not in the comments,
but I'll tell you right now,

01:27:23.771 --> 01:27:25.173
it absolutely does not.

01:27:25.173 --> 01:27:27.809
It's funny. Their veggie paradise

01:27:27.809 --> 01:27:29.277
is my pizza hell.

01:27:29.277 --> 01:27:31.312
Next up, deluxe veggie.

01:27:31.312 --> 01:27:35.483
Mushrooms, paneer, corn,
capsicum, and onion.

01:27:38.152 --> 01:27:40.822
I typically don't like when
there's too much on my pizza,

01:27:40.822 --> 01:27:42.857
but the things here really
complement each other.

01:27:42.857 --> 01:27:45.627
Pretty good. But, again, there's
so much going on in this.

01:27:45.627 --> 01:27:47.595
It's truly a deluxe pizza.

01:27:47.595 --> 01:27:50.732
Next up, we have Peppy Paneer. How fun!

01:27:50.732 --> 01:27:54.736
Red peppers, capsicum, and paneer.

01:27:54.736 --> 01:27:56.638
If you are wondering what paneer is,

01:27:56.638 --> 01:27:58.439
it's basically cottage cheese,

01:27:58.439 --> 01:28:02.176
and we love our paneer.

01:28:02.176 --> 01:28:04.312
OK, next up we have paneer makhani.

01:28:04.312 --> 01:28:05.980
If you're wondering what makhani means,

01:28:05.980 --> 01:28:08.016
it's a paneer version of butter chicken.

01:28:08.016 --> 01:28:09.984
If you're wondering
what butter chicken is,

01:28:09.984 --> 01:28:13.254
friend, you need a culinary education.

01:28:15.890 --> 01:28:16.724
Hm.

01:28:16.724 --> 01:28:18.826
Would I ever want paneer
makhani on a pizza?

01:28:18.826 --> 01:28:20.261
Maybe not. I don't like it.

01:28:20.261 --> 01:28:22.730
Next up, we have cheese and corn.

01:28:22.730 --> 01:28:24.632
It's got cheese, it's got corn.

01:28:24.632 --> 01:28:28.970
And finally, Indi paneer tandoori pizza.

01:28:28.970 --> 01:28:31.572
Tandoor is basically an oven we use here.

01:28:31.572 --> 01:28:33.741
It's cylindrical. We use
wood fire and coal in it

01:28:33.741 --> 01:28:36.978
to sort of give the meat
and bread some char to it.

01:28:36.978 --> 01:28:40.548
And Indi, well, this pizza has
just not hit mainstream yet.

01:28:42.850 --> 01:28:46.187
Oh, that is spicy and a half.

01:28:46.187 --> 01:28:48.723
If you can't take heat, avoid this one.

01:28:48.723 --> 01:28:51.125
My favorite so far,

01:28:51.125 --> 01:28:53.628
none of them. I will
order a non-veg pizza.

01:28:53.628 --> 01:28:56.898
Wow, India has a lot
more vegetarian options

01:28:56.898 --> 01:28:58.700
than we do, and good for them.

01:28:58.700 --> 01:29:00.468
I personally don't want any of that.

01:29:00.468 --> 01:29:03.771
We do have two of our own
exclusive veggie options.

01:29:03.771 --> 01:29:06.140
This here is the Pacific veggie.

01:29:06.140 --> 01:29:09.477
And over here we have
the spinach and feta.

01:29:09.477 --> 01:29:11.546
I don't want to try either of these.

01:29:11.546 --> 01:29:13.348
Do I have to?

01:29:13.348 --> 01:29:16.284
It's wasting valuable
stomach space, you know?

01:29:16.284 --> 01:29:17.852
Like, it's only so big.

01:29:17.852 --> 01:29:19.821
All this awesome Domino's food here,

01:29:19.821 --> 01:29:21.856
you think I want any of this
in my stomach? Who cares?

01:29:21.856 --> 01:29:22.890
All right, fine.

01:29:24.292 --> 01:29:25.760
What's it got, like, feta cheese on it?

01:29:25.760 --> 01:29:26.828
This isn't so bad.

01:29:28.396 --> 01:29:30.598
Nonvegetarian pizzas.

01:29:30.598 --> 01:29:33.067
No. 1, we have the pepper barbecue.

01:29:33.067 --> 01:29:35.803
Doesn't look like it has any vegetables,

01:29:35.803 --> 01:29:38.139
just a bunch of chicken pieces

01:29:38.139 --> 01:29:41.109
and with a nice smoky barbecue flavor.

01:29:41.109 --> 01:29:44.779
But you can choose a pepper
barbecue chicken with onion.

01:29:46.280 --> 01:29:48.015
That is a great combination.

01:29:48.015 --> 01:29:51.285
Chicken sausage. Quite
sausage-y, for sure.

01:29:51.285 --> 01:29:54.021
The next pizza is what I believe to be

01:29:54.021 --> 01:29:56.557
the best pizza you can
order from Domino's India.

01:29:56.557 --> 01:29:59.260
The Chicken Golden Delight.

01:29:59.260 --> 01:30:00.995
What a delightful name.

01:30:00.995 --> 01:30:03.297
This is one of the oldest
pizzas that's been there

01:30:03.297 --> 01:30:05.333
on the Domino's India menu.

01:30:05.333 --> 01:30:07.068
It's got nice sweet corn,

01:30:07.068 --> 01:30:08.803
it's got some jalapeños in there,

01:30:08.803 --> 01:30:12.440
and some delicious, delightful chicken.

01:30:13.741 --> 01:30:18.045
Next, we have the Dominator,
which seems to have

01:30:18.045 --> 01:30:22.917
every single meat-topping
option on the menu.

01:30:22.917 --> 01:30:24.118
My God.

01:30:25.420 --> 01:30:27.422
Consider me dominated.

01:30:27.422 --> 01:30:29.424
I don't think he knows what that means.

01:30:30.258 --> 01:30:33.461
Wow. We're learning a lot
about Nikhil today, aren't we?

01:30:33.461 --> 01:30:34.862
Whatever you're into, my man.

01:30:34.862 --> 01:30:36.497
And next we have chicken fiesta.

01:30:36.497 --> 01:30:38.466
It's got some tandoori chicken pieces,

01:30:38.466 --> 01:30:41.469
some capsicum, onion.
Nice, simple flavors.

01:30:41.469 --> 01:30:42.737
You can't go wrong with this one.

01:30:42.737 --> 01:30:45.440
And finally, Indi chicken tikka,

01:30:45.440 --> 01:30:47.175
which is just the chicken version

01:30:47.175 --> 01:30:49.210
of that paneer pizza I had.

01:30:49.210 --> 01:30:50.978
And that one just burned my lips,

01:30:50.978 --> 01:30:54.215
so steer clear of this one
if you can't handle spice,

01:30:54.215 --> 01:30:57.285
but if you do, this is
the one you should get.

01:30:57.285 --> 01:30:58.586
Actually, some of those look pretty good.

01:30:58.586 --> 01:30:59.687
I'm very impressed.

01:30:59.687 --> 01:31:01.155
Now, here in the US,

01:31:01.155 --> 01:31:05.560
every pizza that has beef
on it is an exclusive.

01:31:05.560 --> 01:31:07.061
And we also got some chicken ones.

01:31:07.061 --> 01:31:08.463
Let's do this. I am starving.

01:31:08.463 --> 01:31:10.198
All the way over here,

01:31:10.198 --> 01:31:14.268
this is the ExtravaganZZa,
which looks to have

01:31:14.268 --> 01:31:17.839
bunch of veggies,
mushrooms, and pepperoni.

01:31:23.678 --> 01:31:24.612
Yeah.

01:31:24.612 --> 01:31:28.149
This is the MeatZZa. That's
with two capital Z's.

01:31:28.149 --> 01:31:32.386
I'm seeing pepperoni, ham,
sausage, possibly hamburger.

01:31:32.386 --> 01:31:33.454
All the meats.

01:31:33.454 --> 01:31:34.755
Hell, yeah. Let's go.

01:31:37.325 --> 01:31:38.159
Mm.

01:31:38.159 --> 01:31:39.393
I can maybe do one bite of that.

01:31:39.393 --> 01:31:40.461
My neck's starting to sweat.

01:31:40.461 --> 01:31:42.830
Next, we got the Hawaiian pizza.

01:31:44.365 --> 01:31:45.399
Mm.

01:31:45.399 --> 01:31:47.435
A-plus on this one. I f--- with this one.

01:31:47.435 --> 01:31:48.736
Definitely. Very good.

01:31:48.736 --> 01:31:51.072
Cali chicken bacon ranch.

01:31:51.072 --> 01:31:54.141
And you see, it looks like
it has sun-dried tomatoes,

01:31:54.141 --> 01:31:57.378
bacon, I'm assuming, and
chicken, white sauce.

01:31:57.378 --> 01:31:59.080
Little flimsy guy. This
is the Brooklyn style,

01:31:59.080 --> 01:32:00.448
so I don't know why it's California.

01:32:02.250 --> 01:32:03.351
Oh, yeah.

01:32:03.351 --> 01:32:04.185
That white sauce.

01:32:04.185 --> 01:32:06.220
Buffalo chicken pizza.

01:32:06.220 --> 01:32:07.555
I mean, they drizzled it on there, right?

01:32:07.555 --> 01:32:09.023
You see that? It's just drizzled.

01:32:11.158 --> 01:32:12.793
This one's surprisingly very good.

01:32:12.793 --> 01:32:13.995
The ultimate pepperoni.

01:32:13.995 --> 01:32:15.596
Not just any pepperoni pizza.

01:32:15.596 --> 01:32:16.998
The ultimate pepperoni.

01:32:16.998 --> 01:32:18.165
Oh, yeah.

01:32:18.165 --> 01:32:19.700
It's covered in pepperoni.

01:32:19.700 --> 01:32:20.868
"Ooh" is right!

01:32:21.802 --> 01:32:22.870
Mm!

01:32:22.870 --> 01:32:25.006
Oh, yeah, put me in a pepperoni coma.

01:32:25.006 --> 01:32:26.173
Oh, yeah.

01:32:26.173 --> 01:32:27.208
Oh, the deluxe.

01:32:27.208 --> 01:32:29.610
Deluxe is just that,
little bit of everything.

01:32:29.610 --> 01:32:34.348
Black olives, sausage,
peppers, ham, probably bacon.

01:32:36.717 --> 01:32:38.486
You put black olives on anything,

01:32:38.486 --> 01:32:39.921
it just tastes like black olives.

01:32:39.921 --> 01:32:41.622
Ooh, Memphis barbecue.

01:32:41.622 --> 01:32:44.625
I am pro barbecue sauce on pizza.

01:32:44.625 --> 01:32:45.860
And it looks like they
got chicken here too.

01:32:45.860 --> 01:32:46.961
Yeah. Onions.

01:32:48.496 --> 01:32:49.997
Mm.

01:32:49.997 --> 01:32:52.366
Yeah. Oh, man.

01:32:52.366 --> 01:32:54.302
That barbecue sauce. That's really nice.

01:32:54.302 --> 01:32:57.171
Wisconsin six cheese.

01:32:57.171 --> 01:32:59.273
There's no way there's six cheeses here.

01:32:59.273 --> 01:33:00.808
I don't think I can name six cheeses.

01:33:00.808 --> 01:33:03.277
We have mozzarella, cheddar, Asiago,

01:33:03.277 --> 01:33:04.812
does American count as cheese?

01:33:04.812 --> 01:33:06.714
Did I say cheddar yet?

01:33:06.714 --> 01:33:08.416
Blue, I don't know.

01:33:08.416 --> 01:33:10.618
Next up, if all of those non-veg pizzas

01:33:10.618 --> 01:33:11.786
aren't enough for you,

01:33:11.786 --> 01:33:15.289
they have an entire section
called chicken lovers,

01:33:15.289 --> 01:33:19.427
and they have these four pizzas
that look absolutely insane.

01:33:19.427 --> 01:33:22.263
They're more topping
than pizza at this point.

01:33:22.263 --> 01:33:25.366
This one is called the chicken five feast.

01:33:25.366 --> 01:33:29.704
So they have chicken,
pepperoni, chicken tikka,

01:33:29.704 --> 01:33:31.405
chicken meatballs.

01:33:33.474 --> 01:33:35.409
There is so much going on over there.

01:33:35.409 --> 01:33:39.714
I like it, but it feels
like a drug, a pizza drug.

01:33:39.714 --> 01:33:41.482
Next up, we have the spicy double chicken.

01:33:41.482 --> 01:33:43.117
It has two different types of chicken,

01:33:43.117 --> 01:33:44.785
pepper chicken and tandoori chicken.

01:33:44.785 --> 01:33:46.721
And I assume it will be spicy,

01:33:46.721 --> 01:33:48.789
and I'm going to take
Domino's word for it.

01:33:48.789 --> 01:33:51.993
And then we have Chicken Maximus,

01:33:51.993 --> 01:33:56.130
which sounds like a Roman
emperor who was also a coward.

01:33:57.198 --> 01:34:00.501
They have chicken sausage, chicken tikka,

01:34:00.501 --> 01:34:03.004
just a lot of chicken.
Just a lot of chicken.

01:34:03.004 --> 01:34:03.871
That's what this has.

01:34:03.871 --> 01:34:07.441
Like, oh, my God, can I just weigh this?

01:34:07.441 --> 01:34:09.510
It feels like a small baby.

01:34:09.510 --> 01:34:11.712
I'm holding a small baby.

01:34:11.712 --> 01:34:15.650
545 grams for a medium pizza.

01:34:15.650 --> 01:34:19.086
And finally, we have what
appears to be the king

01:34:19.086 --> 01:34:21.122
of all of these chicken-lover pizzas.

01:34:21.122 --> 01:34:25.426
It's an Indo fusion max.

01:34:25.426 --> 01:34:27.028
Sounds like, I don't know,

01:34:27.028 --> 01:34:28.562
some sort of detergent.

01:34:28.562 --> 01:34:32.299
But, dude, you can't even tell what,

01:34:32.299 --> 01:34:35.069
like, what number of
ingredients is on this?

01:34:35.069 --> 01:34:37.171
I can't even see the pizza at this point.

01:34:40.908 --> 01:34:42.476
Oh, my God.

01:34:42.476 --> 01:34:44.445
I feel like a new man.

01:34:44.445 --> 01:34:47.114
You have to order this once in your life.

01:34:47.114 --> 01:34:49.450
It gives me deep displeasure to announce

01:34:49.450 --> 01:34:52.753
that Domino's India has decided to create

01:34:52.753 --> 01:34:56.657
these monstrosities called pizza burgers.

01:34:56.657 --> 01:34:58.459
Look at this. [knocking]

01:34:58.459 --> 01:35:00.728
Is a burger supposed to make this noise?

01:35:01.929 --> 01:35:03.130
In Bengaluru, where I'm from,

01:35:03.130 --> 01:35:05.533
if something bad happens to you,

01:35:05.533 --> 01:35:08.002
your friend will say you got a bun.

01:35:08.002 --> 01:35:10.871
And this is the bun they're talking about.

01:35:10.871 --> 01:35:12.840
They have three flavors, classic veg,

01:35:12.840 --> 01:35:15.976
premium veg, and classic non-veg.

01:35:15.976 --> 01:35:19.580
Ah! Oh, man!

01:35:19.580 --> 01:35:21.282
No!

01:35:21.282 --> 01:35:23.751
It's just veggies and
sauce. Is that cheese?

01:35:23.751 --> 01:35:26.287
No! No, no, no, no, no.

01:35:26.287 --> 01:35:27.455
[sighs]

01:35:29.990 --> 01:35:30.925
You know what?

01:35:30.925 --> 01:35:32.860
I thought this would be bad.

01:35:32.860 --> 01:35:35.362
And it's worse.

01:35:35.362 --> 01:35:37.865
It's much worse. It's not a burger.

01:35:37.865 --> 01:35:40.501
Nothing about this is a
burger except for the bun.

01:35:40.501 --> 01:35:41.969
This might be the worst thing I've eaten

01:35:41.969 --> 01:35:43.904
on "Food Wars" so far.

01:35:43.904 --> 01:35:46.574
OK. We did kind of the same thing,

01:35:46.574 --> 01:35:48.209
only we call them sandwiches.

01:35:48.209 --> 01:35:50.478
I've never gotten one of
these outside of "Food Wars."

01:35:50.478 --> 01:35:52.046
I'm just going to pick
this one right here.

01:35:52.046 --> 01:35:54.515
It looks like it is a chicken habanero.

01:35:54.515 --> 01:35:57.918
Everyone want to get bummed out? Aw.

01:35:57.918 --> 01:36:00.821
Philly cheesesteak.
Listen up, Philadelphia.

01:36:00.821 --> 01:36:03.691
Domino's wants to make you guys proud.

01:36:03.691 --> 01:36:05.960
Philadelphia, why are
you not rioting right now

01:36:05.960 --> 01:36:07.595
at the Domino's
headquarters, wherever it is?

01:36:07.595 --> 01:36:09.230
Because this is just insulting.

01:36:09.230 --> 01:36:10.231
Oh, no.

01:36:10.231 --> 01:36:11.999
Remember the Mediterranean veggie?

01:36:11.999 --> 01:36:13.901
Here it is in sandwich form.

01:36:13.901 --> 01:36:15.136
Oh, this one has banana peppers on it.

01:36:15.136 --> 01:36:16.470
Ooh, here we go.

01:36:16.470 --> 01:36:19.440
Chicken bacon ranch.

01:36:19.440 --> 01:36:20.574
Love that combination.

01:36:20.574 --> 01:36:23.244
Oh, no. Yuelei, look at this.

01:36:23.244 --> 01:36:24.645
Look at this!

01:36:24.645 --> 01:36:26.380
This is just too much.

01:36:26.380 --> 01:36:27.515
This one I just labeled "sandwich."

01:36:27.515 --> 01:36:28.449
I didn't know which one it was.

01:36:28.449 --> 01:36:30.985
What the f---? Look at this. What is this?

01:36:30.985 --> 01:36:32.453
Is this the Buffalo chicken?

01:36:32.453 --> 01:36:34.421
No on this one, guys.

01:36:34.421 --> 01:36:36.824
Buffalo, let us know in the chat

01:36:36.824 --> 01:36:38.325
how insulted you are by this.

01:36:38.325 --> 01:36:41.929
Both residents of Buffalo
and Buffalo the animals.

01:36:41.929 --> 01:36:44.298
Uh, Italian.

01:36:44.298 --> 01:36:45.766
They didn't skimp on the pepperoni,

01:36:45.766 --> 01:36:46.967
I gotta give them credit for that one.

01:36:46.967 --> 01:36:49.136
The chicken Parm sandwich.

01:36:52.306 --> 01:36:54.341
Surprisingly bland.

01:36:54.341 --> 01:36:56.210
They're not terrible, but, I mean,

01:36:56.210 --> 01:36:58.779
why get this instead of pizza?

01:36:58.779 --> 01:37:02.116
Continuing the list of
exclusive abominations,

01:37:02.116 --> 01:37:04.285
we have a string of pastas,

01:37:04.285 --> 01:37:07.321
but also pasta pizzas,

01:37:07.321 --> 01:37:10.291
which look, um, fascinating.

01:37:10.291 --> 01:37:13.260
Here in Domino's India,
we use fusilli pasta,

01:37:13.260 --> 01:37:17.832
fusilli being the whole
helix DNA strand of pastas.

01:37:17.832 --> 01:37:20.534
We have creamy tomato, veg, non-veg,

01:37:20.534 --> 01:37:24.104
and we have Moroccan
spice, veg and non-veg.

01:37:24.104 --> 01:37:28.108
And to accompany these
I'm sure delicious pastas,

01:37:28.108 --> 01:37:31.645
we have pasta pizzas in the same flavors.

01:37:31.645 --> 01:37:36.383
Wow, just really inventive
stuff going on over here.

01:37:36.383 --> 01:37:40.287
This is the Moroccan spice
vegetarian pasta pizza.

01:37:40.287 --> 01:37:41.322
Here we go.

01:37:41.322 --> 01:37:42.156
Voice-over: They ask you how you are,

01:37:42.156 --> 01:37:43.724
and you just have to say that you're fine

01:37:43.724 --> 01:37:44.792
when you're not really fine.

01:37:50.931 --> 01:37:53.567
It sent a shiver down my spine.

01:37:53.567 --> 01:37:56.170
It's so bad.

01:37:56.170 --> 01:37:58.772
How many different types
of carbs are in this?

01:37:58.772 --> 01:38:01.909
My disappointment is immeasurable,
and my day is ruined.

01:38:01.909 --> 01:38:06.146
OK, I'm going to try one
pasta just in case it's good.

01:38:06.146 --> 01:38:07.314
Let's mix it up.

01:38:07.314 --> 01:38:10.050
This one has some tomato sauce in it.

01:38:13.921 --> 01:38:15.623
This is bad.

01:38:15.623 --> 01:38:18.759
We here in the US have our pasta options

01:38:18.759 --> 01:38:21.328
that come in penne noodles,
these type of noodle guys.

01:38:21.328 --> 01:38:22.930
Is that a good shot of a penne noodle?

01:38:22.930 --> 01:38:25.699
You can get it in pasta primavera,

01:38:25.699 --> 01:38:27.635
chicken carbonara,

01:38:27.635 --> 01:38:28.836
chicken Alfredo,

01:38:28.836 --> 01:38:30.804
Italian sausage marinara.

01:38:30.804 --> 01:38:32.206
Again, I don't know why
you're getting pasta

01:38:32.206 --> 01:38:33.307
at a pizza place.

01:38:34.842 --> 01:38:36.610
I like it just fine.

01:38:36.610 --> 01:38:38.879
Is this the best pasta you
can get in your neighborhood?

01:38:38.879 --> 01:38:40.047
Most certainly not.

01:38:40.047 --> 01:38:41.382
Now on to chicken wings.

01:38:41.382 --> 01:38:44.785
We have three flavors, tomato chili sauce,

01:38:44.785 --> 01:38:47.655
peri-peri, and boneless peri-peri.

01:38:47.655 --> 01:38:48.989
I'm going to try the peri-peri wings

01:38:48.989 --> 01:38:51.258
just to see how they stack up.

01:38:53.394 --> 01:38:54.228
They're all right.

01:38:54.228 --> 01:38:56.397
They're just your standard,
run-of-the-mill chicken wings.

01:38:56.397 --> 01:38:58.999
In a country full of millions of flavors,

01:38:58.999 --> 01:39:00.501
I can't believe we're
still doing these same

01:39:00.501 --> 01:39:03.203
standard flavors like
peri-peri, barbecue, and ranch.

01:39:03.203 --> 01:39:06.874
Where is my chicken
65, my chicken mughlai,

01:39:06.874 --> 01:39:08.442
my chicken ghee roast?

01:39:08.442 --> 01:39:09.443
Oh, chicken ghee roast.

01:39:09.443 --> 01:39:12.513
Domino's, if you do
chicken ghee roast wings,

01:39:12.513 --> 01:39:13.881
I think you're going to
get a lot more people.

01:39:13.881 --> 01:39:16.383
Wings in the US. We got them too.

01:39:16.383 --> 01:39:18.652
Here's three flavors that
we have here in the US.

01:39:18.652 --> 01:39:22.289
Honey barbecue, sweet mango
habanero, and garlic Parmesan.

01:39:22.289 --> 01:39:24.258
Domino's, if you're watching,

01:39:24.258 --> 01:39:26.760
you need to, effective immediately,

01:39:26.760 --> 01:39:29.296
stop doing this.

01:39:29.296 --> 01:39:31.398
I don't know who in
your organization said,

01:39:31.398 --> 01:39:32.566
"You know what we should do?

01:39:32.566 --> 01:39:34.435
Instead of tossing it in the sauce,

01:39:34.435 --> 01:39:36.737
you know, how everyone
expects their wings to come,

01:39:36.737 --> 01:39:38.372
we'll just put it on here and drizzle."

01:39:38.372 --> 01:39:40.107
Look at this. Look at this mess.

01:39:40.107 --> 01:39:43.344
Toss it. Toss the wings.
Toss it in the sauce.

01:39:43.344 --> 01:39:44.611
Toss it in the sauce.

01:39:44.611 --> 01:39:46.680
That's how everyone does this,
how it's supposed to be done.

01:39:46.680 --> 01:39:49.216
Next up, exclusive sides.

01:39:49.216 --> 01:39:52.419
No. 1, cheese pops.

01:39:52.419 --> 01:39:54.355
Tater tots, as you call them.

01:39:54.355 --> 01:39:57.791
We have fries, and they're
crinkle-cut. That's unique.

01:39:57.791 --> 01:40:00.060
Not a lot of restaurants
here in India do this.

01:40:00.060 --> 01:40:02.696
They have been flavored with
a bunch of stuff, though, so.

01:40:02.696 --> 01:40:04.965
I think they've used their oregano

01:40:04.965 --> 01:40:06.700
and chili flakes over here.

01:40:06.700 --> 01:40:08.202
They have here a veg parcel.

01:40:08.202 --> 01:40:09.703
It's like a little puff

01:40:09.703 --> 01:40:12.906
with the same paneer pieces over here.

01:40:12.906 --> 01:40:16.510
Then they have what they call tacos.

01:40:16.510 --> 01:40:17.745
There's a vegetarian version

01:40:17.745 --> 01:40:21.915
with some simple veg cutlets,

01:40:21.915 --> 01:40:25.185
and they have a nonvegetarian version with

01:40:25.185 --> 01:40:27.154
[laughs] a slab of chicken.

01:40:27.154 --> 01:40:28.689
I did not expect that.

01:40:28.689 --> 01:40:32.059
I am speechless at the level
of quality these sides have

01:40:32.059 --> 01:40:33.527
compared to the pizzas.

01:40:33.527 --> 01:40:35.162
Then you have a chicken parcel.

01:40:35.162 --> 01:40:39.500
And finally, they have
little meatballs of chicken

01:40:39.500 --> 01:40:41.402
with peri-peri dust on top of them.

01:40:41.402 --> 01:40:44.671
This is literally just one
of their pizza toppings

01:40:44.671 --> 01:40:46.373
that they're selling as a side.

01:40:46.373 --> 01:40:50.044
Yes, India has breadsticks
and stuff with cheesy bread,

01:40:50.044 --> 01:40:51.845
but they don't have garlic ones.

01:40:51.845 --> 01:40:52.846
We got those.

01:40:52.846 --> 01:40:57.418
We also have these Parmesan twists.

01:40:57.418 --> 01:40:58.752
Look at these twisty guys.

01:40:58.752 --> 01:41:01.088
And for stuffed cheesy bread,

01:41:01.088 --> 01:41:03.724
you can get it as spinach and feta

01:41:03.724 --> 01:41:05.259
or bacon and jalapeño.

01:41:05.259 --> 01:41:06.994
Dips. This, I don't know what,

01:41:06.994 --> 01:41:07.828
they just were like,

01:41:07.828 --> 01:41:09.997
"How can we give people
pizza without bread?"

01:41:09.997 --> 01:41:12.166
Behold, this.

01:41:12.166 --> 01:41:16.437
It is a dish of cheese and marinara sauce.

01:41:16.437 --> 01:41:17.738
They're calling them dips.

01:41:17.738 --> 01:41:19.440
Cheesy marinara.

01:41:19.440 --> 01:41:22.242
And the five cheese. Come on.

01:41:22.242 --> 01:41:23.777
Look at that. Look at that oil.

01:41:23.777 --> 01:41:25.245
You see that right there?

01:41:25.245 --> 01:41:28.015
Exclusive sauces at the US Domino's.

01:41:28.015 --> 01:41:29.817
You know what that means.

01:41:29.817 --> 01:41:31.418
Sauce talk.

01:41:31.418 --> 01:41:35.189
Here, you can get these
exclusive sauces in the US.

01:41:35.189 --> 01:41:36.356
Can't get them in India.

01:41:36.356 --> 01:41:41.161
We got hot Buffalo, sweet mango habanero,

01:41:41.161 --> 01:41:45.032
honey barbecue, ranch,

01:41:45.032 --> 01:41:48.469
ooh, blue cheese, for the wings, right?

01:41:48.469 --> 01:41:50.304
And garlic.

01:41:51.138 --> 01:41:52.239
Yeah, it says ranch.

01:41:52.239 --> 01:41:53.474
They gave us two ranches instead of

01:41:53.474 --> 01:41:54.808
a ranch and a garlic.

01:41:54.808 --> 01:41:56.510
And marinara.

01:41:56.510 --> 01:41:58.112
They were generous with the marinara.

01:41:58.112 --> 01:41:59.379
That's a big one.

01:41:59.379 --> 01:42:02.382
We have two separate dips
over here in Domino's India.

01:42:02.382 --> 01:42:04.251
We have a cheesy dip,

01:42:04.251 --> 01:42:07.955
and we have a cheesy jalapeño dip.

01:42:09.256 --> 01:42:11.291
Cheesy dip.

01:42:11.291 --> 01:42:12.126
Ooh.

01:42:14.728 --> 01:42:16.063
Oh, that tastes good. OK.

01:42:16.063 --> 01:42:18.232
Cheesy jalapeño dip, really yum.

01:42:18.232 --> 01:42:19.967
Something about this tastes spoiled.

01:42:19.967 --> 01:42:22.136
Is this past its expiry date?

01:42:22.136 --> 01:42:23.804
It tastes like curdled milk.

01:42:23.804 --> 01:42:25.906
Go with the cheesy jalapeño dip, for sure.

01:42:25.906 --> 01:42:28.442
It's time for desserts!

01:42:28.442 --> 01:42:29.576
Dessert.

01:42:29.576 --> 01:42:32.346
We just have one dessert
here in Domino's India,

01:42:32.346 --> 01:42:34.047
but it's a banger.

01:42:34.047 --> 01:42:35.983
This is a choco lava cake.

01:42:35.983 --> 01:42:39.686
You heat it up, and boom,

01:42:39.686 --> 01:42:42.990
gooey lava goodness.

01:42:45.392 --> 01:42:46.960
Oh, wow.

01:42:46.960 --> 01:42:49.730
This fixed everything that was wrong

01:42:49.730 --> 01:42:52.499
with the menu of Domino's up until now.

01:42:52.499 --> 01:42:54.801
Just eating this is so comforting.

01:42:54.801 --> 01:42:58.038
I can feel those memories of the pasta

01:42:58.038 --> 01:43:01.241
and the burger and that
ridiculousness that they served

01:43:01.241 --> 01:43:03.310
slowly disappearing from my head,

01:43:03.310 --> 01:43:06.079
like thoughts from Dumbledore's head

01:43:06.079 --> 01:43:08.148
when he's near the pensieve.

01:43:08.148 --> 01:43:10.517
Hey, India, check out
these desserts we got.

01:43:10.517 --> 01:43:12.019
You can't have them.

01:43:12.019 --> 01:43:14.988
Over here, we have a
marbled cookie brownie.

01:43:14.988 --> 01:43:16.890
I'd go for a brownie. Right?

01:43:19.259 --> 01:43:21.128
What the hell, dude? These are great.

01:43:21.128 --> 01:43:22.496
Oh, my God.

01:43:22.496 --> 01:43:24.665
It's cookie dough and brownie.

01:43:24.665 --> 01:43:26.433
What a great idea!

01:43:26.433 --> 01:43:28.468
These dips. I don't know who

01:43:28.468 --> 01:43:31.772
in your organization
said, "Let's do dips,"

01:43:31.772 --> 01:43:34.575
but you need to let that person go.

01:43:34.575 --> 01:43:39.479
It's, like, chunky apple
sauce and cinnamon twists.

01:43:39.479 --> 01:43:40.681
Now it's time for drinks.

01:43:40.681 --> 01:43:42.916
Yet again, it's PepsiCo winning.

01:43:42.916 --> 01:43:47.688
Over here, we have Pepsi,
we have 7Up, and Mirinda.

01:43:47.688 --> 01:43:49.289
Unlike a lot of other restaurants,

01:43:49.289 --> 01:43:52.392
Domino's is yet to switch
from plastic PET bottles

01:43:52.392 --> 01:43:56.396
to something like cans or reusable cups.

01:43:56.396 --> 01:43:58.765
Drinks you can get in the
US, can't get in India.

01:43:58.765 --> 01:44:02.402
I almost said the UK.
Jesus. I'm cracking up.

01:44:02.402 --> 01:44:05.239
Coke, diet Coke,

01:44:05.239 --> 01:44:08.141
Fanta orange, the Doctor,

01:44:08.141 --> 01:44:10.978
Sprite, Dasani water.

01:44:10.978 --> 01:44:12.379
I'm taking the Dr. Pepper.

01:44:14.948 --> 01:44:16.183
It's time for calories.

01:44:16.183 --> 01:44:19.186
Our large hand-tossed margherita pizza

01:44:19.186 --> 01:44:23.523
has 256.4 calories per slice.

01:44:23.523 --> 01:44:28.161
So that means the full
pizza is 2,051.5 calories,

01:44:28.161 --> 01:44:31.098
which is over twice your daily
recommended protein intake

01:44:31.098 --> 01:44:33.934
and 172.5%

01:44:33.934 --> 01:44:35.869
your daily sodium intake.

01:44:35.869 --> 01:44:37.304
Yeesh!

01:44:37.304 --> 01:44:41.108
Our large cheese pizza is 2,240 calories.

01:44:41.108 --> 01:44:44.378
That's a 9.19% increase

01:44:44.378 --> 01:44:46.647
from India's cheese pizza.

01:44:46.647 --> 01:44:48.682
Look, I screwed up.

01:44:48.682 --> 01:44:53.053
I needed a thin crust for the
crust section of this video,

01:44:53.053 --> 01:44:55.355
and I just randomly made it this large.

01:44:55.355 --> 01:44:57.924
Just understand that ...

01:44:57.924 --> 01:45:00.694
maybe, Victoria, can you do me a favor

01:45:00.694 --> 01:45:04.064
and take this pizza here
and just put it right there?

01:45:04.064 --> 01:45:06.233
Like, can you just do
that in post, please?

01:45:06.233 --> 01:45:09.269
Next up, one slice of a
large deluxe veg pizza

01:45:09.269 --> 01:45:11.738
is 220.5 calories.

01:45:11.738 --> 01:45:13.774
And so the entire pizza

01:45:13.774 --> 01:45:17.311
is 1,764 calories.

01:45:17.311 --> 01:45:20.781
This is our large Pacific
veggie veggie pizza,

01:45:20.781 --> 01:45:23.717
and it is 310 calories per slice,

01:45:23.717 --> 01:45:28.288
which makes the full pizza 2,480 calories.

01:45:28.288 --> 01:45:32.125
That's a 40% calorie increase in the US.

01:45:32.125 --> 01:45:34.961
And, oof, get a load of that sodium,

01:45:34.961 --> 01:45:37.564
over 200% your daily amount.

01:45:37.564 --> 01:45:41.635
At Domino's India, our
highest calorific pizza

01:45:41.635 --> 01:45:45.439
is the chicken dominatrix.

01:45:45.439 --> 01:45:47.674
Chicken Dominator!

01:45:47.674 --> 01:45:52.179
The chicken Dominator,
dominating the calories, I guess.

01:45:52.179 --> 01:45:55.515
One slice will cost you 399 calories,

01:45:55.515 --> 01:45:58.785
and the entire pizza is a whopping

01:45:58.785 --> 01:46:01.888
3,192 calories,

01:46:01.888 --> 01:46:04.858
which is 159.6%

01:46:04.858 --> 01:46:07.361
of your recommended daily intake.

01:46:07.361 --> 01:46:09.730
Please steer clear from eating

01:46:09.730 --> 01:46:12.666
an entire chicken Dominator.

01:46:12.666 --> 01:46:15.035
Our US Domino's pizza with
the most calories is this,

01:46:15.035 --> 01:46:18.438
the Cali chicken bacon ranch.

01:46:18.438 --> 01:46:23.076
One XL Brooklyn slice
of this is 560 calories.

01:46:23.076 --> 01:46:26.580
That makes the full pie 3,360 calories.

01:46:26.580 --> 01:46:30.917
That's 168% your daily
recommended calorie amount.

01:46:30.917 --> 01:46:32.619
It's worth it. It's delicious.

01:46:32.619 --> 01:46:33.820
Go get a slice.

01:46:33.820 --> 01:46:36.256
Tell 'em Joe from "Food Wars" sent you.

01:46:36.256 --> 01:46:38.258
They'll have no idea what
you're talking about.

01:46:38.892 --> 01:46:40.627
Joe: From calorie count to portion sizes,

01:46:40.627 --> 01:46:42.396
we wanted to find out all the differences

01:46:42.396 --> 01:46:44.898
between Subway in India and the US.

01:46:44.898 --> 01:46:46.700
This is "Food Wars."

01:46:50.637 --> 01:46:53.974
Subway sandwiches in
India come in two sizes:

01:46:53.974 --> 01:46:57.544
6 inches, 12 inches.

01:46:57.544 --> 01:47:00.514
Subway in the US also has those two sizes,

01:47:00.514 --> 01:47:03.049
6-inch and 12-inch.

01:47:03.049 --> 01:47:05.385
Now, the website also
says there's a 4-inch sub

01:47:05.385 --> 01:47:08.422
called a chhota sub, chhota meaning small,

01:47:08.422 --> 01:47:10.056
but mysteriously, it is unavailable.

01:47:10.056 --> 01:47:12.559
We called four outlets. Wasn't there.

01:47:12.559 --> 01:47:14.461
And now we shall measure the 12-inch sub

01:47:14.461 --> 01:47:17.664
to see if it actually is 12 inches.

01:47:17.664 --> 01:47:19.199
Joe: Keeping them honest, right?

01:47:19.199 --> 01:47:20.934
That's 12 inches.

01:47:20.934 --> 01:47:22.035
All right, Subway.

01:47:22.035 --> 01:47:24.337
I'm getting more than 12 inches here.

01:47:24.337 --> 01:47:26.740
Subway has given me a 13-inch sub.

01:47:27.908 --> 01:47:29.409
This is why I love Subway.

01:47:29.409 --> 01:47:31.278
Fun doesn't stop there, 'cause in the US,

01:47:31.278 --> 01:47:33.814
Subway also offers catering options.

01:47:33.814 --> 01:47:35.816
First, you can get this, a platter,

01:47:35.816 --> 01:47:38.685
which is five foot-long
subs cut into threes,

01:47:38.685 --> 01:47:41.755
making a total of 15 pieces.

01:47:41.755 --> 01:47:43.623
See? Boom, boom.

01:47:43.623 --> 01:47:45.792
The discrepancies continue here in India.

01:47:45.792 --> 01:47:48.195
The website says that we
too have a platter option,

01:47:48.195 --> 01:47:50.163
but we called a bunch of stores,

01:47:50.163 --> 01:47:51.331
no platter option.

01:47:52.365 --> 01:47:53.400
And on top of that, in the US,

01:47:53.400 --> 01:47:56.369
you can get a 3-foot-long party sub.

01:47:56.369 --> 01:47:58.138
Gush!

01:47:58.138 --> 01:47:59.940
We didn't get it this time.

01:47:59.940 --> 01:48:01.374
Graphics, you can go ahead and put a

01:48:01.374 --> 01:48:02.943
3-foot party sub right in front of me.

01:48:04.077 --> 01:48:05.145
Thanks, guys.

01:48:06.012 --> 01:48:07.514
OK, is my ex-girlfriend running

01:48:07.514 --> 01:48:08.715
the Subway and their website?

01:48:08.715 --> 01:48:10.217
Because it's full of lies.

01:48:10.217 --> 01:48:12.185
They not only advertise a 3-foot sub,

01:48:12.185 --> 01:48:14.187
but a 6-foot giant sub.

01:48:14.187 --> 01:48:16.456
And surprise, surprise, we
called a couple of stores,

01:48:16.456 --> 01:48:18.124
no 6-foot giant sub.

01:48:18.124 --> 01:48:20.327
In fact, they said, "There
are barely any 6-foot humans

01:48:20.327 --> 01:48:22.429
here in India, why would
there be a 6-foot sub?"

01:48:22.429 --> 01:48:25.065
And I was like, "Yeah,
sorry, I am the idiot."

01:48:25.065 --> 01:48:26.132
Hang up!

01:48:26.132 --> 01:48:27.701
OK, I am a short king.

01:48:27.701 --> 01:48:30.837
175 centimeters.

01:48:30.837 --> 01:48:33.807
This is how much I measure.

01:48:33.807 --> 01:48:37.811
Now, this is a 6-foot sub next to me.

01:48:37.811 --> 01:48:39.546
Why would this be a thing?

01:48:39.546 --> 01:48:41.181
It's taller than me.

01:48:42.415 --> 01:48:46.753
Well, Joe is 6 feet tall, so,

01:48:46.753 --> 01:48:49.823
I'll go ahead and [grunts].

01:48:49.823 --> 01:48:51.992
So, if graphics go ahead
and make me a sandwich

01:48:51.992 --> 01:48:53.960
in three, two, one.

01:48:55.662 --> 01:48:56.763
You know, this is pretty comfortable.

01:48:56.763 --> 01:48:58.832
Can we do the rest of the shoot like this?

01:48:58.832 --> 01:49:00.700
Ah, this is pretty nice.

01:49:00.700 --> 01:49:02.769
Here in India, Subway
has actually opted out

01:49:02.769 --> 01:49:04.070
of using a lot of plastic,

01:49:04.070 --> 01:49:07.874
which is why they only
stock these 330 ml cans,

01:49:07.874 --> 01:49:09.943
which I am going to
measure just to make sure

01:49:09.943 --> 01:49:12.913
we are not being fooled by PepsiCo.

01:49:12.913 --> 01:49:16.917
Mm. Smells like my teeth decaying.

01:49:16.917 --> 01:49:18.852
Yeah, looks about right, 330 ml.

01:49:20.453 --> 01:49:23.690
Subway in the US, we're still
totally using plastic cups.

01:49:23.690 --> 01:49:26.393
Small, medium, large,

01:49:26.393 --> 01:49:29.429
and the large is supposed to be 40 ounces.

01:49:29.429 --> 01:49:31.364
Why someone would want to
drink 40 ounces of something

01:49:31.364 --> 01:49:33.967
that's not malt liquor in
one sitting is beyond me,

01:49:33.967 --> 01:49:37.771
but if you want 40 ounces
of soda, good Lord,

01:49:37.771 --> 01:49:38.872
Subway has you covered.

01:49:38.872 --> 01:49:39.973
I, of course, am curious to see

01:49:39.973 --> 01:49:42.309
if there actually is 40
ounces in this drink.

01:49:42.309 --> 01:49:44.277
Full "Food Wars" transparency,

01:49:44.277 --> 01:49:46.680
I did have to fill up
my own fountain drink.

01:49:46.680 --> 01:49:47.647
Let's be honest.

01:49:47.647 --> 01:49:50.016
Can we agree that if you
had to get your own drink,

01:49:50.016 --> 01:49:52.986
fill it up to go, you would
probably get this much?

01:49:52.986 --> 01:49:56.122
Now, keep in mind, the cap is recessed.

01:49:56.122 --> 01:49:57.390
For everyone roasting me in the comments

01:49:57.390 --> 01:49:58.358
for not filling it up enough,

01:49:58.358 --> 01:50:00.126
like, you can only fill
this thing up so much.

01:50:02.028 --> 01:50:04.898
Oh, my God, not even close.

01:50:04.898 --> 01:50:05.865
You know, I'm even gonna, like,

01:50:05.865 --> 01:50:07.968
get the condensation on the cup in there

01:50:07.968 --> 01:50:10.770
just to even, like, help tip
the scales in their favor.

01:50:10.770 --> 01:50:11.605
Right?

01:50:11.605 --> 01:50:12.906
34?

01:50:12.906 --> 01:50:14.774
6? You guys are ... [sighs].

01:50:14.774 --> 01:50:18.078
Just say it's the 34-ounce
cup. Or 35 ounces.

01:50:18.078 --> 01:50:19.446
We're still gonna get it.

01:50:19.446 --> 01:50:20.614
Still gonna get it.

01:50:20.614 --> 01:50:22.115
Shame on you.

01:50:22.115 --> 01:50:24.284
I saw that John Oliver episode.

01:50:24.284 --> 01:50:26.353
Terrible, Subway. Shame on you.

01:50:26.353 --> 01:50:27.621
What you're doing with the franchisees,

01:50:27.621 --> 01:50:29.556
and what you're doing
skimping on the sodas.

01:50:32.058 --> 01:50:34.027
Here are all the Subway
menu items from India

01:50:34.027 --> 01:50:35.962
that you won't find in the US.

01:50:35.962 --> 01:50:37.597
Here's all the Subway menu items

01:50:37.597 --> 01:50:40.500
from the US you won't find in India.

01:50:40.500 --> 01:50:43.036
Obviously, Subway lets you
customize your sandwiches,

01:50:43.036 --> 01:50:44.070
so we're not talking about

01:50:44.070 --> 01:50:45.972
every single different combination.

01:50:45.972 --> 01:50:48.642
We're just going on
what is on the menu now.

01:50:48.642 --> 01:50:49.676
Let's begin.

01:50:49.676 --> 01:50:50.744
It's glorious.

01:50:50.744 --> 01:50:52.946
This feels like a Subway buffet,

01:50:52.946 --> 01:50:55.048
and I get to pick whatever I want.

01:50:55.048 --> 01:50:57.717
First of all, the aloo patty.

01:50:57.717 --> 01:51:01.221
This is basically potato which
has been cut up into pieces

01:51:01.221 --> 01:51:03.089
and then fried with breadcrumbs on top.

01:51:04.691 --> 01:51:06.126
Mm.

01:51:06.126 --> 01:51:08.328
This is not bad, but I think you can add

01:51:08.328 --> 01:51:10.664
all the fancy sauces you
want into this thing,

01:51:10.664 --> 01:51:13.667
nothing will beat a
humble Mumbai vada pav.

01:51:13.667 --> 01:51:16.936
Corn and peas. That
looks like a lot of mayo.

01:51:16.936 --> 01:51:19.439
I don't think I shall ever order this sub.

01:51:19.439 --> 01:51:23.009
This is a local legend,
the hara bhara kebab sub.

01:51:23.009 --> 01:51:24.878
This is the first thing
a vegetarian will order

01:51:24.878 --> 01:51:26.379
at an Indian restaurant,

01:51:26.379 --> 01:51:28.014
because it's this delicious mishmash

01:51:28.014 --> 01:51:30.650
of spices, vegetables, and potato,

01:51:30.650 --> 01:51:33.286
fried, tangy, delicious.

01:51:33.286 --> 01:51:35.588
Next up, we have a Mexican patty.

01:51:35.588 --> 01:51:37.891
I would like to extend an apology

01:51:37.891 --> 01:51:39.459
to all my Mexican brethren watching

01:51:39.459 --> 01:51:41.327
that their great culture has been reduced

01:51:41.327 --> 01:51:44.731
to a patty of aloo and beans.

01:51:44.731 --> 01:51:47.500
Paneer tikka, beautiful pieces

01:51:47.500 --> 01:51:49.869
of cottage cheese, as you call it.

01:51:49.869 --> 01:51:51.971
Is it weird for me to bite a Subway

01:51:51.971 --> 01:51:53.640
right through the middle?

01:51:53.640 --> 01:51:55.375
Would that upset you?

01:52:00.280 --> 01:52:01.181
It's nice.

01:52:01.181 --> 01:52:02.982
I wouldn't go with this
particular combination

01:52:02.982 --> 01:52:04.751
of vegetables and sauces.

01:52:04.751 --> 01:52:06.786
Also, I just want to point
out there are literally

01:52:06.786 --> 01:52:08.288
three pieces of paneer in here.

01:52:08.288 --> 01:52:09.656
When I used to go to Subway in college,

01:52:09.656 --> 01:52:13.927
I would make sure that they
put in a lot of protein.

01:52:13.927 --> 01:52:15.528
This is despicable.

01:52:15.528 --> 01:52:17.330
Veg seekh kebab.

01:52:17.330 --> 01:52:20.133
Seekh kebab, typically, is minced meat

01:52:20.133 --> 01:52:22.802
that's sort of pressed onto
a skewer and then grilled.

01:52:22.802 --> 01:52:23.970
But this is a veg version.

01:52:23.970 --> 01:52:27.774
It has a lot of different
mixed vegetables and potato.

01:52:27.774 --> 01:52:28.942
Mm!

01:52:28.942 --> 01:52:30.310
That's pretty yummy.

01:52:30.310 --> 01:52:33.079
I love the onions. The
sauce combination is great.

01:52:33.079 --> 01:52:35.882
And the seekh kebab itself, lot of flavor.

01:52:35.882 --> 01:52:38.918
Next up, we have the
vegetarian shammi kebab.

01:52:38.918 --> 01:52:41.588
As you can see, they're
nice round little balls.

01:52:41.588 --> 01:52:44.157
Shammi kebabs are from
Lucknow here in India.

01:52:44.157 --> 01:52:45.592
They have a very crispy exterior

01:52:45.592 --> 01:52:47.427
and a delicious
melt-in-your-mouth interior.

01:52:47.427 --> 01:52:49.562
They're typically minced meat,

01:52:49.562 --> 01:52:51.364
but this is a vegetarian version.

01:52:51.364 --> 01:52:52.499
Let me try this.

01:52:53.767 --> 01:52:54.934
Mm.

01:52:56.069 --> 01:52:57.370
Oh!

01:52:57.370 --> 01:52:58.838
Best one so far.

01:52:58.838 --> 01:53:00.774
♪ I'm so full ♪

01:53:00.774 --> 01:53:03.910
Next up, chatpata chana Subway.

01:53:03.910 --> 01:53:05.111
What a fun name.

01:53:05.111 --> 01:53:07.547
Chatpata means full of masala,

01:53:07.547 --> 01:53:09.916
zingy flavor, really delicious.

01:53:09.916 --> 01:53:11.718
Chana is lentils.

01:53:11.718 --> 01:53:14.487
It looks kind of like a dirty diaper,

01:53:14.487 --> 01:53:17.957
but I assure you this is going
to be absolutely delicious.

01:53:19.726 --> 01:53:21.694
Oh, yeah.

01:53:21.694 --> 01:53:22.529
That's pretty good.

01:53:22.529 --> 01:53:24.397
Now we're on to the nonvegetarian subs,

01:53:24.397 --> 01:53:27.333
starting with this one,
the Indian chicken tikka.

01:53:27.333 --> 01:53:28.501
Looks pretty good.

01:53:30.470 --> 01:53:33.406
I just took a mouthful, and
there was absolutely no chicken.

01:53:33.406 --> 01:53:35.675
Every bite should have
a bit of everything.

01:53:35.675 --> 01:53:37.377
Chicken kofta.

01:53:37.377 --> 01:53:39.913
Kofta is basically meatballs,

01:53:39.913 --> 01:53:41.347
and this is chicken-flavored.

01:53:41.347 --> 01:53:43.216
You can see the meatballs right there.

01:53:45.752 --> 01:53:47.887
Whoa, that's actually really good.

01:53:47.887 --> 01:53:50.156
Whoever picked the sauces on this one,

01:53:50.156 --> 01:53:51.658
this is the way.

01:53:51.658 --> 01:53:54.561
Barbecue, sweet onion, bit of ranch,

01:53:54.561 --> 01:53:56.229
a bit of mint mayo.

01:53:56.229 --> 01:53:58.965
This is the best sub out of all of them.

01:53:58.965 --> 01:54:01.734
I actually think it's
the combination of sauces

01:54:01.734 --> 01:54:03.403
that makes the sub what it is.

01:54:03.403 --> 01:54:04.938
It's leaking flavor.

01:54:04.938 --> 01:54:06.840
Peri-peri chicken.

01:54:06.840 --> 01:54:09.175
Ever since McDonald's
released peri-peri fries

01:54:09.175 --> 01:54:10.176
here in India,

01:54:10.176 --> 01:54:12.812
there has been a peri-peri
revolution over here.

01:54:12.812 --> 01:54:16.983
A peri-perevolution, as I like to call it.

01:54:16.983 --> 01:54:20.353
Lot of chicken, lot of
meat, not a lot of veggies.

01:54:20.353 --> 01:54:21.521
What happened here?

01:54:21.521 --> 01:54:22.922
Some olives would've been nice.

01:54:22.922 --> 01:54:25.658
And finally, this
rejected Subway over here

01:54:25.658 --> 01:54:29.662
is tandoori tofu, which I
refuse to eat on principle

01:54:29.662 --> 01:54:32.298
because we also have paneer over here.

01:54:32.298 --> 01:54:34.567
It looks pretty much the same,
and I'm sure it tastes great.

01:54:34.567 --> 01:54:35.635
You know what I realized?

01:54:35.635 --> 01:54:37.437
Subways opened up like this

01:54:37.437 --> 01:54:40.573
don't really look all that
great on camera, do they?

01:54:40.573 --> 01:54:41.541
Oh, my God.

01:54:41.541 --> 01:54:44.077
This looks like somebody's organs.

01:54:44.077 --> 01:54:45.678
US-exclusive sandwiches.

01:54:45.678 --> 01:54:46.746
You know what they say?

01:54:46.746 --> 01:54:48.648
Greatness is in the agency of others?

01:54:48.648 --> 01:54:50.683
Well, I'm here to say
greatness is in the agency

01:54:50.683 --> 01:54:52.452
of other sandwiches.

01:54:52.452 --> 01:54:54.954
I've tried almost none of these.

01:54:54.954 --> 01:54:55.955
Starting over down here,

01:54:55.955 --> 01:54:58.057
we have something called the mozza meat.

01:54:58.057 --> 01:54:59.525
Let's take a look at this, Yuelei.

01:54:59.525 --> 01:55:00.727
Oh, I don't think I've
ever seen this before.

01:55:00.727 --> 01:55:02.795
Look, they even got the little, like,

01:55:02.795 --> 01:55:05.365
the fresh mutzarel.

01:55:05.365 --> 01:55:08.301
Has what looks to be
all the Italian meats.

01:55:08.301 --> 01:55:12.005
Oh, by the way, unless otherwise
important to the sandwich,

01:55:12.005 --> 01:55:14.107
I got everything with
lettuce, tomato, and onion

01:55:14.107 --> 01:55:17.243
and no sauce unless it
includes a sauce. So.

01:55:17.243 --> 01:55:19.746
Some mercy on the people
who had to wake up

01:55:19.746 --> 01:55:21.180
two hours earlier to
make these sandwiches.

01:55:21.180 --> 01:55:23.316
It's just like, yeah, just put
the same junk on all of them.

01:55:23.316 --> 01:55:24.217
Moving on.

01:55:24.217 --> 01:55:25.919
Supreme meats.

01:55:25.919 --> 01:55:28.154
Oh, yeah. This is up my alley.

01:55:28.154 --> 01:55:32.325
Salami, the other salami,
ham. No turkey though, huh?

01:55:32.325 --> 01:55:34.928
Is this capocollo? What
is this? Provolone cheese.

01:55:34.928 --> 01:55:36.896
This is something that I
would probably get at Subway.

01:55:36.896 --> 01:55:39.565
The Baja turkey avocado.

01:55:39.565 --> 01:55:40.800
Gonna open it up for you here.

01:55:40.800 --> 01:55:42.435
Turkey. Oh, yeah, hey, they were generous

01:55:42.435 --> 01:55:43.836
with the avocado I think, right?

01:55:43.836 --> 01:55:45.138
Going right in the middle.

01:55:48.174 --> 01:55:49.776
No big deal.

01:55:49.776 --> 01:55:50.944
Moving on.

01:55:50.944 --> 01:55:54.013
Honey mustard rotisserie-style chicken.

01:55:56.516 --> 01:55:57.784
Oh, yeah.

01:55:57.784 --> 01:56:00.153
I like the flavor of that
better than the regular chicken.

01:56:00.153 --> 01:56:01.554
The all-American club.

01:56:01.554 --> 01:56:04.123
Ham, turkey, bacon.

01:56:04.123 --> 01:56:05.858
The Baja chicken and bacon.

01:56:07.493 --> 01:56:08.828
It was, like, weak.

01:56:10.229 --> 01:56:13.066
Even the bacon doesn't
have a lot of flavor.

01:56:13.066 --> 01:56:14.567
Let's get into the steak.

01:56:14.567 --> 01:56:16.869
Baja steak and Jack cheese.

01:56:16.869 --> 01:56:17.937
Black Forest ham.

01:56:19.072 --> 01:56:20.873
Buffalo chicken.

01:56:20.873 --> 01:56:22.308
Oh, yeah, look at that.

01:56:22.308 --> 01:56:23.943
Wow, they were generous
with the Buffalo sauce.

01:56:23.943 --> 01:56:26.379
Chicken bacon ranch.

01:56:30.550 --> 01:56:32.085
What does it say if the
strongest flavor in this

01:56:32.085 --> 01:56:33.353
is the tomatoes?

01:56:33.353 --> 01:56:35.421
You guys don't have the cold-cut combo?

01:56:35.421 --> 01:56:37.223
That looks like bologna.

01:56:37.223 --> 01:56:39.258
Then we have this next one.

01:56:39.258 --> 01:56:41.094
Whoa!

01:56:41.094 --> 01:56:43.262
The meatball, right?

01:56:43.262 --> 01:56:47.467
India, I assure you, this
tastes way better than it looks.

01:56:47.467 --> 01:56:50.069
Roast beef is, you guessed it, roast --

01:56:50.069 --> 01:56:52.705
oh, God, that turned the
bread pink. Is that normal?

01:56:52.705 --> 01:56:55.375
Ooh, spicy Italian. A favorite of mine.

01:56:55.375 --> 01:56:56.809
Two salamis, both spicy.

01:56:56.809 --> 01:56:58.745
You know, just like in Italy.

01:56:58.745 --> 01:57:00.279
The turkey Cali fresh.

01:57:00.279 --> 01:57:02.715
I think when something's a Cali sandwich,

01:57:02.715 --> 01:57:04.984
the Cali means bacon and avocado.

01:57:04.984 --> 01:57:08.955
The steak Cali fresh,

01:57:08.955 --> 01:57:12.892
which has, let me guess,
bacon and avocado?

01:57:12.892 --> 01:57:13.726
No.

01:57:13.726 --> 01:57:14.927
Ah, there's the bacon.

01:57:16.396 --> 01:57:18.965
So, unless I got COVID
in the past five minutes,

01:57:18.965 --> 01:57:22.168
the food at Subway has seemingly
become incredibly bland.

01:57:22.168 --> 01:57:23.803
Steak and cheese.

01:57:23.803 --> 01:57:26.939
[laughs] These steak
sandwiches are like bricks.

01:57:26.939 --> 01:57:29.108
Look at this. Oh, Yuelei!

01:57:29.108 --> 01:57:30.543
Yeesh.

01:57:30.543 --> 01:57:33.613
Now, there are some sandwiches
which appear on both menus

01:57:33.613 --> 01:57:35.948
but have little differences
when it comes to ingredients.

01:57:35.948 --> 01:57:39.252
For instance, our Subway
club comes with turkey,

01:57:39.252 --> 01:57:43.456
ham, and bacon, and our
Italian BMT has ham.

01:57:43.456 --> 01:57:46.893
In India, our Subway club
actually has turkey, lamb,

01:57:46.893 --> 01:57:50.396
and chicken slices, and our
BMT does not contain bacon.

01:57:50.396 --> 01:57:52.432
This is because most
fast-food outlets here

01:57:52.432 --> 01:57:54.700
don't serve ham or beef

01:57:54.700 --> 01:57:56.436
because it'll hurt the
religious sentiments

01:57:56.436 --> 01:57:57.670
of Hindus and Muslims.

01:57:57.670 --> 01:57:59.338
In addition to our sandwich fillings,

01:57:59.338 --> 01:58:01.474
we also have some differences
in our bread options.

01:58:01.474 --> 01:58:03.743
We have honey oat multigrain,

01:58:03.743 --> 01:58:05.378
we have roasted garlic,

01:58:05.378 --> 01:58:09.182
and Parmesan oregano Italian white bread,

01:58:09.182 --> 01:58:10.750
but this looks oddly similar

01:58:10.750 --> 01:58:13.586
to the American Italian cheese and herbs.

01:58:13.586 --> 01:58:15.088
Is it the same thing, Joe?

01:58:15.088 --> 01:58:15.988
Let me know.

01:58:15.988 --> 01:58:17.156
No.

01:58:17.156 --> 01:58:19.859
Here's the exclusive US
bread options at Subway.

01:58:19.859 --> 01:58:22.595
Cheddar jalapeño bread, gluten-free bread,

01:58:22.595 --> 01:58:24.797
tomato basil wrap, and hero bread.

01:58:24.797 --> 01:58:27.467
In both the US and India,
you can get any sandwich

01:58:27.467 --> 01:58:29.635
as a wrap or in a salad bowl.

01:58:29.635 --> 01:58:31.938
Other US-exclusive option is the melt.

01:58:31.938 --> 01:58:33.906
I wasn't going to get every single melt.

01:58:33.906 --> 01:58:35.074
The list goes as follows.

01:58:35.074 --> 01:58:38.211
Baja chicken and bacon melt,
chicken and bacon ranch melt,

01:58:38.211 --> 01:58:40.746
Baja steak and Jack melt,
Buffalo chicken melt,

01:58:40.746 --> 01:58:43.116
ham and cheese melt, Italian BMT melt,

01:58:43.116 --> 01:58:46.219
meatball marinara melt,
oven-roasted turkey melt,

01:58:46.219 --> 01:58:50.423
spiced Italian melt, steak and
cheese melt, and tuna melt.

01:58:50.423 --> 01:58:51.824
I went ahead and got two,

01:58:51.824 --> 01:58:54.727
steak melt, and, which one is --

01:58:54.727 --> 01:58:57.563
oh, brother, the tuna melt.

01:58:57.563 --> 01:58:59.499
Oh, God. It looks like cat food.

01:59:00.800 --> 01:59:02.268
[whimpers]

01:59:04.003 --> 01:59:05.471
All right, I definitely don't have COVID,

01:59:05.471 --> 01:59:06.472
'cause I tasted that.

01:59:06.472 --> 01:59:09.976
I need a steak-and-cheese-melt
palate cleanser after that.

01:59:09.976 --> 01:59:12.345
Uh-huh. Mm!

01:59:12.345 --> 01:59:13.279
Now we're talking.

01:59:13.279 --> 01:59:15.581
Here are our breakfast-sandwich options.

01:59:15.581 --> 01:59:17.783
We have egg and cheese,

01:59:17.783 --> 01:59:19.719
chicken slice, egg, and cheese,

01:59:19.719 --> 01:59:22.021
and Western egg and cheese.

01:59:22.021 --> 01:59:25.591
I am very curious to know
what makes this Western.

01:59:26.626 --> 01:59:28.227
Mm.

01:59:28.227 --> 01:59:30.696
I can see how this would
be a Western option.

01:59:30.696 --> 01:59:34.233
Nice, bland, easy on the palate.

01:59:34.233 --> 01:59:36.102
Let me tell you something
about India, all right?

01:59:36.102 --> 01:59:37.904
If you flavor something that we are buying

01:59:37.904 --> 01:59:40.139
at a restaurant with just salt and pepper,

01:59:40.139 --> 01:59:41.774
we call that a rip-off.

01:59:41.774 --> 01:59:44.777
At least 10 spices.

01:59:44.777 --> 01:59:48.114
For some inconceivable reason,

01:59:48.114 --> 01:59:50.650
you can get their breakfast sandwiches

01:59:50.650 --> 01:59:52.685
foot-long flatbreads.

01:59:52.685 --> 01:59:55.421
Oh, good God. This, and they're so greasy.

01:59:55.421 --> 01:59:56.455
[groans]

01:59:56.455 --> 01:59:57.423
Egg and cheese.

01:59:57.423 --> 01:59:59.926
Oh, look how terrible this looks.

01:59:59.926 --> 02:00:02.094
[laughs] Ah, oh, no!

02:00:02.094 --> 02:00:03.329
Where's the cheese? And, what?

02:00:03.329 --> 02:00:04.664
Oh, come on, man.

02:00:09.402 --> 02:00:10.603
Absolutely not.

02:00:11.537 --> 02:00:13.272
This really is a bummer.

02:00:14.507 --> 02:00:15.942
Oh, my God.

02:00:15.942 --> 02:00:17.710
[squelching]
Oh, did you hear that?

02:00:17.710 --> 02:00:19.612
I mean, these eggs, are
you kidding me with this?

02:00:19.612 --> 02:00:20.446
What?

02:00:25.151 --> 02:00:28.621
I couldn't imagine eating a
whole one of these for breakfast

02:00:28.621 --> 02:00:31.224
without going directly back to bed.

02:00:31.224 --> 02:00:33.526
There's a Black Forest
ham, egg, and cheese.

02:00:36.929 --> 02:00:38.297
Oh, God.

02:00:38.297 --> 02:00:41.634
And now let's never speak of
those breakfasts ever again.

02:00:41.634 --> 02:00:43.836
We have some exclusive
Subway toppings here

02:00:43.836 --> 02:00:48.040
in the US you cannot get
in India, such as spinach,

02:00:48.040 --> 02:00:50.076
banana peppers [groans],

02:00:50.076 --> 02:00:52.378
and Monterey cheddar cheese.

02:00:52.378 --> 02:00:53.746
According to the Subway website,

02:00:53.746 --> 02:00:57.216
in certain parts of the country
you can also get avocado,

02:00:57.216 --> 02:01:01.387
carrot, guacamole, sweet
peppers, feta cheese,

02:01:01.387 --> 02:01:05.524
Pepper Jack cheese, provolone
cheese, Swiss cheese.

02:01:05.524 --> 02:01:07.193
Here in India, unfortunately,

02:01:07.193 --> 02:01:10.596
all the toppings we have are
also available in the US.

02:01:10.596 --> 02:01:12.765
Dammit, Subway. Are we not special enough?

02:01:12.765 --> 02:01:14.700
Guys, let Subway know in the comments

02:01:14.700 --> 02:01:17.536
what special toppings we
should have here in India.

02:01:17.536 --> 02:01:20.840
However, we do have our
own exclusive sauces.

02:01:20.840 --> 02:01:22.308
Sauce talk.

02:01:22.308 --> 02:01:26.412
Starting with mint mayo,
which is absolutely a banger,

02:01:26.412 --> 02:01:28.714
and the entire world needs to taste this.

02:01:28.714 --> 02:01:30.616
Tandoori mayo, which we end up using

02:01:30.616 --> 02:01:32.218
because we overuse the mint mayo.

02:01:32.218 --> 02:01:34.120
This balances it out.

02:01:34.120 --> 02:01:36.856
And, finally, red chili sauce.

02:01:36.856 --> 02:01:38.658
I've also never heard of mint mayonnaise,

02:01:38.658 --> 02:01:40.159
and that sounds incredible, actually.

02:01:40.159 --> 02:01:42.995
So, in the US, we have a few
of our own exclusive sauces,

02:01:42.995 --> 02:01:45.364
such as ranch, oil,

02:01:45.364 --> 02:01:48.034
Subway vinaigrette, and plain mustard.

02:01:48.034 --> 02:01:49.435
You guys have honey mustard like us,

02:01:49.435 --> 02:01:50.569
but not plain mustard.

02:01:50.569 --> 02:01:52.371
And in certain locations
around the country

02:01:52.371 --> 02:01:55.641
you can also get Buffalo
sauce, creamy Italian sauce,

02:01:55.641 --> 02:01:59.312
golden Italian sauce,
savory Caesar, Sriracha,

02:01:59.312 --> 02:02:00.313
and, uh-oh.

02:02:01.380 --> 02:02:03.082
Taziki cucumber.
[buzzer rings]

02:02:03.082 --> 02:02:05.551
Taziki, or just, is the T silent? Ziki.

02:02:05.551 --> 02:02:07.086
Tzatziki cucumber.

02:02:07.086 --> 02:02:09.822
In my defense, I am incredibly nauseous.

02:02:09.822 --> 02:02:13.359
What if we took all of
the US-exclusive items

02:02:13.359 --> 02:02:14.860
and put them in one sandwich?

02:02:14.860 --> 02:02:17.430
Well, this time we're not
going to, and thank you.

02:02:17.430 --> 02:02:19.465
We actually made an effort

02:02:19.465 --> 02:02:23.469
to make an edible US-only sandwich.

02:02:23.469 --> 02:02:26.305
What we have is a steak
sub, cheddar jalapeño bread,

02:02:26.305 --> 02:02:29.275
with spinach, banana peppers,
Monterey Jack cheese,

02:02:29.275 --> 02:02:30.476
ranch, and mustard.

02:02:33.713 --> 02:02:34.647
Hm.

02:02:34.647 --> 02:02:36.415
This all works well together,

02:02:36.415 --> 02:02:37.817
except the mustard stands out,

02:02:37.817 --> 02:02:39.685
which is kind of a, mm,
could do without it.

02:02:39.685 --> 02:02:42.054
And the spinach is fine.
I don't taste the spinach.

02:02:42.054 --> 02:02:43.989
Guess it wouldn't kill me
to get some green in here.

02:02:43.989 --> 02:02:46.192
Now, what about an India-only sub?

02:02:46.192 --> 02:02:48.561
Here is one with the roast garlic bread,

02:02:48.561 --> 02:02:49.962
tandoori chicken tikka,

02:02:49.962 --> 02:02:53.399
mint mayo, tandoori mayo,
and red chili sauce.

02:02:55.801 --> 02:02:56.769
Mm.

02:02:56.769 --> 02:02:58.237
I'm really feeling the lack

02:02:58.237 --> 02:03:00.206
of exclusive toppings here, Subway.

02:03:00.206 --> 02:03:03.409
This is just meat dripping in sauce.

02:03:03.409 --> 02:03:07.980
Make India-exclusive toppings
happen right now, Subway.

02:03:07.980 --> 02:03:10.116
This is the "Eat Pray
Love" version of a sub,

02:03:10.116 --> 02:03:11.250
in the sense that it makes sense

02:03:11.250 --> 02:03:14.086
to everybody else in the
world except Indians.

02:03:14.086 --> 02:03:16.989
Moving away from subs, our
snack section will tell you

02:03:16.989 --> 02:03:19.925
that we have a pepperoni
toastie and a veggie toastie.

02:03:19.925 --> 02:03:22.161
Unfortunately, at the
time that we ordered,

02:03:22.161 --> 02:03:23.229
it was not available.

02:03:23.229 --> 02:03:24.830
I have tasted them before, though,

02:03:24.830 --> 02:03:26.732
and the pepperoni one is pretty yummy.

02:03:26.732 --> 02:03:28.934
Subway has potato chips, of course,

02:03:28.934 --> 02:03:31.771
and these are some US
exclusives, starting on this end.

02:03:31.771 --> 02:03:34.607
SunChips cheddar harvest.

02:03:34.607 --> 02:03:36.876
SunChips and Subway have always
had a really good alliance.

02:03:36.876 --> 02:03:38.043
Good for them.

02:03:38.043 --> 02:03:41.747
My favorite, Miss Vickie's.
The jalapeño chips.

02:03:41.747 --> 02:03:42.882
These things are so good.

02:03:42.882 --> 02:03:44.550
You can also get the Miss Vickie's

02:03:44.550 --> 02:03:46.218
lime and cracked pepper chips.

02:03:46.218 --> 02:03:48.721
The one I went to didn't have them.

02:03:48.721 --> 02:03:49.622
This I can't believe.

02:03:49.622 --> 02:03:51.957
You guys don't have the
nacho cheese Doritos?

02:03:51.957 --> 02:03:55.661
I mean, this is, like, the
most popular chip, right?

02:03:55.661 --> 02:03:58.831
And last, Lay's baked.

02:03:58.831 --> 02:04:02.334
And also, kids can get
a pouch of applesauce.

02:04:02.334 --> 02:04:03.869
I'm assuming adults can get it too,

02:04:03.869 --> 02:04:05.337
but they're technically for kids.

02:04:05.337 --> 02:04:08.107
In India, Subway's chip
options are a lot more limited,

02:04:08.107 --> 02:04:09.775
and they vary from store to store.

02:04:09.775 --> 02:04:12.678
The one we visited had
a variety of flavors

02:04:12.678 --> 02:04:16.282
in Cornitos, which are basically
nacho chips, and Lay's.

02:04:16.282 --> 02:04:18.651
And they had my personal
favorite Lay's flavor,

02:04:18.651 --> 02:04:20.419
West Indies hot and chili.

02:04:20.419 --> 02:04:22.688
But the crew has informed me
that they will not roll further

02:04:22.688 --> 02:04:25.791
if I don't give a shout-out
to India's Magic Masala.

02:04:27.226 --> 02:04:29.562
Our Subway cookies have
one exclusive flavor,

02:04:29.562 --> 02:04:32.398
and that is this, the
raspberry cheesecake.

02:04:33.566 --> 02:04:35.000
This is so good.

02:04:35.000 --> 02:04:36.101
I don't know how they do it.

02:04:36.101 --> 02:04:38.370
We sort of have an
exclusive here in India.

02:04:38.370 --> 02:04:40.306
In the US, you can get
a chocolate chip cookie,

02:04:40.306 --> 02:04:43.909
but here you can get dark
chocolate chunk cookie,

02:04:43.909 --> 02:04:46.612
or, if you really want
to join the dark side,

02:04:46.612 --> 02:04:49.315
a double dark chocolate cookie.

02:04:49.315 --> 02:04:50.583
Here at the Subway in the US,

02:04:50.583 --> 02:04:52.785
Coca-Cola rules everything around me.

02:04:52.785 --> 02:04:54.553
We got a lot of Coke products here.

02:04:54.553 --> 02:04:56.789
I put these in order of

02:04:56.789 --> 02:04:59.859
which one I would probably
want to have with a sandwich.

02:04:59.859 --> 02:05:00.693
Coke.

02:05:00.693 --> 02:05:02.761
Diet Coke. Not a big
diet guy, but it's like,

02:05:02.761 --> 02:05:03.996
eh, with the calories.

02:05:03.996 --> 02:05:04.864
Next is Sprite.

02:05:04.864 --> 02:05:06.765
I mean, who doesn't love
Sprite? It's a little strong.

02:05:06.765 --> 02:05:08.334
I don't know if it goes well
with a sandwich, but why not?

02:05:08.334 --> 02:05:10.769
Then we move on to the Simply drinks.

02:05:10.769 --> 02:05:12.605
You got yourself Simply lemonade.

02:05:12.605 --> 02:05:13.806
Who doesn't like lemonade, right?

02:05:13.806 --> 02:05:15.875
Simply orange juice. I
feel like this is more

02:05:15.875 --> 02:05:17.142
for the breakfast sandwiches, right?

02:05:17.142 --> 02:05:20.813
I mean, OJ after 11 a.m.
seems kind of strange to me.

02:05:20.813 --> 02:05:22.147
And then this apple juice.

02:05:22.147 --> 02:05:26.519
If you want to have an energy
drink with your sandwich,

02:05:26.519 --> 02:05:28.888
Vitaminwater XXX.

02:05:28.888 --> 02:05:30.656
And then Gatorade. Gatorade?

02:05:30.656 --> 02:05:32.491
Yeah, I mean, I like Gatorade, but,

02:05:32.491 --> 02:05:34.593
I mean, it doesn't pair with food at all.

02:05:34.593 --> 02:05:37.596
Last but not least,
all-natural-energy green tea,

02:05:37.596 --> 02:05:39.965
hydrated coconut water, antioxidants,

02:05:39.965 --> 02:05:43.235
electrolytes, with ribose.

02:05:43.235 --> 02:05:44.603
Let's find out.

02:05:48.107 --> 02:05:49.208
Whoa, that's terrible.

02:05:49.575 --> 02:05:50.676
This one smells like BO.

02:05:52.511 --> 02:05:55.214
Here in India, Subway's
actually partnered with PepsiCo.

02:05:55.214 --> 02:05:56.649
So instead of Coca-Cola products,

02:05:56.649 --> 02:06:00.853
you can get things like Pepsi,
Mountain Dew, Pepsi Black,

02:06:00.853 --> 02:06:03.822
Mirinda, Tropicana orange juice,

02:06:03.822 --> 02:06:06.058
and Aquavista water.

02:06:06.058 --> 02:06:07.626
"From the makers of Aquafina."

02:06:07.626 --> 02:06:10.162
That's so complicated. Why?

02:06:10.162 --> 02:06:12.298
It's like a movie title at this point.

02:06:14.833 --> 02:06:17.536
Which country is getting
a better deal on its subs?

02:06:17.536 --> 02:06:20.739
Let's compare a foot-long
turkey sub in both.

02:06:20.739 --> 02:06:25.210
In the US, this will cost you $8.99.

02:06:25.210 --> 02:06:28.447
In India, ordering a
foot-long turkey club sandwich

02:06:28.447 --> 02:06:30.449
on Zomato, one of our food-delivery apps,

02:06:30.449 --> 02:06:34.253
will cost you 476.19 rupees.

02:06:34.253 --> 02:06:36.956
That's around $6.27 right now.

02:06:36.956 --> 02:06:39.358
And while that's 30%
cheaper than the US sub,

02:06:39.358 --> 02:06:42.328
it's still pretty expensive
for the average Indian.

02:06:42.328 --> 02:06:44.063
For context, in under $7,

02:06:44.063 --> 02:06:46.332
you can feed an entire family of four,

02:06:46.332 --> 02:06:48.701
and you're going to get a
very delicious, hearty meal

02:06:48.701 --> 02:06:50.235
in most restaurants over here.

02:06:50.235 --> 02:06:51.804
Now, to play devil's advocate,

02:06:51.804 --> 02:06:54.740
the Subway near my college back in the day

02:06:54.740 --> 02:06:56.208
had a crazy deal going on

02:06:56.208 --> 02:06:59.244
where they gave us a 6-inch sub, a cookie,

02:06:59.244 --> 02:07:02.381
and a drink of our choice in under $2,

02:07:02.381 --> 02:07:05.150
and we used to eat lunch
there nearly every single day.

02:07:05.150 --> 02:07:08.921
So, I guess, from store to store
there are different offers,

02:07:08.921 --> 02:07:12.257
and Subway is and can
be kind of affordable.

02:07:12.257 --> 02:07:14.727
Subway prices have been
a contentious issue

02:07:14.727 --> 02:07:16.295
in America for a long time.

02:07:16.295 --> 02:07:20.466
A franchisee named Stuart
Frankel invented the $5 foot-long

02:07:20.466 --> 02:07:24.336
back in 2003, which hit
the mainstream in 2008.

02:07:24.336 --> 02:07:26.839
Cheaper labor and food costs
combined with an increase

02:07:26.839 --> 02:07:29.008
in foot traffic meant the
promotion was actually

02:07:29.008 --> 02:07:30.609
a huge earner for Subway.

02:07:30.609 --> 02:07:32.277
Sadly, it didn't last,

02:07:32.277 --> 02:07:35.080
and the deal was phased out around 2012.

02:07:35.080 --> 02:07:37.783
When Subway tried to
bring it back in 2017,

02:07:37.783 --> 02:07:41.020
it was met with uproar
from many franchisees

02:07:41.020 --> 02:07:42.621
who said it was impossible

02:07:42.621 --> 02:07:44.289
to make a profit from the promotion.

02:07:44.289 --> 02:07:46.158
The same thing happened again in 2020

02:07:46.158 --> 02:07:49.495
when Subway tried to push a
$10-for-two-foot-longs deal,

02:07:49.495 --> 02:07:51.530
which was killed after two weeks.

02:07:54.633 --> 02:07:56.835
Which country's Subway
is the most unhealthy?

02:07:56.835 --> 02:07:58.804
Let's start with a foot-long turkey sub

02:07:58.804 --> 02:08:00.339
on whole-grain bread with lettuce,

02:08:00.339 --> 02:08:03.375
tomato, onion, peppers, and cucumbers.

02:08:03.375 --> 02:08:06.712
In the US, this sandwich
contains 520 calories,

02:08:06.712 --> 02:08:09.748
6 grams of total fat, 2
grams of saturated fat,

02:08:09.748 --> 02:08:12.551
78 grams of carbs, of which 12 are sugars,

02:08:12.551 --> 02:08:15.054
and 1,580 milligrams of sodium.

02:08:15.054 --> 02:08:16.755
In India, the nutritional information

02:08:16.755 --> 02:08:19.758
for this same sandwich is 586 calories,

02:08:19.758 --> 02:08:22.928
6 grams of total fat, 4
grams of saturated fat,

02:08:22.928 --> 02:08:26.131
94 grams of carbs, of
which 8 grams are sugars,

02:08:26.131 --> 02:08:29.601
and 1,362 milligrams of sodium.

02:08:29.601 --> 02:08:33.739
When you break food down like
this, it sounds pretty scary.

02:08:33.739 --> 02:08:36.241
So, the US sandwich has more sugar

02:08:36.241 --> 02:08:37.976
and more sodium than the Indian version,

02:08:37.976 --> 02:08:41.280
but they have the same total fat content.

02:08:41.280 --> 02:08:42.948
I don't know what to take from that.

02:08:42.948 --> 02:08:45.951
But the Indian version has
more calories, saturated fats,

02:08:45.951 --> 02:08:48.253
and carbohydrates than the US version.

02:08:48.253 --> 02:08:51.423
My theory is because we
have that extra inch.

02:08:51.423 --> 02:08:53.358
What's the most calorific
thing on the US menu?

02:08:53.358 --> 02:08:56.261
Currently, it's a foot-long
Cali fresh steak sub

02:08:56.261 --> 02:08:59.031
with smashed avocado.
On whole Italian bread,

02:08:59.031 --> 02:09:02.267
one of these is a hefty 1,220 calories.

02:09:02.267 --> 02:09:05.337
There is also 68 grams of fat in there,

02:09:05.337 --> 02:09:08.674
87% of your daily allowance,

02:09:08.674 --> 02:09:12.144
as well as 2,380 milligrams of sodium,

02:09:12.144 --> 02:09:14.813
over 100% of your daily allowance.

02:09:14.813 --> 02:09:17.516
The most calorific thing
on the Indian Subway menu

02:09:17.516 --> 02:09:20.319
is this: paneer tikka sub,

02:09:20.319 --> 02:09:23.555
foot-long, whole-wheat
bread with standard salad.

02:09:23.555 --> 02:09:26.725
It's a whopping 820 calories.

02:09:26.725 --> 02:09:29.762
Now, this is less calorific
than the American Cali steak sub

02:09:29.762 --> 02:09:31.697
and contains significantly less fat,

02:09:31.697 --> 02:09:34.566
at just 41% of your
recommended daily intake.

02:09:34.566 --> 02:09:36.468
The main thing to watch out for, however,

02:09:36.468 --> 02:09:37.936
is the saturated fat.

02:09:37.936 --> 02:09:39.571
There's 16 grams of it in here,

02:09:39.571 --> 02:09:42.808
which is 80% of your
recommended daily intake.

02:09:42.808 --> 02:09:45.844
Oh, saturated fats, you sly dog.

02:09:46.311 --> 02:09:47.913
Nikhil: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

02:09:47.913 --> 02:09:49.515
we wanted to find out all the differences

02:09:49.515 --> 02:09:51.884
between Burger King in India and the US.

02:09:51.884 --> 02:09:53.619
This is "Food Wars."

02:09:57.055 --> 02:09:59.992
In Burger King India, our drinks
come in one standard size,

02:09:59.992 --> 02:10:02.261
which looks to be your small or medium,

02:10:02.261 --> 02:10:05.764
but you can also opt for a can of 330 ml.

02:10:05.764 --> 02:10:09.334
Burger King in the US, our
drinks come in four sizes.

02:10:09.334 --> 02:10:11.637
Value, small,

02:10:11.637 --> 02:10:13.806
medium, and large.

02:10:15.240 --> 02:10:16.341
Let's measure this cup to see

02:10:16.341 --> 02:10:17.609
how much is actually in here.

02:10:17.609 --> 02:10:19.845
Does this make anybody else want to pee,

02:10:19.845 --> 02:10:21.213
or is it just me?

02:10:21.213 --> 02:10:22.447
Joe: 34 ounces.

02:10:22.447 --> 02:10:24.249
Well, it says 38 at the bottom of the cup.

02:10:24.249 --> 02:10:25.884
It ain't 38.

02:10:25.884 --> 02:10:28.921
Our Burger King fries come in two sizes,

02:10:28.921 --> 02:10:31.757
medium and king.

02:10:31.757 --> 02:10:33.125
[angelic singing]

02:10:33.125 --> 02:10:34.793
Our fries come in four sizes.

02:10:34.793 --> 02:10:36.829
Value, small,

02:10:36.829 --> 02:10:38.564
medium, large.

02:10:39.865 --> 02:10:41.867
I remember the large
being bigger than this.

02:10:41.867 --> 02:10:44.736
I'm just glad that the fuss we rose

02:10:44.736 --> 02:10:48.574
for the first UK-US
"Food Wars" Burger King

02:10:48.574 --> 02:10:52.277
has resulted fry transparency.

02:10:52.277 --> 02:10:53.912
Next up, chicken fries.

02:10:53.912 --> 02:10:54.847
I didn't know this was a thing,

02:10:54.847 --> 02:10:56.748
so I'm very excited to eat them.

02:10:56.748 --> 02:10:58.083
It should have five pieces.

02:10:58.083 --> 02:10:59.351
Three.

02:10:59.351 --> 02:11:00.586
Four.

02:11:00.586 --> 02:11:01.520
Five.

02:11:01.520 --> 02:11:02.888
Six!

02:11:02.888 --> 02:11:04.356
Thank you, Burger King!

02:11:05.591 --> 02:11:06.592
Oh, never mind.

02:11:06.592 --> 02:11:08.861
One of the fries had
broken. They gave me five.

02:11:08.861 --> 02:11:12.197
Ours also is one size. Nine chicken fries.

02:11:12.197 --> 02:11:15.467
It's like a pack of chicken cigarettes.

02:11:15.467 --> 02:11:17.469
Seven, eight, nine.

02:11:17.469 --> 02:11:18.804
A nice brown on brown.

02:11:18.804 --> 02:11:21.039
Yeah. We thought ahead for this one.

02:11:21.039 --> 02:11:23.242
Next one we shoot, I'm wearing all brown.

02:11:23.242 --> 02:11:24.543
I'm wearing a brown jumpsuit.

02:11:24.543 --> 02:11:26.078
We're gonna paint this brown.

02:11:26.078 --> 02:11:27.279
The most unwatchable series.

02:11:28.513 --> 02:11:29.948
Here's everything you'll find on the menu

02:11:29.948 --> 02:11:32.851
at Burger King India that
you won't find in the US.

02:11:32.851 --> 02:11:35.520
And here's everything you
can get at a US Burger King

02:11:35.520 --> 02:11:37.055
you can't get in India.

02:11:37.055 --> 02:11:39.625
Let's begin with the Whoppers!

02:11:39.625 --> 02:11:41.426
This is a good time to
mention that here in India,

02:11:41.426 --> 02:11:44.830
most fast-food restaurants
do not serve beef or pork

02:11:44.830 --> 02:11:47.699
to keep the religious sentiments
of both Hindus and Muslims.

02:11:47.699 --> 02:11:48.901
Conservative Hindus will not

02:11:48.901 --> 02:11:50.402
enter a restaurant that serves beef.

02:11:50.402 --> 02:11:51.770
Conservative Muslims might not

02:11:51.770 --> 02:11:53.672
enter a restaurant that serves pork.

02:11:53.672 --> 02:11:55.140
All right. Keeping all of that in mind,

02:11:55.140 --> 02:11:57.709
let us begin with the chicken Whopper.

02:11:57.709 --> 02:11:59.511
Whoo, boy!

02:11:59.511 --> 02:12:02.314
OK, Burger King definitely
has larger burgers

02:12:02.314 --> 02:12:04.283
than most other restaurants here in India.

02:12:04.283 --> 02:12:06.084
Look at this. It's the size of my face.

02:12:06.084 --> 02:12:07.386
I am the Burger King.

02:12:09.855 --> 02:12:10.889
That's so good.

02:12:10.889 --> 02:12:12.591
You might notice if you are a regular

02:12:12.591 --> 02:12:15.360
Burger King consumer of the foreign lands

02:12:15.360 --> 02:12:17.062
that if you were to eat this one,

02:12:17.062 --> 02:12:18.597
it's a little spicier.

02:12:18.597 --> 02:12:19.798
And I think they've done that

02:12:19.798 --> 02:12:21.767
because most Indians love their spice.

02:12:21.767 --> 02:12:23.101
There's a lot of bite to it.

02:12:23.101 --> 02:12:25.470
Next up, double chicken patty.

02:12:25.470 --> 02:12:27.839
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa!

02:12:27.839 --> 02:12:30.175
This one's got some heft to it, huh?

02:12:30.175 --> 02:12:32.210
The mutton Whopper.

02:12:32.210 --> 02:12:34.579
Mutton, if you are unaware, is goat meat,

02:12:34.579 --> 02:12:37.115
and Burger King is one of
the few fast-food chains here

02:12:37.115 --> 02:12:39.484
that actually serves
red meat of some kind.

02:12:39.484 --> 02:12:40.752
Indians love their mutton.

02:12:40.752 --> 02:12:41.887
I love my mutton.

02:12:43.622 --> 02:12:45.924
It's definitely more meaty.

02:12:45.924 --> 02:12:48.060
Has a lot more bite to
it than the chicken.

02:12:48.060 --> 02:12:49.695
God, Burger King, what are you doing?

02:12:49.695 --> 02:12:51.663
The quality is out of control.

02:12:51.663 --> 02:12:56.001
Every beef burger at Burger
King is a US exclusive.

02:12:56.001 --> 02:12:57.269
Got all the Whoppers.

02:12:57.269 --> 02:12:59.037
Let's start down here.

02:12:59.037 --> 02:13:02.107
The little guy, the Whopper Jr.

02:13:02.107 --> 02:13:03.275
Not enough meat, you say?

02:13:03.275 --> 02:13:04.876
You can get yourself a double Whopper.

02:13:04.876 --> 02:13:06.712
Same burger, two patties.

02:13:06.712 --> 02:13:08.613
Can they go bigger? They can.

02:13:08.613 --> 02:13:11.016
The triple Whopper.

02:13:11.016 --> 02:13:12.884
Look at this thing.

02:13:12.884 --> 02:13:14.019
Hey.

02:13:14.019 --> 02:13:16.121
Close your mouth when
you're taking a picture.

02:13:16.121 --> 02:13:17.556
The Texans of the audience

02:13:17.556 --> 02:13:19.224
might have to help us
out in the comments here.

02:13:19.224 --> 02:13:20.826
The Texas double Whopper.

02:13:20.826 --> 02:13:22.861
Texas prides itself, from what I can tell,

02:13:22.861 --> 02:13:23.962
on always going bigger.

02:13:23.962 --> 02:13:26.098
So why wouldn't it be
the Texas triple Whopper?

02:13:26.098 --> 02:13:29.167
A rare moment where Texas was reserved.

02:13:31.203 --> 02:13:33.271
Texans of the internet,

02:13:33.271 --> 02:13:34.940
I think you guys need to step in here.

02:13:34.940 --> 02:13:37.042
I don't think that sandwich
is doing you guys proud.

02:13:37.042 --> 02:13:38.877
On to the veg options.

02:13:38.877 --> 02:13:40.946
This is a veg Whopper.

02:13:40.946 --> 02:13:43.582
I expect great things from this bad boy.

02:13:44.683 --> 02:13:46.952
I would say this is pretty lackluster.

02:13:46.952 --> 02:13:50.088
Next up, veggie double burger,

02:13:50.088 --> 02:13:51.890
if you want double the disappointment.

02:13:51.890 --> 02:13:54.459
Another thing that we have
that technically isn't beef

02:13:54.459 --> 02:13:55.794
is the Impossible Whopper,

02:13:55.794 --> 02:13:57.863
which is made with Impossible beef.

02:13:57.863 --> 02:13:58.964
I'm actually very curious,

02:13:58.964 --> 02:14:02.134
how does the Impossible
burger patty taste, Joe?

02:14:02.134 --> 02:14:03.168
Regular beef.

02:14:06.471 --> 02:14:08.407
I have to hand it to them.
It tastes exactly the same.

02:14:08.407 --> 02:14:10.442
If you want to give the
environment a break,

02:14:10.442 --> 02:14:11.910
maybe get one of these
every once in a while.

02:14:11.910 --> 02:14:16.615
Next up, we have an exclusive
King collection of burgers.

02:14:16.615 --> 02:14:20.685
These better be quite
royal and aristocratic.

02:14:20.685 --> 02:14:24.122
No. 1, Hot 'n' Cheezy veg.

02:14:24.122 --> 02:14:26.425
Lot of jalapeños.

02:14:28.293 --> 02:14:30.762
The patty actually has,
like, cheese melt in it.

02:14:30.762 --> 02:14:32.297
Hot 'n' Cheezy Kings collection,

02:14:32.297 --> 02:14:36.535
on a scale of common
villager to the king himself,

02:14:36.535 --> 02:14:39.204
I would rate this village bard.

02:14:39.204 --> 02:14:40.038
Once in a while

02:14:40.038 --> 02:14:42.641
you want him there just
to appease a few people,

02:14:42.641 --> 02:14:45.644
but otherwise pretty lackluster.

02:14:45.644 --> 02:14:47.913
Paneer Royale.

02:14:47.913 --> 02:14:50.515
Just by the name itself,

02:14:50.515 --> 02:14:53.118
this one should be incredible.

02:14:53.118 --> 02:14:55.854
So, paneer, if you don't
know, is cottage cheese,

02:14:55.854 --> 02:14:58.523
and here in India, it is almost a staple.

02:14:58.523 --> 02:15:00.192
We eat it in everything.
We eat it in curries.

02:15:00.192 --> 02:15:02.494
We sometimes just sear
it and eat it plain.

02:15:02.494 --> 02:15:04.896
And obviously it had to
make its way to burgers.

02:15:07.399 --> 02:15:10.769
The paneer is really
good. Chewy and delicious.

02:15:10.769 --> 02:15:13.738
I would rate the Paneer Royale

02:15:13.738 --> 02:15:15.073
a local baron.

02:15:15.073 --> 02:15:17.042
Helps the king around a little bit.

02:15:17.042 --> 02:15:20.479
Now on to the two non-veg
options. We have fiery chicken.

02:15:20.479 --> 02:15:21.947
Plain and simple.

02:15:21.947 --> 02:15:24.216
They just want this meat to blow my mind.

02:15:25.684 --> 02:15:27.652
It's just spicy. That's all it is.

02:15:27.652 --> 02:15:29.387
It doesn't have the depth of flavor

02:15:29.387 --> 02:15:30.989
that the chicken Whoppers did.

02:15:30.989 --> 02:15:31.823
Chicken tandoori.

02:15:31.823 --> 02:15:33.525
If you guys don't know what a tandoor is,

02:15:33.525 --> 02:15:36.461
it's basically this cylindrical oven

02:15:36.461 --> 02:15:39.898
that we heat up using wood fire
and charcoal traditionally,

02:15:39.898 --> 02:15:43.902
and we use it to create
everything from kebabs to breads.

02:15:43.902 --> 02:15:45.604
I doubt all Burger King outlets

02:15:45.604 --> 02:15:47.439
have an actual tandoor
in their restaurants,

02:15:47.439 --> 02:15:48.673
but let's see if they were able

02:15:48.673 --> 02:15:50.442
to replicate that smoky flavor.

02:15:51.910 --> 02:15:56.882
On a scale of absolute
street urchins to maharajas,

02:15:56.882 --> 02:16:00.252
I would rate these two court traitors

02:16:00.252 --> 02:16:03.488
that tried to backstab the
king, and now they're on trial.

02:16:03.488 --> 02:16:06.324
They have a lot of bark
but not enough bite.

02:16:06.324 --> 02:16:07.959
They're gonna be executed.

02:16:07.959 --> 02:16:10.495
Non-Whopper burgers, aka burgers.

02:16:10.495 --> 02:16:12.330
You can get yourself
something called the Big King.

02:16:12.330 --> 02:16:14.065
And that's what it looks
like. Don't have it.

02:16:14.065 --> 02:16:17.736
What we do have is the
single quarter-pound King.

02:16:17.736 --> 02:16:19.337
Bacon King!

02:16:19.337 --> 02:16:21.173
I would say generous amount of bacon.

02:16:22.374 --> 02:16:23.208
It's great.

02:16:23.208 --> 02:16:25.777
Then these little, much more
reasonable-size burgers.

02:16:25.777 --> 02:16:26.745
Bacon cheeseburger.

02:16:26.745 --> 02:16:28.046
Bacon double cheeseburger.

02:16:28.046 --> 02:16:30.315
A bacon-free double cheeseburger, right?

02:16:30.315 --> 02:16:32.717
One of the most hilarious
things on the Burger King menu

02:16:32.717 --> 02:16:33.885
is, of course, the Rodeo burger,

02:16:33.885 --> 02:16:35.987
a burger with barbecue
sauce and onion rings,

02:16:35.987 --> 02:16:37.389
because why not?

02:16:37.389 --> 02:16:38.423
Then you got cheeseburger.

02:16:38.423 --> 02:16:40.392
Regular dry-ass hamburger.

02:16:40.392 --> 02:16:41.426
Who cares?

02:16:41.426 --> 02:16:42.827
Enough kingly sandwiches.

02:16:42.827 --> 02:16:44.229
It's now time for the regular

02:16:44.229 --> 02:16:46.264
vegetarian options that they have.

02:16:46.264 --> 02:16:48.233
We have crispy veg.

02:16:48.233 --> 02:16:49.267
Crispy veg double.

02:16:49.267 --> 02:16:51.236
Crispy veg with cheese.

02:16:51.236 --> 02:16:52.504
BK classic.

02:16:52.504 --> 02:16:54.406
BK classic with cheese.

02:16:54.406 --> 02:16:56.341
Lite Whopper Jr.

02:16:56.341 --> 02:16:58.810
And Lite Whopper Jr. with cheese.

02:16:58.810 --> 02:17:01.646
Why is it called Lite Whopper Jr.?

02:17:01.646 --> 02:17:03.982
How many more things do
you need to add to the name

02:17:03.982 --> 02:17:05.317
to make it seem small?

02:17:05.317 --> 02:17:10.255
Mini lite small Whopper
junior kindergartner burger.

02:17:10.255 --> 02:17:12.290
How about that next time, Burger King?

02:17:12.290 --> 02:17:14.025
OK, I don't want to try
any more veg burgers,

02:17:14.025 --> 02:17:17.095
but this one, the BK classic
veg, seems different.

02:17:17.095 --> 02:17:19.064
Like, the bun looks to be the same,

02:17:19.064 --> 02:17:22.667
but they've definitely
used more perky buns here.

02:17:22.667 --> 02:17:25.737
Don't use that audio clip out of context.

02:17:27.205 --> 02:17:29.107
OK. Finally.

02:17:29.107 --> 02:17:30.408
If you're a vegetarian,

02:17:30.408 --> 02:17:34.246
I would recommend the
BK classic with cheese.

02:17:34.246 --> 02:17:35.113
Boom.

02:17:35.113 --> 02:17:36.982
Although it is currently
for a limited time,

02:17:36.982 --> 02:17:38.550
I thought I would share with
you guys, here in the US,

02:17:38.550 --> 02:17:42.587
we have the Southwest
options at Burger King,

02:17:42.587 --> 02:17:45.523
starting with the Southwest bacon Jr.

02:17:45.523 --> 02:17:46.791
Southwest Whopper.

02:17:46.791 --> 02:17:48.760
The Southwest Impossible Whopper.

02:17:48.760 --> 02:17:50.362
What makes a Southwest?

02:17:50.362 --> 02:17:52.731
Ooh, I'm seeing, like,
crispy little chippy guys.

02:17:52.731 --> 02:17:54.399
Ooh, spicy. Ooh, it's got some heat to it.

02:17:54.399 --> 02:17:56.468
Yeah, there's guacamole on here. Hang on.

02:17:58.203 --> 02:17:59.604
I kinda fuck with it.

02:17:59.604 --> 02:18:02.307
I wouldn't eat if I didn't
work at "Food Wars," you know?

02:18:02.307 --> 02:18:04.242
And now for the chicken sandwiches.

02:18:04.242 --> 02:18:07.312
These look so tiny
compared to the Whoppers.

02:18:07.312 --> 02:18:09.514
We have crispy chicken.

02:18:09.514 --> 02:18:10.849
Crispy chicken double.

02:18:10.849 --> 02:18:12.717
Crispy chicken with cheese.

02:18:12.717 --> 02:18:14.352
BK classic chicken.

02:18:14.352 --> 02:18:16.621
Spicy grill chicken.

02:18:16.621 --> 02:18:19.758
Big smoky grill chicken.

02:18:19.758 --> 02:18:22.594
Lite Whopper chicken Jr.

02:18:22.594 --> 02:18:24.162
Lite Whopper double chicken Jr.

02:18:24.162 --> 02:18:28.199
And Lite Whopper chicken Jr. with cheese.

02:18:29.134 --> 02:18:32.103
Yes! I could work at
Burger King right now.

02:18:32.103 --> 02:18:33.772
We're going to try just
two of these burgers

02:18:33.772 --> 02:18:35.440
just to see if they're any different.

02:18:35.440 --> 02:18:39.044
First one, the spicy grill chicken.

02:18:40.412 --> 02:18:41.313
Oh, my God.

02:18:41.313 --> 02:18:43.982
I can imagine myself
going to a drive-through,

02:18:43.982 --> 02:18:45.717
taking one of these, driving to work,

02:18:45.717 --> 02:18:47.519
sitting in Silk Board traffic,

02:18:47.519 --> 02:18:49.854
getting annoyed with all
the other people honking,

02:18:49.854 --> 02:18:51.856
realizing I should have
gotten a bigger burger,

02:18:51.856 --> 02:18:54.225
and next day, ordering two. Nice.

02:18:54.225 --> 02:18:58.463
Next up, the big smoky grill chicken.

02:19:00.498 --> 02:19:02.233
I don't see how this is smoky at all.

02:19:02.233 --> 02:19:04.069
In fact, it's kind of sweet.

02:19:04.069 --> 02:19:07.972
On to the non-beef options.

02:19:07.972 --> 02:19:09.874
I personally think these
new Ch'King sandwiches

02:19:09.874 --> 02:19:11.009
are fantastic.

02:19:11.009 --> 02:19:12.644
The Ch'King,

02:19:12.644 --> 02:19:15.780
that's C-H-apostrophe-King,
because it's Burger King.

02:19:15.780 --> 02:19:18.316
Spicy Ch'King sandwich. Same thing.

02:19:18.316 --> 02:19:20.418
Got some spicy sauce on
it. This is very good.

02:19:20.418 --> 02:19:22.587
If you like these but
want a little more veggies

02:19:22.587 --> 02:19:24.589
because you're some old fogy,

02:19:24.589 --> 02:19:26.157
here you go, vegetables.

02:19:26.157 --> 02:19:27.759
They also make the Ch'King deluxe.

02:19:27.759 --> 02:19:29.494
Deluxe equals lettuce and tomato.

02:19:29.494 --> 02:19:33.531
This car crash of a
sandwich is the spicy ...

02:19:33.531 --> 02:19:36.034
actually, the spicy with veggies
is actually kind of nice.

02:19:36.034 --> 02:19:37.502
The coolness of the lettuce

02:19:37.502 --> 02:19:41.139
and the tomato actually
counterbalances the spice.

02:19:41.139 --> 02:19:43.541
The original chicken sandwich,

02:19:43.541 --> 02:19:46.077
shaped like the new iPhone
for some strange reason.

02:19:46.077 --> 02:19:47.145
This guy's been around forever.

02:19:47.145 --> 02:19:48.313
It's their answer to the McChicken.

02:19:48.313 --> 02:19:50.014
It tastes exactly like a McChicken.

02:19:50.014 --> 02:19:52.083
Chicken Jr. Look at this little guy.

02:19:52.083 --> 02:19:53.718
A spicy chicken Jr.

02:19:53.718 --> 02:19:57.389
And last, the only non-chicken
thing in the chicken section

02:19:57.389 --> 02:19:58.957
is the big fish.

02:19:58.957 --> 02:20:00.191
And now for a set of snacks

02:20:00.191 --> 02:20:02.560
that comes under their Stunner menu.

02:20:03.795 --> 02:20:06.264
[whistling]

02:20:06.264 --> 02:20:08.833
We have King egg burger.

02:20:08.833 --> 02:20:10.368
King egg wrap.

02:20:10.368 --> 02:20:12.036
Crispy veg wrap.

02:20:12.036 --> 02:20:14.305
Veg crunchy volcano.

02:20:14.305 --> 02:20:16.441
That's right. This is not even a wrap.

02:20:16.441 --> 02:20:19.344
This is a little geological formation.

02:20:19.344 --> 02:20:20.879
Tikki Twist burger.

02:20:20.879 --> 02:20:22.313
Veg makhani burger.

02:20:22.313 --> 02:20:24.582
And chicken makhani burger.

02:20:24.582 --> 02:20:26.217
And finally, crispy chicken wrap

02:20:26.217 --> 02:20:28.853
and crunch chicken volcano.

02:20:28.853 --> 02:20:30.321
All right, the first burger we're trying

02:20:30.321 --> 02:20:32.390
is the chicken makhani burger.

02:20:32.390 --> 02:20:35.126
So, makhan means butter,

02:20:35.126 --> 02:20:37.262
and it also means a lot to us Indians.

02:20:37.262 --> 02:20:39.397
You just walk into a room
and you say "makhan,"

02:20:39.397 --> 02:20:40.732
it will resound through the room.

02:20:40.732 --> 02:20:42.467
Like, people's eyes will perk up.

02:20:42.467 --> 02:20:44.669
The hairs on their arms will rise.

02:20:46.171 --> 02:20:48.940
Oh, my God, yeah ... mm.

02:20:48.940 --> 02:20:50.308
OK, so they've gone for, like,

02:20:50.308 --> 02:20:53.411
a butter chicken, more makhani flavor,

02:20:53.411 --> 02:20:55.680
but it just tastes like tomato puree

02:20:55.680 --> 02:20:58.116
over a stale chicken patty.

02:20:58.116 --> 02:21:02.754
Next thing that I really want
to try is the volcano itself.

02:21:02.754 --> 02:21:05.557
And I think this is their answer
to Taco Bell's Crunchwrap.

02:21:07.258 --> 02:21:09.360
Oh, that's pretty good.

02:21:09.360 --> 02:21:11.863
You were this close to
offending two communities

02:21:11.863 --> 02:21:14.466
and Mother Earth herself, but pretty good.

02:21:14.466 --> 02:21:17.335
Next thing I'm going to
try is an Aloo Tikki Twist.

02:21:17.335 --> 02:21:18.770
Tikki Twist sounds like a cocktail,

02:21:18.770 --> 02:21:21.239
but aloo tikki is actually,

02:21:21.239 --> 02:21:24.209
it's like mashed potato
fried with breadcrumbs,

02:21:24.209 --> 02:21:25.443
and it's used in chaats.

02:21:25.443 --> 02:21:27.145
It's used in a lot of other dishes.

02:21:27.145 --> 02:21:31.816
And they put these crispy
shards of what seems to be

02:21:31.816 --> 02:21:35.220
the same material in the volcano!

02:21:35.220 --> 02:21:36.454
["The X-Files" music]

02:21:36.454 --> 02:21:38.323
Illuminati confirmed.

02:21:39.424 --> 02:21:43.027
On to breakfasts!

02:21:43.027 --> 02:21:45.697
We got breakfast at the BK in the US.

02:21:45.697 --> 02:21:48.066
You can get an assortment
of Croissan'wiches,

02:21:48.066 --> 02:21:49.801
biscuits, melts.

02:21:49.801 --> 02:21:51.069
I didn't get all of them.

02:21:51.069 --> 02:21:52.003
Starting down here.

02:21:52.003 --> 02:21:53.972
A Croissan'wich, of course, for
those of you not in America,

02:21:53.972 --> 02:21:58.443
is they took a croissant
and stuffed eggs and cheese

02:21:58.443 --> 02:21:59.944
and your choice of breakfast meat.

02:21:59.944 --> 02:22:01.513
Bacon, egg, and cheese croissant.

02:22:01.513 --> 02:22:03.114
Sausage, egg, and cheese croissant.

02:22:03.114 --> 02:22:05.250
Ham, egg, and cheese croissant.

02:22:05.250 --> 02:22:06.784
Bacon, egg, and cheese biscuit.

02:22:06.784 --> 02:22:08.453
Sausage, egg, and cheese biscuit.

02:22:08.453 --> 02:22:10.054
Ham, egg, and cheese biscuit.

02:22:10.054 --> 02:22:11.723
Cheesy ham breakfast melt.

02:22:11.723 --> 02:22:13.424
Sausage and cheese breakfast melt.

02:22:13.424 --> 02:22:15.293
Cheesy bacon breakfast melt.

02:22:15.293 --> 02:22:18.129
And for both the Croissan'wiches
and the biscuits,

02:22:18.129 --> 02:22:20.932
you can also get pretty
much every combination

02:22:20.932 --> 02:22:25.169
of meat, egg, and cheese on
said biscuit or Croissan'wich.

02:22:25.169 --> 02:22:26.704
Egg-normous burrito.

02:22:26.704 --> 02:22:27.772
Ah, no, no, no, no, no.

02:22:27.772 --> 02:22:30.208
I am not starting off my morning
with this. No, thank you.

02:22:30.208 --> 02:22:32.343
This looks like a dirty diaper.

02:22:32.343 --> 02:22:33.878
Like, what is any of this?

02:22:33.878 --> 02:22:35.380
I feel like if I bit this,

02:22:35.380 --> 02:22:37.181
like, one bite of this in the morning,

02:22:37.181 --> 02:22:38.416
and I'm on the toilet.

02:22:38.416 --> 02:22:40.084
Get yourself two platters.

02:22:40.084 --> 02:22:41.886
Sausage and pancakes platter.

02:22:41.886 --> 02:22:44.022
And this one, I think, is,
like, the platter deluxe.

02:22:44.022 --> 02:22:45.189
You get yourself pancakes,

02:22:45.189 --> 02:22:46.224
get yourself bacon,

02:22:46.224 --> 02:22:47.225
get yourself eggs,

02:22:47.225 --> 02:22:48.693
and, of course, syrup.

02:22:48.693 --> 02:22:50.628
Next up, chicken wings.

02:22:50.628 --> 02:22:53.164
Burger King here sells
boneless chicken wings.

02:22:53.164 --> 02:22:54.699
They feel like chicken tenders.

02:22:56.000 --> 02:22:57.735
They're super meaty.
It's like proper chicken.

02:22:57.735 --> 02:23:00.171
It's not like that processed, nuggety

02:23:00.171 --> 02:23:02.574
chicken-juice thing that happens.

02:23:02.574 --> 02:23:05.209
In the US, our Burger King has nuggets,

02:23:05.209 --> 02:23:09.647
and they come in four
pieces and eight pieces.

02:23:09.647 --> 02:23:14.052
I asked the Burger King
employees about the 16-piece,

02:23:14.052 --> 02:23:16.521
and they said they don't have a 16-piece.

02:23:16.521 --> 02:23:18.790
They just give you two eight-pieces.

02:23:18.790 --> 02:23:22.060
Now it's time for Burger
King India sides and sauces.

02:23:22.060 --> 02:23:24.562
No. 1, we have the
classic peri-peri fries.

02:23:24.562 --> 02:23:26.164
They give it to you with a little sachet

02:23:26.164 --> 02:23:29.133
of the peri-peri powder
and a little shake bag.

02:23:29.133 --> 02:23:30.568
Pour it in there.

02:23:32.403 --> 02:23:37.408
Voilà! Your simple plain
fries are now peri-peried.

02:23:37.709 --> 02:23:39.043
Hm.

02:23:39.043 --> 02:23:40.979
Go with McDonald's peri-peri fries.

02:23:40.979 --> 02:23:42.213
I'm sorry, Burger King.

02:23:42.213 --> 02:23:43.948
Too powdery. Almost chalky.

02:23:43.948 --> 02:23:45.783
And the flavor is not quite there.

02:23:45.783 --> 02:23:47.218
[coughs]

02:23:47.218 --> 02:23:48.052
OK.

02:23:50.054 --> 02:23:51.990
Peri-peri fries has come
back with a vengeance.

02:23:51.990 --> 02:23:54.125
Fair enough. There is
a bit of spice to it.

02:23:54.125 --> 02:23:56.894
Next up, cheesy fries.

02:23:56.894 --> 02:23:58.863
Italian cheesy fries.

02:23:58.863 --> 02:24:00.932
And I don't know what makes these Italian,

02:24:00.932 --> 02:24:03.701
but I think it's a whole lot of oregano.

02:24:03.701 --> 02:24:06.404
And finally, veggie strips.

02:24:06.404 --> 02:24:08.206
Well, at the BK here in the US,

02:24:08.206 --> 02:24:10.174
you can get yourself onion rings.

02:24:10.174 --> 02:24:12.510
Jalapeño cheddar bites.

02:24:12.510 --> 02:24:13.811
See what one of these looks like.

02:24:13.811 --> 02:24:14.912
Mozzarella stick.

02:24:14.912 --> 02:24:16.981
Mott's applesauce.

02:24:16.981 --> 02:24:19.951
Can't have nuggets without sauces!

02:24:19.951 --> 02:24:23.588
You know what that means!

02:24:23.588 --> 02:24:25.156
Sauce talk.

02:24:25.156 --> 02:24:27.859
As for the dips, we have Easy Cheesy.

02:24:27.859 --> 02:24:29.494
Twisted mustard.

02:24:29.494 --> 02:24:31.429
Fiery Hell.

02:24:31.429 --> 02:24:36.000
They literally named one
of their dips Fiery Hell.

02:24:36.000 --> 02:24:37.969
First up, Buffalo sauce.

02:24:37.969 --> 02:24:39.671
Honey mustard. Ranch.

02:24:39.671 --> 02:24:40.905
Sweet and sour.

02:24:40.905 --> 02:24:42.373
Zesty sauce?

02:24:42.373 --> 02:24:43.574
Do we know what this is?

02:24:45.243 --> 02:24:47.311
That is just mayonnaise
and, like, brown mustard.

02:24:47.311 --> 02:24:48.613
Marinara sauce.

02:24:48.613 --> 02:24:50.782
Salsa del Sol.

02:24:50.782 --> 02:24:52.250
It is milkshake time.

02:24:52.250 --> 02:24:54.452
Burger King has three flavors right now.

02:24:54.452 --> 02:24:58.923
They have mango, berry
blast, and chocolate.

02:24:58.923 --> 02:25:00.558
Guys, at the time of filming this,

02:25:00.558 --> 02:25:03.628
it is currently mango
season here in India.

02:25:03.628 --> 02:25:06.197
None of you have tasted a real mango

02:25:06.197 --> 02:25:08.866
until you've tasted the king
of all mangoes, Alphonso,

02:25:08.866 --> 02:25:10.234
available here.

02:25:10.234 --> 02:25:11.302
Everywhere you go right now,

02:25:11.302 --> 02:25:13.571
you're going to get a
delicious mango milkshake.

02:25:13.571 --> 02:25:15.339
We also make something called aamras,

02:25:15.339 --> 02:25:18.876
which is like a delicious mango juice

02:25:18.876 --> 02:25:20.511
that we eat with puris and stuff.

02:25:20.511 --> 02:25:24.615
Let's see if this compares
to fresh mango juice.

02:25:26.150 --> 02:25:28.453
Oh, it's pretty good.

02:25:28.453 --> 02:25:29.854
It's not too sweet.

02:25:29.854 --> 02:25:34.225
It does kind of taste like
mango ice cream sort of mixed.

02:25:34.225 --> 02:25:36.160
But I like it. I really like it.

02:25:36.160 --> 02:25:37.562
Next up, berry blast.

02:25:37.562 --> 02:25:39.263
Paper straws. Burger King, thank you.

02:25:39.263 --> 02:25:41.666
The dolphins appreciate
it just as much as I do.

02:25:44.702 --> 02:25:47.105
Whoa, I did not expect that flavor.

02:25:47.105 --> 02:25:50.274
Here, we have something
called black currant ice cream

02:25:50.274 --> 02:25:53.978
that's rampant in very demented families

02:25:53.978 --> 02:25:56.614
that order the black currant ice cream.

02:25:56.614 --> 02:25:58.983
I'm sorry to single out these
Indian families like this,

02:25:58.983 --> 02:26:00.651
but this tastes like that.

02:26:00.651 --> 02:26:01.886
I'm sensing a pattern here.

02:26:01.886 --> 02:26:03.821
So it won't be a surprise to me

02:26:03.821 --> 02:26:05.590
if the chocolate milkshake

02:26:05.590 --> 02:26:09.627
also just tastes like
watered-down chocolate ice cream.

02:26:09.627 --> 02:26:12.363
The mango one, I suppose
if it wasn't mango season,

02:26:12.363 --> 02:26:14.265
you could go and get a mango milkshake,

02:26:14.265 --> 02:26:16.768
but otherwise, go to any other fruit

02:26:16.768 --> 02:26:18.402
or milkshake store in India,

02:26:18.402 --> 02:26:21.672
get a nice thick mango
shake with actual mangoes.

02:26:21.672 --> 02:26:22.740
Way better.

02:26:22.740 --> 02:26:25.143
On to the cold drinks.
Let's start with the shakes.

02:26:25.143 --> 02:26:26.944
Over here, we have a frozen Coke.

02:26:26.944 --> 02:26:29.013
You can also get a
frozen Fanta wild cherry.

02:26:29.013 --> 02:26:31.616
Sounds amazing. Our Burger
King did not have it.

02:26:31.616 --> 02:26:34.085
First one is this, the Oreo shake.

02:26:34.986 --> 02:26:35.987
Why is that so good?

02:26:35.987 --> 02:26:39.457
It's like a shake made out
of the stuff in the middle.

02:26:39.457 --> 02:26:40.324
Brilliant idea.

02:26:40.324 --> 02:26:42.627
And you can also get chocolate Oreo shake.

02:26:43.528 --> 02:26:45.296
No, it's not. This one's better.
But this one's very good.

02:26:45.296 --> 02:26:46.564
Desserts!

02:26:46.564 --> 02:26:47.732
I'm a sucker for desserts,

02:26:47.732 --> 02:26:50.935
but why would you order
dessert from a fast-food place?

02:26:50.935 --> 02:26:53.337
Unless I'm going to be proven wrong.

02:26:53.337 --> 02:26:57.108
First up, they have chocolate mousse cup.

02:26:57.108 --> 02:26:59.610
OK, it's got a little bit
of cake at the bottom.

02:26:59.610 --> 02:27:01.679
Chocolate, chocolate,
chocolate at the top.

02:27:01.679 --> 02:27:03.014
Chocolate chips on the top.

02:27:04.515 --> 02:27:06.050
Too decadent. Very sweet.

02:27:06.050 --> 02:27:08.386
Next up, they have a choco lava cup,

02:27:08.386 --> 02:27:12.657
keeping in theme with their
random volcano-based food items.

02:27:12.657 --> 02:27:15.026
And I'm sure this would
ooze out chocolate,

02:27:15.026 --> 02:27:16.928
but you have to heat it first.

02:27:20.131 --> 02:27:21.632
That is so sweet!

02:27:21.632 --> 02:27:23.100
When would I eat this?
I'm trying to think of

02:27:23.100 --> 02:27:25.436
when I would eat something this sweet.

02:27:25.436 --> 02:27:26.270
Never.

02:27:26.270 --> 02:27:27.538
We have three dessert exclusives.

02:27:27.538 --> 02:27:30.208
The first one is this,
the Hershey's sundae pie.

02:27:30.208 --> 02:27:31.542
Chocolate chip cookies.

02:27:31.542 --> 02:27:33.344
A soft-serve cup or cone.

02:27:33.344 --> 02:27:34.212
Where is it, Joe?

02:27:34.212 --> 02:27:37.481
Well, it's roughly 100 degrees
here in Southern California,

02:27:37.481 --> 02:27:39.150
and that thing would've melted into a soup

02:27:39.150 --> 02:27:40.785
before we even got it to the studio.

02:27:40.785 --> 02:27:43.921
Imagine either a
soft-serve ice cream cone,

02:27:43.921 --> 02:27:46.524
or a melted soft-serve ice cream cone

02:27:46.524 --> 02:27:47.959
would be more accurate.

02:27:47.959 --> 02:27:51.729
As for cold drinks, we
have Pepsi; Mountain Dew;

02:27:51.729 --> 02:27:54.665
Mirinda, which is an orange soda;

02:27:54.665 --> 02:27:56.400
and iced tea.

02:27:56.400 --> 02:27:59.704
All of these are under the
PepsiCo range of products.

02:27:59.704 --> 02:28:01.572
And, of course, in India,

02:28:01.572 --> 02:28:04.442
the Pepsi slogan is,
"Har Ghoont Mein Swag,"

02:28:04.442 --> 02:28:07.645
which means, "Every
sip has a lot of swag."

02:28:07.645 --> 02:28:09.280
And I have to live with this cringe

02:28:09.280 --> 02:28:10.915
for the rest of my life now.

02:28:10.915 --> 02:28:12.216
Here in the US,

02:28:12.216 --> 02:28:15.286
we have obviously a
variety of exclusive drinks

02:28:15.286 --> 02:28:16.988
you can't get in India.

02:28:16.988 --> 02:28:17.922
Coke.

02:28:17.922 --> 02:28:19.123
Dr. Pepper.

02:28:19.123 --> 02:28:20.224
Diet Coke.

02:28:20.224 --> 02:28:21.425
There it is. Barq's, baby.

02:28:21.425 --> 02:28:22.293
Fanta orange.

02:28:22.293 --> 02:28:24.362
I should say that at
least the BKs that I go to

02:28:24.362 --> 02:28:26.297
here in sunny Southern California

02:28:26.297 --> 02:28:28.232
has those Coke Freestyle machines, so.

02:28:28.232 --> 02:28:30.101
You can also get yourself an orange juice.

02:28:30.101 --> 02:28:32.370
It's really funny looking at orange juice

02:28:32.370 --> 02:28:33.738
next to orange drink.

02:28:33.738 --> 02:28:35.072
Like, look at the difference with it.

02:28:35.072 --> 02:28:36.807
Orange juice. Orange drink.

02:28:36.807 --> 02:28:38.576
Capri Sun apple juice.

02:28:38.576 --> 02:28:39.944
Burger King iced coffee.

02:28:39.944 --> 02:28:42.046
The BK café, which is, of course, coffee.

02:28:42.046 --> 02:28:42.880
Milk.

02:28:43.948 --> 02:28:45.616
Let's talk price.

02:28:45.616 --> 02:28:50.154
A single Indian chicken Whopper
will cost you 199 rupees,

02:28:50.154 --> 02:28:53.991
or 1.56 US dollars at
current conversion rates.

02:28:53.991 --> 02:28:57.361
In the US, a Whopper costs $8.79,

02:28:57.361 --> 02:29:00.698
or 668 Indian rupee.

02:29:00.698 --> 02:29:04.802
That's around a 236% increase in price.

02:29:04.802 --> 02:29:07.638
Make it a meal with medium
fries and a large drink,

02:29:07.638 --> 02:29:12.476
and it'll cost you 383
rupees, or 5.03 US dollars.

02:29:12.476 --> 02:29:14.712
Add a medium fry and a
medium drink to the order,

02:29:14.712 --> 02:29:18.282
and that brings the price to $16.37,

02:29:18.282 --> 02:29:21.552
or 1,246 Indian rupee.

02:29:21.552 --> 02:29:25.122
Again, about a 225% increase.

02:29:25.122 --> 02:29:26.390
Now upgrade to the large size,

02:29:26.390 --> 02:29:30.261
and it's 407 rupees, or 5.35 US dollars.

02:29:30.261 --> 02:29:33.331
Make it a large, $16.77,

02:29:33.331 --> 02:29:36.634
or 1,276 Indian rupee.

02:29:36.634 --> 02:29:39.236
That's a 214% increase.

02:29:39.236 --> 02:29:42.807
200 rupees for a single burger
is actually very expensive.

02:29:42.807 --> 02:29:45.042
And while fast food in the US

02:29:45.042 --> 02:29:47.311
and other foreign countries
might seem like something

02:29:47.311 --> 02:29:49.880
that the average person can easily afford,

02:29:49.880 --> 02:29:51.916
here in India, this is expensive,

02:29:51.916 --> 02:29:53.584
and only the upper-middle
class and the rich

02:29:53.584 --> 02:29:55.653
can actually go out and
have a burger like this.

02:29:55.653 --> 02:29:58.189
In fact, in Mumbai, where
we're filming this right now,

02:29:58.189 --> 02:30:00.391
our most popular street food is vada pav,

02:30:00.391 --> 02:30:02.693
which is like a potato burger,

02:30:02.693 --> 02:30:05.997
and it costs just 15
rupees, which is $0.20.

02:30:05.997 --> 02:30:07.531
It can fill you up.

02:30:07.531 --> 02:30:10.267
Downgrade the cost. Upgrade the taste.

02:30:10.267 --> 02:30:11.769
Get a vada pav.

02:30:11.769 --> 02:30:13.270
To better illustrate the price difference,

02:30:13.270 --> 02:30:15.806
let's compare the US large Whopper combo

02:30:15.806 --> 02:30:18.442
to our combination of two Whoppers,

02:30:18.442 --> 02:30:20.244
two crispy chicken sandwiches,

02:30:20.244 --> 02:30:24.415
five-piece chicken strips,
king fries, and four drinks.

02:30:24.415 --> 02:30:26.684
All of this still costs less,

02:30:26.684 --> 02:30:29.053
at just 1,102 rupees,

02:30:29.053 --> 02:30:32.423
or 14.45 US dollars.

02:30:32.423 --> 02:30:34.125
We would have to add a
crispy veg with cheese

02:30:34.125 --> 02:30:35.326
and a crispy chicken with cheese

02:30:35.326 --> 02:30:37.595
to get around the same price.

02:30:37.595 --> 02:30:40.097
But again, I have to
remind you that in $14,

02:30:40.097 --> 02:30:41.499
an average family here in India

02:30:41.499 --> 02:30:43.567
could eat at home for a week.

02:30:44.935 --> 02:30:46.003
Calories time.

02:30:46.003 --> 02:30:48.672
My favorite part of these
videos because I realize

02:30:48.672 --> 02:30:52.309
how much I should not be eating this food.

02:30:52.309 --> 02:30:54.445
Let's start off with a
crispy chicken sandwich

02:30:54.445 --> 02:30:55.880
from Burger King.

02:30:55.880 --> 02:30:59.083
Ahem. It has 430 calories.

02:30:59.083 --> 02:30:59.917
And in the US,

02:30:59.917 --> 02:31:03.921
our crispy chicken
sandwich is 670 calories.

02:31:03.921 --> 02:31:05.523
Next up is one of Burger King India's

02:31:05.523 --> 02:31:08.492
most popular burgers, the veg Whopper,

02:31:08.492 --> 02:31:11.328
at 728 calories.

02:31:11.328 --> 02:31:14.799
Imagine that. High calories, low taste.

02:31:14.799 --> 02:31:16.267
We don't have that, but in the US,

02:31:16.267 --> 02:31:18.903
our Burger King does have
the Impossible Whopper,

02:31:18.903 --> 02:31:21.572
which contains 630 calories.

02:31:21.572 --> 02:31:23.107
Next, let's compare the fries.

02:31:23.107 --> 02:31:25.643
An average box of king-sized fries

02:31:25.643 --> 02:31:28.712
will cost you 535 calories.

02:31:28.712 --> 02:31:30.748
If I had to choose between these fries

02:31:30.748 --> 02:31:32.483
and an hour of cycling,

02:31:32.483 --> 02:31:34.351
that's very, like,
probably skip the cycling.

02:31:34.351 --> 02:31:37.488
But this is still bad.
It's a lot of calories.

02:31:37.488 --> 02:31:41.392
And in the US, a large
fry has 430 calories.

02:31:41.392 --> 02:31:42.693
And now, for some reason

02:31:42.693 --> 02:31:45.362
if you're really looking
to pack on those calories,

02:31:45.362 --> 02:31:49.433
introducing Burger King India's
most calorific sandwich,

02:31:49.433 --> 02:31:52.970
the masala veg Whopper,

02:31:52.970 --> 02:31:57.975
at a total of 734 calories.

02:31:58.275 --> 02:31:59.210
Damn!

02:31:59.210 --> 02:32:01.345
The website of Burger King India also says

02:32:01.345 --> 02:32:04.014
they sell a 15-piece
grilled chicken wings,

02:32:04.014 --> 02:32:07.284
with a total of 1,256 calories.

02:32:07.284 --> 02:32:09.753
But we called a bunch of
stores, it was unavailable,

02:32:09.753 --> 02:32:11.422
and I think they discontinued it

02:32:11.422 --> 02:32:13.991
because they did not want
to kill half the country.

02:32:13.991 --> 02:32:16.060
Oh, yo!

02:32:16.060 --> 02:32:17.194
Yeah.

02:32:17.194 --> 02:32:20.064
This is definitely a block of calories.

02:32:20.064 --> 02:32:20.998
And in the US BK,

02:32:20.998 --> 02:32:24.902
our most calorific sandwich
is this, the Bacon King.

02:32:24.902 --> 02:32:29.907
Just one of these bad
boys, 1,359 calories.

02:32:29.907 --> 02:32:31.442
Oof!

02:32:31.442 --> 02:32:32.443
God dammit.

02:32:32.443 --> 02:32:35.079
Brown on brown on brown.
Brown on brown on brown!

02:32:35.079 --> 02:32:38.048
Brown, brown, brown, brown, brown.

02:32:38.048 --> 02:32:39.750
Hey, you got to hand it to
these fast-food companies, man.

02:32:39.750 --> 02:32:41.218
They make this s--- look real appetizing

02:32:41.218 --> 02:32:42.386
for what is literally

02:32:42.386 --> 02:32:44.088
how many different shades of brown?

